{"case_id": "q012-2", "row_id": "q012", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Lenvatinib + Nofazinlimab pivotal, registrational, or Phase 3 trial in Unresectable or Metastatic Hepatocellular Carcinoma: planned or initiated status and expected start date", "query": "Lenvatinib + Nofazinlimab NCT04194775 current trial status", "anchors": ["Lenvatinib + Nofazinlimab NCT04194775", "Lenvatinib", "Nofazinlimab", "NCT04194775"], "search_latency_ms": 5311.3, "target": "Lenvatinib + Nofazinlimab NCT04194775 / Lenvatinib / Nofazinlimab / NCT04194775", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 340.1, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9989, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.00042, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.9834, "results": [{"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "NCT04194775: An ongoing trial by CStone Pharmaceuticals", "url": "https://fdaaa.trialstracker.net/trial/NCT04194775/", "domain": "fdaaa.trialstracker.net", "snippet": "## NCT04194775: An ongoing trial by CStone Pharmaceuticals\nThis trial is ongoing.\nIt must report results 1 year from now.\n...\n|Title|A Multi-Center, Double-Blind, Randomized, Phase III Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Combination With Lenvatinib Compared to Placebo in Combination With Lenvatinib as First-Line Therapy in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)|\n|Results Status|Ongoing|\n|ACT or pACT?|This is what FDAAA officially calls an \"Applicable Clinical Trial\"|\n|Start date|Dec. 13, 2019|\n|Completion date|June 30, 2025|\n|Required reporting date|June 30, 2026, midnight|\n|Actual reporting date|None|\n|Date last checked at ClinicalTrials.gov|June 13, 2025|", "date": "2025-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-06-13", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.99, "evidence": 0.9933}, "jev_score": 0.9834, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With ...", "url": "https://www.guidelinecentral.com/clinical-trial/?id=NCT04194775&v=tabular", "domain": "guidelinecentral.com", "snippet": "# A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma\n- Recruitment Status\n- ACTIVE, NOT RECRUITING(See Contacts and Locations)Verified July 2025 by CStone Pharmaceuticals\n...\n- NCT04194775\n...\n- Last Update Posted\n- July 31, 2025\n- Last Verified\n- July 2025\nClinicalTrials.gov processed this data on July 2025.\nLink to the current ClinicalTrials.gov record .\n...\n|Study Start Date|December 13, 2019|\n|Actual Primary Completion Date|June 18, 2025|\n...\n|Official Title|A Multi-Center, Double-Blind, Randomized, Phase III Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Combination With Lenvatinib Compared to Placebo in Combination With Lenvatinib as First-Line Therapy in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)|\n|Brief Summary|This is a multi-center, double-blind, randomized, phase III study to investigate the efficacy and safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in combination with lenvatinib and placebo in combination with lenvatinib in the treatment of subjects with no prior systemic treatment and with unresectable advanced hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC).\nIn this study, Nofazinlimab (CS1003) (or placebo) and lenvatinib are both considered as the study treatment while Nofazinlimab (CS1003) (or placebo) is the investigational product of and lenvatinib is selected as the basic treatment for HCC.|\n...\n|Recruitment Status|Active, not recruiting|\n|--|--|\n|Anticipated Enrollment|534|\n|Anticipated Study Completion Date|1w 1d from now|\n|Anticipated Primary Study Completion Date|June 18, 2025|", "date": "2019-12-13", "last_updated": "2025-10-22", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.99}, "jev_score": 0.9702, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in... | Clinical Trial", "url": "https://trial.medpath.com/clinical-trial/f021ad7c4cfbc551/nct04194775-nofazinlimab-lenvatinib-advanced-hepatocellular-carcinoma", "domain": "trial.medpath.com", "snippet": "NCT04194775Active, not recruitingPhase 3\n# A Multi-Center, Double-Blind, Randomized, Phase III Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Combination With Lenvatinib Compared to Placebo in Combination With Lenvatinib as First-Line Therapy in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)\nCStone Pharmaceuticals125 sites in 6 countries534 enrolledStarted: December 13, 2019Last updated: July 30, 2026\n...\n- **Phase**\nPhase 3\n- **Status**\nActive, not recruiting\n...\n534\n...\n- **Primary Endpoint**\n...\nThis is a multi-center, double-blind, randomized, phase III study to investigate the efficacy and safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in combination with lenvatinib and placebo in combination with lenvatinib in the treatment of subjects with no prior systemic treatment and with unresectable advanced hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC).\n...\nOverall Survival (OS)\nTime Frame: From enrollment to end of follow-up, a median of 42.5 months\n...\nResults posted to ClinicalTrials.gov on 2026-07-30.\n...\n534 started · 0 completed\n...\nJune 18, 2025 (last year)\n- **Study Completion**\nSeptember 30, 2026 (2 days ago)\n- **Last Verified**", "date": "2026-07-30", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.97}, "jev_score": 0.9506, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Emerging Therapies for Hepatocellular Carcinoma - PMC", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12100529/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Several phase 3 trials encompass combination therapy and monotherapy for advanced HCC.\nThese options include several PD-1 inhibitors, including tislelizumab, camrelizumab, budigalimab, toripalimab, finotonlimab, nofazinlimab, penpulimab, and sintilimab.\n...\n|**Nofazinlimab (CS1003)**| |Anti-PD-1 antibody| | |\n|+ Lenvatinib|NCT04194775|VEGFR-1, VEGFR-2, and VEGFR-3 inhibitor|Multinational|Phase 3 Active, not recruiting|\n...\nIn a double-blind, multicenter phase 3 study, toripalimab plus lenvatinib (NCT04523493) is being compared with lenvatinib monotherapy and placebo.\nA similar study combining nofazinlimab and lenvatinib is underway (NCT04194775).", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-05", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.84}, "jev_score": 0.8232, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Nofazinlimab - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/bf31aad0266d41688ed754613150c716", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|NCT04194775 (CS1003-305, ESMO2025)|Phase 3|Hepatocellular Carcinoma First line|534|Nofazinlimab + Lenvatinib|crgoxwqgbt(rzfiobiepn) = wfpwygxeca czvdkshulz (pvclpucluq ) View more|Positive|17 Oct 2025|\n|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|\n|NCT04194775 (CS1003-305, ESMO2025)|Phase 3|Hepatocellular Carcinoma First line|534|Placebo + Lenvatinib|crgoxwqgbt(rzfiobiepn) = cupywigtzp czvdkshulz (pvclpucluq ) View more|Positive|17 Oct 2025|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-15", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.8433}, "jev_score": 0.8096, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "The current landscape of therapies for hepatocellular carcinoma", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10588973/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Selected ongoing prospective phase III randomized controlled trials of systemic therapies in advanced HCC in the United States\n...\n|CheckMate 459: A Study of Nivolumab vs Sorafenib as First-Line Treatment in Pts with Advanced HCC (NCT02576509)|743|Nivolumab vs Sorafenib (1L)|OS|16.4 vs 14.7 mo (HR 0.85, 95% CI 0.72–1.02, *P* = 0.075)|(77)|\n...\n|A Study of Nofazinlimab in Combination with Lenvatinib vs Lenvatinib Alone as First-Line Therapy in Pts with Advanced HCC (NCT04194775)|534|Nofazinlimab + Lenvatinib vs Lenvatinib (1L)|OS, PFS-BICR|Not yet completed| |", "date": "2023-07-10", "last_updated": "2026-05-05", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.8033}, "jev_score": 0.7631, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT04194775", "domain": "clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "Drug: Nofazinlimab (CS1003)+Lenvatinib Drug: Nofazinlimab (CS1003) Placebo+Lenvatinib\n- CS1003-305\n...\nInclusion criteria\n- Age ≥18 years on the day of signing informed consent-(For Taiwan, the lower limit of age is 20 years).\n- Subjects with unresectable advanced HCC, that is not eligible for surgery and/or locoregional therapy (Stage B or C based on Barcelona Clinic Liver Cancer [BCLC] staging system, and meets either one of the following criteria: 1) histologically or cytologically confirmed diagnosis of HCC, 2) clinically confirmed diagnosis of HCC according to American Association for the Study of Liver Diseases (AASLD) criteria.\nPatients without cirrhosis require histological confirmation of diagnosis.\n- With at least one measurable lesion can be assessed\n- Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group performance status (ECOG PS) 0 or 1.\n- Life expectancy ≥ 3 months.\n- Child-Pugh A\n- No prior systemic treatment for advanced HCC\n- Subjects with hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection, are willing to continue receiving antiviral treatment while on study.\nSubjects have adequate organ and marrow function.\nFemale subjects with childbearing potential must have negative serum pregnancy test result at screening.\n...\nExclusion criteria\n- Fibrolamellar-HCC, sarcomatoid, cholangiocellular carcinoma or mixed cholangiocarcinoma and HCC.\n- A prior bleeding event due to esophageal within 6 months or other gastrointestinal bleeding events within 28 days prior to screening.\n- Malabsorption syndrome or inability to take oral medication due to other causes.\n- HBV and HCV co-infection.\n...\n- Surgery or locoregional therapy for palliative purpose within 4 weeks prior to study treatment.\n...\n- Known history of human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection or acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS).\n...\n- History of bone marrow transplantation or organ transplantation.\n- History of anaphylaxis or hypersensitivity to any ingredient of the investigational product.\n- Any contraindication of lenvatinib.\n...\n- Pregnant or lactating female subjects.\n...\n|Overall survival (OS)|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n...\n|Objective response rate (ORR) assessed by blinded independent central review committee(BICR)|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Progression-free survival(PFS) assessed by blinded independent central review committee(BICR) based on Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors(RECIST) v1.1|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n...\n|Percentage of Participants with Adverse Events|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Peak and trough serum concentrations of CS1003|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Number and percentage of subjects who develop anti-CS1003 antibody (ADA)|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Time to deterioration (TTD), defined as the time from randomization to the first deterioration of European Organization for the Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) Quality-of-Life Questionnaire Core 30 (QLQ-C30) scale|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|", "date": "2019-12-10", "last_updated": "2025-08-12", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_tar