{"case_id": "q013-1", "row_id": "q013", "mode": "queries", "objective": "SD-133 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma animal models", "query": "SD-133 pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma monotherapy xenograft TGI", "anchors": ["SD-133"], "search_latency_ms": 6863.1, "target": "SD-133", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 367.5, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 16472, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000692, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 0, "abstain": true, "top_score": 0.071, "results": [{"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Pancreatic Cancer Treatment (PDQ®)", "url": "https://www.cancer.gov/types/pancreatic/hp/pancreatic-treatment-pdq", "domain": "cancer.gov", "snippet": "- Based on these findings, the adjuvant combination of gemcitabine and capecitabine is the standard of care after a resection for pancreatic cancer.\n...\n- The pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of S-1 may be different between Eastern and Western patient populations because grade 3/4 gastrointestinal toxicities, especially diarrhea, have been reported more commonly in the Western patient population.\nS-1 is not currently approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for use in the United States.\n...\n- None of these phase III trials have demonstrated a statistically significant advantage favoring the use of combination chemotherapy in the first-line treatment of metastatic pancreatic cancer.", "date": "2026-09-22", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.3, "evidence": 0.2367}, "jev_score": 0.071, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma: Treatment hurdles ...", "url": "https://www.wjgnet.com/1948-5204/full/v12/i2/173.htm", "domain": "wjgnet.com", "snippet": "In addition to mesothelin, other cancer-associated antigens are being tested in ongoing clinical trials as potential targets of CAR-T-based therapeutic regimes (anti-CEA, anti-CD-133, anti-ROR1, anti-WT1) alone or in combination with chemotherapy[60]; and (5) Immune modulating agents targeting the dense pancreatic microenvironment could also exert substantial antitumor activity.", "date": "2020-02-15", "last_updated": "2026-09-29", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.2, "evidence": 0.3533}, "jev_score": 0.0707, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma: Treatment hurdles, tumor ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7031151/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "In addition to mesothelin, other cancer-associated antigens are being tested in ongoing clinical trials as potential targets of CAR-T-based therapeutic regimes (anti-CEA, anti-CD-133, anti-ROR1, anti-WT1) alone or in combination with chemotherapy[60]; and (5) Immune modulating agents targeting the dense pancreatic microenvironment could also exert substantial antitumor activity.", "date": "2020-02-15", "last_updated": "2026-09-27", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.16, "evidence": 0.36}, "jev_score": 0.0576, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Radioimmunotherapy of Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma: A Review of the Current Status of Literature", "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2072-6694/12/2/481", "domain": "mdpi.com", "snippet": "Clinical studies were limited to investigating β radioimmunotherapy only.\nPhase I and II trials observed disease control rates of 11.2%–57.9%, with synergistic effects noted for combination therapies.", "date": "2020-02-19", "last_updated": "2026-08-13", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.09, "evidence": 0.32}, "jev_score": 0.0288, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Immune therapies in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma: Where are we now?", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5974576/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Therefore, the subset of PDAC patients eligible for CPI monotherapy is small.\n...\nOverall, except for MSI-H tumors, PDAC are considered to be resistant to single-agent immune therapy.", "date": "2018-05-28", "last_updated": "2026-03-15", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.08, "evidence": 0.32}, "jev_score": 0.0256, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Full article: Next-generation therapies for pancreatic cancer", "url": "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17474124.2024.2322648", "domain": "tandfonline.com", "snippet": "For patients with an ECOG PS of 2, GnP is considered in selected patients, and gemcitabine monotherapy is a preferred option for patients with a less favorable performance status [Citation15,Citation16].\n...\nThere continues to be significant interest in adoptive cellular therapy with chimeric antigen receptor T cells (CAT-T) and T cell receptor therapy (TCR-T) in PDAC.\nBoth approaches aim to generate cellular and humoral immunity against selected tumor-associated proteins such as *KRAS* mutant alleles (G12D, G12V), CD133, CD137, EGFR, or mesothelin [Citation148].\nA phase I trial of anti-CD133, a cancer stem cell marker highly expressed in PDAC, CAR-T included seven patients with mPDAC and showed that three individuals achieved SD, 2 PR, and 2 patients with POD [Citation149].", "date": "2024-03-03", "last_updated": "2026-09-23", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.1, "evidence": 0.2367}, "jev_score": 0.0237, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "E> ��?�\"�T����Ԩ$h��N$lyf~����������50#���W||w��衴�*�a��ǔ N�<������D�W�oP��-�9촦�Mr{��b4�����q�*����#��lQ��O-O�v8Gx�a�ԗ����]��-����dkZ[��ڹ��z�r�V�>'2Aޖ'�2A{-����vr�Li�i�ND8�xL���� {#��0���9֤��ryW~t��/g��K�f�