{"case_id": "q015-3", "row_id": "q015", "mode": "queries", "objective": "GFH375/VS-7375 in vivo monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression tumour shrinkage in KRAS G12D-Mutated/MTAP-Deleted Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma animal models", "query": "GFH375 VS-7375 MTAP-deleted pancreatic xenograft single-agent TGI", "anchors": ["GFH375 VS-7375", "GFH375", "VS-7375"], "search_latency_ms": 28327.8, "target": "GFH375 VS-7375 / GFH375 / VS-7375", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 334.3, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 11595, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000487, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.833, "results": [{"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Verastem Oncology Announces Late Breaking and Regular ...", "url": "https://investor.verastem.com/node/15761/pdf", "domain": "investor.verastem.com", "snippet": "In preclinical pancreatic, lung, and colorectal cancer models, VS-7375 (dual ON/OFF inhibitor) showed deeper and more sustained tumor regression compared to ON-only G12D or pan-RAS inhibitors\n...\nTitle: Strong durable tumor regressions with the KRAS G12D ON/OFF inhibitor VS-7375 in combination with PRMT5 inhibition in MTAP-deleted/KRAS\nG12D-mutant pancreatic cancer\n...\nTitle: VS-7375: An oral, selective KRAS G12D dual ON/OFF inhibitor with potent anti-tumor activity as a single agent and in combination with other\nagents\n...\nIn the KP4 KRAS G12D pancreatic cancer model, VS-7375 (50 mg/kg twice daily), zoldonrasib (100 mg/kg once daily) and daraxonrasib (25 mg/kg once daily), produced similar initial tumor regression through day nine.\nBy approximately day 20, however, zoldonrasib and daraxonrasib lost anti-tumor activity with tumor outgrowth, (mean tumor volume >850 mm by day 30) whereas VS-7375 maintained sustained tumor regression (mean tumor volume ~80 mm by day 30), consistent with pharmacodynamic analyses showing durable pathway inhibition only with VS-7375.\n...\nVerastem selected VS-7375 (also known as GFH375), an oral KRAS G12D\n(ON/OFF) inhibitor, as its lead program in December 2023 and the license for VS-7375 that was exercised in January 2025 is the first one from this", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-06", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.85}, "jev_score": 0.833, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "VS-7375 (GFH375): An oral, selective KRAS G12D (ON/ ...", "url": "https://www.verastem.com/pdf/AACR-VS7375-Poster-Presentation.pdf", "domain": "verastem.com", "snippet": "VS-7375 (GFH375) is an oral KRAS G12D-selective small molecule inhibitor (G12Di) that binds\nKRAS G12D in both the active (ON; GTP-bound) and inactive (OFF; GDP-bound) states (Figure \n1) (2).\n...\nFurthermore, we have shown that oral administration of VS-7375 inhibits tumor \ngrowth in a dose-dependent manner in KRAS G12D-mutant human cancer models in vivo including pancreatic and colorectal cancers (Figure 2) (2).\nVS-7375 monotherapy is currently in phase 2 clinical evaluation (NCT06500676).\n...\n• VS-7375 induces strong tumor regressions (>30% reduction) in contrast to G12D ON (RMC-9805) and\npan-RAS ON (RMC-6236) inhibitors in a KRAS G12D-mutant xenograft model\n• VS-7375 monotherapy induces tumor regressions in multiple KRAS G12D-mutant cancer models and \nshows strong combinatorial anti-tumor efficacy with cetuximab\n...\nVS-7375 is superior to chemotherapy\nin KRAS G12D-mutant colorectal and pancreatic cancer models", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-14", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7233}, "jev_score": 0.7088, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "展现产品强效抑瘤活性、持久通路抑制及多种联用方案开发潜力", "url": "https://www.moomoo.com/hans/news/post/70379510", "domain": "moomoo.com", "snippet": "GFH375为口服KRAS G12D（ON/OFF）抑制剂，临床前研究显示其相较于海外同靶点及泛RAS抑制剂，展现出更优的抗肿瘤活性、更高的靶点选择性\n与更持久的信号通路抑制作用；本次公布的研究还系统探索了RAS抑制剂的潜在耐药机制及可逆性，显示了GFH375超越KRAS G12D（ON）抑制剂的抗耐药潜力，并为多种联用方案提供了坚实的科学依据。\nGFH375于2025年在中国进入全球首个口服KRAS G12D抑制剂III期注册临床研究；2026年GFH375率先获得国内两项KRAS G12D抑制剂单药治疗的突破性疗法认定，分别\n用于治疗G12D突变型胰腺癌与非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）；此外，该产品已获美国FDA快速通道资格认定，针对G12D突变型转移性胰腺导管腺癌（PDAC）各线治疗。目前，GFH375/VS-7375多项单药和联合疗法试验正在国内外进行。\n...\nLBA 183 |Strong durable tumor regressions with the KRAS G12D (ON/OFF) inhibitor VS-7375 in combination with PRMT5 inhibition in MTAP-deleted/KRAS G12D-mutant pancreatic cancer\nPoster 7100 |VS-7375: An oral, selective KRAS G12D dual ON/OFF inhibitor with potent anti-tumor activity as a single agent and in combination with other agents\n...\n在PDAC、NSCLC及CRC动物模型中，GFH375联合用药的抗肿瘤活性显著优于单药治疗，潜在可联用方案包括GFH375联合西妥昔单抗、联合FAK抑制剂±RAF/MEK抑制剂avutometinib，或联合PRMT5抑制剂（在KRAS G12D突变伴MTAP缺失的PDAC中获益尤为显著）。\n既往公开研究证实，MTA协同型PRMT5抑制剂可选择性作用于MTAP缺失、KRAS突变型胰腺癌；本次壁报公布的细胞实验进一步验证，RAS抑制剂与PRMT5抑制剂之间无交叉耐药，为约25%携带MTAP缺失的KRAS突变PDAC患者，提供了序贯治疗或联合治疗的科学依据。\n...\n关于GFH375/VS-7375GFH375为口服高活性、高选择性小分子KRAS G12D（ON/OFF）抑制剂，通过非共价形式结合KRAS G12D蛋白，抑制其与下游效应蛋白结合，从而在细胞中破坏KRAS G12D对下游通路的持续活化，最终高效抑制肿瘤细胞增殖。\n临床前研究已显示GFH375单药对肿瘤生长的抑制效应随用药剂量和周期增长而提升，且在激酶选择性和安全性靶点测试中显示低脱靶风险。", "date": "2026-05-21", "last_updated": "2026-06-09", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.72}, "jev_score": 0.7056, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "展現產品強效抑瘤活性、持久通路抑制及多種聯用方案開發潛力", "url": "https://www.moomoo.com/hant/news/post/70379510", "domain": "moomoo.com", "snippet": "GFH375爲口服KRAS G12D（ON/OFF）抑制劑，臨床前研究顯示其相較於海外同靶點及泛RAS抑制劑，展現出更優的抗腫瘤活性、更高\n...\n治療的突破性療法認定，分別用於治療G12D突變型胰腺癌與非小細胞肺癌（NSCLC）；此外，該產品已獲美國FDA快速通道資格認定，針對G12D突變型轉移性胰腺導管腺癌（PDAC）各線治療。目前，GFH375/VS-7375多項單藥和聯合療法試驗正在國內外進行。\n...\nLBA 183 |Strong durable tumor regressions with the KRAS G12D (ON/OFF) inhibitor VS-7375 in combination with PRMT5 inhibition in MTAP-deleted/KRAS G12D-mutant pancreatic cancer\nPoster 7100 |VS-7375: An oral, selective KRAS G12D dual ON/OFF inhibitor with potent anti-tumor activity as a single agent and in combination with other agents\n...\n在PDAC、NSCLC及CRC動物模型中，GFH375聯合用藥的抗腫瘤活性顯著優於單藥治療，潛在可聯用方案包括GFH375聯合西妥昔單抗、聯合FAK抑制劑±RAF/MEK抑制劑avutometinib，或聯合PRMT5抑制劑（在KRAS G12D突變伴MTAP缺失的PDAC中獲益尤爲顯著）。\n既往公開研究證實，MTA協同型PRMT5抑制劑可選擇性作用於MTAP缺失、KRAS突變型胰腺癌；本次壁報公佈的細胞實驗進一步驗證，RAS抑制劑與PRMT5抑制劑之間無交叉耐藥，爲約25%攜帶MTAP缺失的KRAS突變PDAC患者，提供了序貫治療或聯合治療的科學依據。\n...\n臨床前研究已顯示GFH375單藥對腫瘤生長的抑制效應隨用藥劑量和週期增長而提升，且在激酶選擇性和安全性靶點測試中顯示低脫靶風險。", "date": "2026-05-21", "last_updated": "2026-05-26", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7167}, "jev_score": 0.6952, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "GenFleet Therapeutics Announces Data of VS-7375 ...", "url": "https://www.genfleet.com/en/press_release-110", "domain": "genfleet.com", "snippet": "The studies highlighted the potent and differentiated profile of GFH375, an oral KRAS G12D (ON/OFF) inhibitor, demonstrating superior anti-tumor activity, enhanced potency and selectivity, and more durable pathway suppression compared with other KRAS/RAS inhibitors across animal models and cellular assays.\n...\nGFH375 entered the world’s first phase III registrational trial as an oral KRAS G12D inhibitor in China in 2025 and was granted with China’s first Breakthrough Therapy Designations for a KRAS G12D inhibitor monotherapy treating G12D-mutant pancreatic cancer and non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) respectively in 2026; VS-7375 also received U.S.\nFDA’s Fast Track Designation for treatment across all lines of G12D-mutant metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC).\nMultiple monotherapy and combination trials of GFH375/VS-7375 are ongoing in China (by GenFleet) and outside of China (by Verastem).\n...\n*LBA 183 | Strong durable tumor regressions with the KRAS G12D (ON/OFF) inhibitor VS-7375 in combination with PRMT5 inhibition in MTAP-deleted/KRAS G12D-mutant pancreatic cancer*\n*Poster 7100 | VS-7375: An oral, selective KRAS G12D dual ON/OFF inhibitor with potent anti-tumor activity as a single agent and in combination with other agents*\n...\nIn PDAC, NSCLC and CRC models, combination regimens demonstrated enhanced anti-tumor activity versus single-agent therapy.\nThe combo regimens include GFH375 with cetuximab, or with FAK inhibitor ± the RAF/MEK clamp avutometinib, or with PRMT5 inhibitors (particular benefit observed in KRAS G12D–mutant, MTAP-deleted PDAC).\nPrior published research demonstrated that MTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitors selectively address MTAP-deleted, KRAS-mutant pancreatic cancers.\nData from Verastem’s preclinical research further validated the absence of cross-resistance between RAS and PRMT5 inhibitors, supporting sequential or combination approaches for the 25% of KRAS-mutant PDAC patients with concurrent MTAP deletion; PRMT5 and KRAS govern independent signaling pathways and distinct transcriptional programs yet converge on core PDAC survival pathways, including cell-cycle progression and MYC-driven oncogenesis.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-09-27", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.6833}, "jev_score": 0.6696, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] VS-7375: An oral, selective KRAS G12D dual ON/OFF inhibitor with ...", "url": "http://www.verastem.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/AACR-2025-VS-7375-poster-E-poster-4.8.26-printed.pdf", "domain": "verastem.com", "snippet": "VS-7375 (GFH375) is an oral KRAS G12D-selective small molecule inhibitor that binds KRAS G12D in both the ON and OFF states.\n...\nVS-7375 monotherapy and in combination with other agents is currently in clinical evaluation in the US\n(NCT07020221) and in China (NCT06500676; NCT07262567; NCT07259590).\n...\n• VS-7375 is a potent KRAS G12D ON/OFF inhibitor with long residence time (18-24 hours) leading to more\npotent and durable suppression of pERK than the KRAS G12D ON-only inhibitor zoldonrasib (RMC-9805)\n...\n• In a KRAS G12D-mutated pancreatic cancer model, mechanisms of resistance observed with the tricomplex \ninhibitors zoldonrasib (RMC-9805) and daraxonrasib (RMC-6236) do not limit the durability of VS-7375 efficacy\n...\n• These results support the ongoing clinical evaluation of VS-7375 as monotherapy and in combinations for \ntreatment of patients with KRAS G12D-mutated cancers (VS-7375-101; NCT06500676)\n...\nCombination of a PRMT5 inhibitor with VS-7375 induces durable tumor regressions            \nin a KRAS G12D-mutated;MTAP-deleted pancreatic cancer model\n...\nFigure 8.\nMice bearing KP4 KRAS G12D-mutated/MTAP-deleted pancreatic tumors were treated with VS-7375 (50 mg/kg orally, twice daily), a PRMT5 inhibitor (BMS-986504 & AMG193: 100 mg/kg orally, once daily; TNG462: 30 mg/kg orally, twice daily) or the combination.\nN = 8 mice/group.\n...\nVS-7375 suppresses pERK, pAKT, pS6 and MYC levels more potently, rapidly, and \ndurably than the KRAS G12D ON-only inhibitor zoldonrasib (RMC-9805)", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-08", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.6767}, "jev_score": 0.6632, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Resources | Verastem, Inc.", "url": "https://www.verastem.com/our-science/resources/", "domain": "verastem.com", "snippet": "### VS-7375: An oral, selective KRAS G12D dual ON/OFF inhibitor with potent anti-tumor activity as a single agent and in combination with other agents\n...\n### VS-7375, a non-covalent dual ON/OFF KRASG12D inhibitor, displays superior activity to ON-only KRASG12D inhibitors in preclinical models of pancreatic cancer\n...\n### Strong durable tumor regressions with the KRASG12D ON/OFF inhibitor VS-7375 in combination with PRMT5inhibition in MTAP-deleted/KRASG12D-mutant pancreatic cancer", "date": "2026-05-05", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.93, "evidence": 0.6733}, "jev_score": 0.6262, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "GenFleet Therapeutics (Shanghai) Inc. 勁方醫藥科技(上海) ...", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0409/2026040900157.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "The board of directors of the Company (the “Board”) is pleased to announce oral \nKRAS G12D (ON/OFF) inhibitor GFH375 has been granted with the Breakthrough \nTherapy Designation (BTD) by the Center for Drug Evaluation of China’s National \nMedical Products Administration.\nThe designation is intended for GFH375 monotherapy treating patients with KRAS G12D-mutant metastatic pancreatic cancer who have received at least one prior systemic therapy, representing China’s first BTD inclusion of KRAS G12D inhibitor monotherapy for pancreatic cancer.\n...\nGenFleet’s partner Verastem Oncology started overseas development of GFH375 (known as VS-7375 outside of China) in 2025, and\nVS-7375 was granted with US FDA’s Fast Track Designation for the treatment of \nKRAS G12D-mutant pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma across all lines of therapy.\nGFH375 entered the world’s first phase III registrational study of a KRAS G12D inhibitor monotherapy (GFH375X1301) in 2025.\n...\nMultiple monotherapy and combination trials of GFH375/VS-\n7375 are currently underway in all lines of setting in China (by GenFleet) and outside \nof China (by Verastem).\n...\nGFH375 is an orally active, potent, highly selective small-molecule KRAS G12D\n(ON/OFF) inhibitor designed to target the GTP/GDP exchange, thereby disrupting the \nactivation of downstream pathways and effectively inhibiting tumor cell proliferation.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-12", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.6}, "jev_score": 0.582, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "GFH-375 (GFH-375) - 药物靶点：KRAS G12D_在研适应症：转移性胰腺癌...", "url": "https://synapse.zhihuiya.com/drug/3d8460adad2148dba2f808bc7077105f", "domain": "synapse.zhihuiya.com", "snippet": "|在研适应症 局部晚期非小细胞肺癌KRAS G12D突变胰腺癌胰腺腺癌+ [7]|\n|非在研适应症 转移性胰腺癌|\n...\n|KRAS G12D突变胰腺癌|临床3期|中国|劲方医药科技（上海）股份有限公司|2025-11-25|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-10", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.88, "evidence": 0.5633}, "jev_score": 0.4957, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "GFH375/VS-7375 Program Update", "url": "https://www.genfleet.com/Public/Uploads/uploadfile/files/20251207/Oct.pdf", "domain": "genfleet.com", "snippet": "• ORR was 40.7% (24/59), 90%CI was [30%, 52%].\n• DCR was 96.7% (57/59), 90%CI was [90%, 99%].\nMajority (91.5%) had reduction in target lesions.\n...\nAbstract number: LBA84\n• Median PFS was 5.52 months (90%CI: 4.27, 7.20), with a median follow-up time 5.65 months (90%CI: 4.96, 6.08).\n• 4-month PFS rate was 78.2% (90%CI: 69.8%, 87.5%).\n...\n• The safety profile of GFH375 in  KRAS G12D mutant PDAC patients is consistent with previous report.1,2\n– Common TRAEs were gastrointestinal and hematological AEs; most were grade 1 or 2 and manageable with supportive treatment.\n– Most frequent TRAEs (≥20%) were diarrhea (56.1%), neutrophil count decreased (48.5%), vomiting (47.0%), nausea (47.0%),\n...\nThe overall safety/tolerability of GFH375 is better than that of daraxonrasib.\n...\nVS-7375-101 Study Schema, Efficiently Testing KRAS G12D+ Indications with Monotherapy and SOC Combinations\nPart A: Single Agent Dose Escalation – Any KRAS G12D Solid Tumor\n...\n• Efficacious starting dose:\n• 400 mg starting dose supported by monotherapy \nefficacy/safety in FIH study\n...\nFDA Engagement Plans\n• Granted Fast Track Designation for: \n• First-line in patients with KRAS G12D locally \nadvanced or metastatic PDAC and\n• Patients with KRAS G12D locally advanced or \nmPDAC who received at least one prior line of standard systemic therapy in July 2025\n• Plan to pursue Breakthrough Therapy \n...\n• First two monotherapy dose levels (400 mg QD and 600 mg QD) cleared, \nwith no dose-limiting toxicities (DLT’s) reported\n• Promising anti-tumor activity observed in patients with various solid \ntumors, including advanced pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma\n• No nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea greater than Grade 1 was observed \n• Enrollment initiated for VS-7375 in combination with cetuximab in \npatients with advanced KRAS G12D mutant solid tumors, including colorectal \ncancer", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-21", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.4833}, "jev_score": 0.464, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}], "total_ms": 28662.1, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:18+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q018-5", "row_id": "q018", "mode": "queries", "objective": "SPR2015 in vivo animal models and results: cell-line xenograft CDX, patient-derived xenograft PDX, syngeneic, orthotopic, or genetically engineered models", "query": "SPR2015 HPAC AsPC-1 tumour volume percentage inhibition", "anchors": ["SPR2015"], "search_latency_ms": 2282.0, "target": "SPR2015", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 371.3, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7318, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000307, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 1, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.5206, "results": [{"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "SPR-2015 (SPR-2015) - 药物靶点：KRAS G12D_在研适应症：结直肠癌，...", "url": "https://synapse.zhihuiya.com/drug/4e2007c62c7e4512bf4b82afcaaf6937", "domain": "synapse.zhihuiya.com", "snippet": "SPR2015是一款针对RAS通路的分子胶（Molecular Glue）药物。该产品旨在解决KRAS等靶点在多种实体瘤中的耐药及难成药问题，主要适应症涵盖胰腺癌、非小细胞肺癌及结直肠癌等。\n目前，SPR2015处于临床前候选药物（PCC）阶段。", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-29", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.5367}, "jev_score": 0.5206, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Safety, pharmacokinetics, and antitumor activity of the anti ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0923753422000035", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-26", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.6, "evidence": 0.0433}, "jev_score": 0.026, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Evaluation of the safety, pharmacokinetics, and antitumor activity of ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S266636432500061X", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-06", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.49, "evidence": 0.03}, "jev_score": 0.0147, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Proprietary Information of MD Anderson", "url": "https://cdn.clinicaltrials.gov/large-docs/27/NCT02684227/Prot_SAP_000.pdf", "domain": "cdn.clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "Proprietary Information of MD Anderson\n...\nProprietary Information of MD Anderson", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-13", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.46, "evidence": 0.02}, "jev_score": 0.0092, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "register", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/my-account/register?siteId=5148&returnUrl=https://academic.oup.com/carcin/article-abstract/25/11/2135/2475855?redirectedFrom=fulltext", "domain": "academic.oup.com", "snippet": "For full access to this pdf, sign in to an existing account, or purchase an annual subscription.", "date": "2025-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-11-24", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.17, "evidence": 0.0033}, "jev_score": 0.0006, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "PubChem BioAssay", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pcassay?LinkName=gene_pcassay_rnai&from_uid=284274", "domain": "ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "The NCBI web site requires JavaScript to function.\n...\nThe https:// ensures that you are connecting to the", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-07-05", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.11, "evidence": 0.0033}, "jev_score": 0.0004, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "PDC000198 - Proteomic Data Commons - National Cancer Institute", "url": "https://proteomic.datacommons.cancer.gov/pdc/study/PDC000198", "domain": "proteomic.datacommons.cancer.gov",