{"case_id": "q020-2", "row_id": "q020", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease competing agents in the same mechanistic class as JTO2, including Monoclonal Antibody and CXCL10 therapies", "query": "JTO2 anti-CXCL10 monoclonal antibody IBD pipeline", "anchors": ["JTO2"], "search_latency_ms": 3416.8, "target": "drugs competing with JTO2: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 363.3, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8032, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000337, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 4, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.644, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Advancing therapeutic frontiers: a pipeline of novel drugs ...", "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/gastroenterology/articles/10.3389/fgstr.2026.1747118/full", "domain": "frontiersin.org", "snippet": "|IP-10 antagonist|Eldelumab (BMS-936557)|Fully human monoclonal IgG1 antibody targeting IP-10/CXCL10|NCT00656890, NCT01294410|Phase 2, Phase 2b|Completed; failed to meet primary endpoints|\n...\nAbrilumab, a human monoclonal IgG2 antibody targeting α4β7 integrin, was evaluated in two Phase 2 studies for moderate-to-severe UC.\n...\nBertilimumab is a recombinant human IgG4 monoclonal antibody that neutralizes human eotaxin-1 (CCL11), a chemokine involved in eosinophil recruitment and activation.", "date": "2026-01-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-29", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.84, "evidence": 0.7667}, "jev_score": 0.644, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Targeting Immune Cell Trafficking – Insights From Research Models ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8129496/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Treatment with anti-CXCL10 antibodies attenuated colitis in IL10-deficient mice and in DSS colitis and reduced cell infiltration to the lamina propria (73–76).\nIn clinical studies, treatment with a monoclonal antibody against CXCL10 was efficient for the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis (MDX-1100) (77).\nHowever, blocking CXCL10 with the antibody eldelumab failed to induce remission in patients with moderate-to-severe UC or CD (78–80).\n...\n|CXCL10|Epithelium|Eldelumab|Monoclonal antibody|IL-10^-/-^ and piroxicam colitis mouse model (74)|Yes|UC (Phase II) (78)|IV|No|Improvement of IBDQ score|", "date": "2021-05-04", "last_updated": "2026-08-30", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.89, "evidence": 0.7233}, "jev_score": 0.6437, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "The IBD Therapeutic Pipeline is Primed to Produce", "url": "https://practicalgastro.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/IBD-Therapeutic-Pipeline-Is-Primed-To-Produce.pdf", "domain": "practicalgastro.com", "snippet": "Eldelumab (BMS-936557) (Bristol-Myers \nSquibb) is a monoclonal antibody that binds to \nInterferon-γ-inducible protein-10 (IP-10, also known as CXCL10) and blocks lymphocyte\nmigration into intestinal epithelial cells.\nResults\n…", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-10", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.87, "evidence": 0.66}, "jev_score": 0.5742, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Chemokines and Chemokine Receptors as Therapeutic Targets in ...", "url": "https://www.bohrium.com/paper-details/chemokines-and-chemokine-receptors-as-therapeutic-targets-in-inflammatory-bowel-disease-pitfalls-and-promise/813089511494909953-97648", "domain": "bohrium.com", "snippet": "The CXCL10/CXCR3 axis mediates monocyte activation and drives tissue inflammation.\nEldelumab, a monoclonal antibody to CXCL10, has been investigated in clinical trials for the treatment of UC and Crohn's disease, but overall efficacy has not been demonstrated, although there were suggestions of responses in specific patient populations.\n...\nFuture research should focus on new ways of modelling pharmacokinetics, considering patient heterogeneity, and using sophisticated data to precisely target specific immune pathways.\n...\n## AbstractThe principal targets for anti-chemokine therapy in inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) have been the receptors CCR9 and CXCR3 and their respective ligands CCL25 and CXCL10. More recently CCR6 and its ligand CCL20 have also received attention, the expression of the latter in enterocytes being manipulated through Smad7 signalling. These pathways, selected based on their fundamental role in regulating mucosal immunity, have led to the development of several therapeutic candidates that have been tested in early phase clinical trials with variable clinical efficacy. In this article, we appraise the status of chemokine-directed therapy in IBD, review recent developments, and nominate future areas for therapeutic focus.", "date": "2025-01-27", "last_updated": "2025-09-06", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.84, "evidence": 0.6833}, "jev_score": 0.574, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Optimising Monoclonal Antibody Therapies for Inflammatory Bowel ...", "url": "https://www.dovepress.com/optimising-monoclonal-antibody-drug-development-for-inflammatory-bowel-peer-reviewed-fulltext-article-CEG", "domain": "dovepress.com", "snippet": "HXN1002 targets both TL1A and α4β7 integrin, which mediates the homing of lymphocytes to gut-associated lymphoid tissue via binding to MAdCAM-1 on endothelial cells.^110^ Preclinical studies presented by SPYRE Therapeutics in 2025 showed enhanced efficacy of dual inhibition in murine colitis models, and a Phase 2 study evaluating the extended half-life antibodies as single agents and pairwise combinations that started in 2025.^111^", "date": "2025-09-30", "last_updated": "2026-10-01", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.51, "evidence": 0.6667}, "jev_score": 0.34, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Product Pipeline Summary", "url": "https://jyanttech.com/index.php?/pipeline", "domain": "jyanttech.com", "snippet": "|Product (Target)|Indication|Pre-Clin.|Phase 1|Phase 2|Phase 3|\n|--|--|--|--|--|--|\n|JT02 (CXCL10)|IBD|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-02-09", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.69, "evidence": 0.34}, "jev_score": 0.2346, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Exploring the Pipeline of Novel Therapies for Inflammatory ...", "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2227-9059/11/3/747", "domain": "mdpi.com", "snippet": "Reference #18.683c217.1742858964.400e5f04", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-03-24", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.24, "evidence": 0.1233}, "jev_score": 0.0296, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Biological agents as attractive targets for inflammatory bowel ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0925443924006422", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-30", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.16, "evidence": 0.06}, "jev_score": 0.0096, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Study Details Page", "url": "https://www.abbvieclinicaltrials.com/study/?id=JSPP-12-01", "domain": "abbvieclinicaltrials.com", "snippet": "AbbVie Clinical Trials is designed to support, inform, and help patients in a clinical study or those who are interested in participating.", "date": "2024-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-05-23", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.09, "evidence": 0.0033}, "jev_score": 0.0003, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 1,