tions the trial is for\nCrohn’s Disease\nWhat the trial is testing?\nMORF-057\nCould I receive a Placebo?\nYes\nEnrollment Goal\n385\nTrial Dates\nJul 18, 2024 - Jun 2030\nHow long will I be in the trial?\nAbout 1 year and 3 months\nTrial Phase\nII\nYesNo\n...\n### Participants Must:\n- Have moderate to severe Crohn’s Disease for at least 3 months\n- Have tried and failed conventional and/or advanced Crohn's disease treatments\n### Participants must not:\n- Have a current diagnosis of:\n- Ulcerative Colitis or has clinical findings of ulcerative colitis.\n- Have had extensive bowel resection or will need intestinal or intra-abdominal surgery\n- Have evidence of toxic megacolon, intra-abdominal abscess, or stricture or stenosis\n...\nThis study is part of a program of research studies for adults with Crohn’s disease, ulcerative colitis, and irritable bowel syndrome (IBS), with each one having its own requirements to participate.\nThe questionnaire below will be used to prescreen you for all available studies.\nYour answers will determine if you are eligible for further screening for one of these studies.\nSpeak to a study nurse at 1-844-952-6623 or\nAnswer a few questions to see if you meet key criteria for this study.\n...\nIf you are in the United States, there is no need to select a clinical trial site.\nJust click here to answer the study questionnaire and, if you are a preliminary fit, a study nurse will be in touch for next steps.", "date": "2024-07-18", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.52, "evidence": 0.4433}, "jev_score": 0.2305, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Mocravimod", "url": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/mocravimod", "domain": "pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Treatment in haematopoietic stem cell transplantation\nActive Substance\n...\nStatus of Orphan Designation", "date": "2025-06-14", "last_updated": "2025-06-15", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.66, "evidence": 0.23}, "jev_score": 0.1518, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "NCT07483073 | A Master Protocol (IIBD): A Study of Multiple Drugs ...", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT07483073", "domain": "clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "## A Master Protocol (IIBD): A Study of Multiple Drugs in Adults With Ulcerative Colitis or Crohn's Disease\nClinicalTrials.gov ID NCT07483073\n...\nStudy IIBD is a master protocol that will support a collection of individual sub studies that share key design components.\nParticipants will be assigned to the appropriate study prior to randomization to a treatment group.\nThe studies aim to evaluate the efficacy and safety of new treatments in adults with moderately to severely active ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease and will last at least 62 weeks.\nOfficial Title\nA Master Protocol for Phase 2, Randomized, Controlled Studies of Multiple Interventions for the Treatment of Adults With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis or Crohn's Disease\nConditions\nColitis, UlcerativeCrohn Disease\n...\nIntervention/Treatment\n- Drug: Mirikizumab - Intravenous (IV)\n- Drug: Mirikizumab - Subcutaneous (SC)\n- Drug: LY4395089\n...\nStudy Start (Actual)\n2026-05-04\nPrimary Completion (Estimated)\n2027-06\nStudy Completion (Estimated)\n2028-03\nEnrollment (Estimated)\n60\nStudy Type\nInterventional\nPhase\nPhase 2\n...\n- Must have an established diagnosis of Ulcerative Colitis (UC) or Crohn's Disease (CD) for at least 3 month duration, which includes clinical and endoscopic evidence of UC or CD and a histopathology report that supports a diagnosis of UC or CD.\n- For UC:\n- Have moderately to severely active UC as defined by a modified Mayo score (mMS) of 5-9 points and Endoscopic Subscore (ES) greater than or equal to (≥) 2, confirmed by the central reader and rectal bleeding (RB)≥1, with endoscopy performed within 21 days prior to Visit 2.\n...\n- Must not have a current diagnosis of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)-unclassified or primary sclerosing cholangitis\n- For UC - must not have a current diagnosis of CD\n- For CD - must not have a current diagnosis of UC\n- Must not have had or will need bowel resection or intestinal or intra-abdominal surgery as specified in the protocol\n- Must not have complications of UC or CD, including but not limited to stricture or stenosis (some exceptions allowed for CD) or short bowel syndrome\n...\n- Must not have failed more than 5 approved advanced treatments for UC or CD with different mechanisms of action\n- Must not have failed an anti-interleukin-23p19 (anti-IL-23p19) antibody treatment\n- Must not have received or will need any prohibited medications for UC or CD as specified in the protocol\nAges Eligible for Study\n18 Years to 80 Years (Adult, Older Adult )\nSexes Eligible for Study\n...\n|Participant Group/Arm|Active Comparator: Mirikizumab Study Period 1: mirikizumab administered via IV.\nStudy Period 2: Responders will receive mirikizumab SC.|\n|Participant Group/Arm|Experimental: LY4395089 and Mirikizumab Co-Administration Study Period 1: Co-administration of LY4395089 administered orally and mirikizumab administered IV.\nStudy Period 2: Responders will stop LY4395089 and receive mirikizumab SC.|", "date": "2026-09-08", "last_updated": "2026-09-19", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.3, "evidence": 0.3967}, "jev_score": 0.119, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Mocravimod", "url": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/11155874", "domain": "pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Treatment in haematopoietic stem cell transplantation\nActive Substance\nMocravimod", "date": "2025-06-21", "last_updated": "2025-06-26", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.68, "evidence": 0.15}, "jev_score": 0.102, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Official Title of Study", "url": "https://cdn.clinicaltrials.gov/large-docs/90/NCT04877990/Prot_SAP_000.pdf", "domain": "cdn.clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "An Open-label, Multi-center Extension Study to Evaluate the Long-term Safety and Efficacy of Deucravacitinib in Participants with Moderate to Severe Crohn’s Disease or\n...\nNCT Number: NCT04877990 \n...\nIM011077 is an open-label, long-term extension study designed to evaluate the long-term safety and efficacy of deucravacitinib (BMS-986165) 6 mg twice daily (BID) in participants who have previously been enrolled in a Phase 2 deucravacitinib study for moderate to severe Crohn’s disease\n(CD) (Study IM011023) or moderate to severe ulcerative colitis (UC) (Studies IM011024 and\nIM011127).\nStudy Population: Adults with CD or UC who have completed participation in a preceding study, including Studies IM011023, IM011024, or IM011127, may be eligible to enroll in Study\nIM011077.\n...\nParticipants will receive deucravacitinib 6 mg BID PO in a tablet formulation.\n...\nThis is an open label, multi-center study to evaluate the long-term safety and tolerability of deucravacitinib in participants with moderate to severe CD or moderate to severe UC who have completed one of the applicable parent studies (IM011023, IM011024, or IM011127), are likely to safely derive a clinical benefit from ongoing treatment with deucravacitinib, and are willing and able to participate.\nParticipants will receive deucravacitinib 6 mg BID PO in a tablet formulation.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-05", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.22, "evidence": 0.24}, "jev_score": 0.0528, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Adjunctive and… · Phase III (2024-512752-38-00) - CTIS.eu", "url": "https://ctis.eu/trial/2024-512752-38-00", "domain": "ctis.eu", "snippet": "- **ClinicalTrials.gov**\nNCT05429632\n...\n|Synopsis of the