ints with MES of at least 2, and inadequate response or intolerance to prior treatments including corticosteroids, immunomodulators, or advanced therapies, while excluding those with CD, toxic megacolon, prior vedolizumab exposure, or contraindicated medications, with the study completing primary outcomes in October 2025 and final completion estimated for February 2027.", "date": "2026-01-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-25", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.9}, "jev_score": 0.873, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Integrin alpha 4 beta 7", "url": "https://jp.acrobiosystems.com/category/target-protein/integrin-alpha-4-beta-7", "domain": "jp.acrobiosystems.com", "snippet": "|Drugs in Clinical Trials|14|Target Synonym|LPAM-1，Lymphocyte Peyer's patch Adhesion Molecule 1|\n...\n|Vedolizumab biosimilar (Polpharma Biologics)|PB-016|Phase 3 Clinical|Polpharma Biologics Sa|Colitis, Ulcerative; Crohn Disease; Pouchitis|Details|\n...\n|Emvistegrast|GS-1427|Phase 2 Clinical|Gilead Sciences Sl|Colitis, Ulcerative; Inflammatory Bowel Diseases|Details|", "date": "2024-09-23", "last_updated": "2026-09-02", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.7933}, "jev_score": 0.7536, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "IBD therapeutics: what is in the pipeline?", "url": "https://fg.bmj.com/content/13/e1/e35", "domain": "fg.bmj.com", "snippet": "In U-ACCOMPLISH randomised controlled phase III trial, 8-week UPA 45 mg once daily has induced clinical remission in 33.5% of patients with UC, vs 4.5% of placebo, endoscopic remission in 44% vs 8.3% and histological remission in 36.7% vs 5.8% (p<0.001) induction treatment led to statistically significant improvements in clinical, endoscopic and combined endoscopic-histological endpoints.\n...\nEtrolizumab is a gut selective monoclonal antibody (mAb) that selectively targets the β7 subunit of both α4β7 and α4E7 integrins.9 The HICKORY phase III study showed 105 mg 4 weekly etrolizumab-induced remission was significantly higher in patients with UC (18.5%) previously treated with anti-TNF agent at week 14 vs placebo (6.3%).\n...\nIn a Japanese phase III double-blind RCT, AJM300 was well tolerated and induced a clinical response(defined as a reduction in Mayo Clinic score of 30% or more and 3 or more, a reduction in rectal bleeding score of 1 or more or rectal bleeding subscore of 1 or less, and an endoscopic subscore of 1 or less) in patients with moderately active UC who had an inadequate response or intolerance to mesalazine, at week 8.\n...\nPhase III UC trials are currently recruiting (NCT03996369, NCT03945188, NCT03950232, NCT04176588).", "date": "2022-08-01", "last_updated": "2024-11-01", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.89, "evidence": 0.7933}, "jev_score": 0.706, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Gilead Diversifies: Emvistegrast, Cancer Catalysts & Q2 2026 ...", "url": "https://www.pienomial.com/publication-reports/gilead-bets-billions-on-diversification-but-key-uc-asset-emvistegrast-remains-a-black-box", "domain": "pienomial.com", "snippet": "# Gilead Bets Billions on Diversification, But Key UC Asset Emvistegrast Remains a Black Box\n...\n|Indication|ulcerative colitis|\n|--|--|\n|Drug|emvistegrast|\n|Mechanism of Action|integrin inhibitor|\n|Company|Gilead|\n|Trial Phase|Phase 2|\n|Trial Acronym|SWIFT|\n|NCT ID|NCT06290934|\n|Category|Regulatory Milestone|\n|Sub Category|Approval Pending|\n...\nKey upcoming catalysts in the latter half of 2026 include data readouts for emvistegrast in Phase 2 for ulcerative colitis and edecesertib in Phase 2 for cutaneous lupus erythematosus.\n...\nThese include Phase 2 data for the integrin inhibitor emvistegrast in the SWIFT trial for ulcerative colitis and for the kinase blocker edecesertib in the COSMIC trial for cutaneous lupus erythematosus.\n...\nEmvistegrast is entering a competitive landscape of gut-selective therapies targeting the α4β7 integrin pathway.\nThis mechanism, successfully commercialized with the approval of vedolizumab for ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease, has a robust pipeline of other investigational agents.\nSeveral other monoclonal antibodies targeting this interaction have been evaluated in clinical trials, demonstrating continued interest in this therapeutic strategy for inflammatory bowel disease.\n|Drug Name|Mechanism of Action|Reported Development Status & Intervention Data|\n...\n|Vedolizumab (MNL-0002)|Gut-specific monoclonal antibody that neutralizes the α4β7 integrin.|Approved for UC and CD.\nPhase III trials showed positive results, and a placebo-controlled RCT confirmed its efficacy in preventing postoperative recurrence in CD patients.|\n|AMG181|Targets the α4β7 integrin.|Identified as an investigational agent in a 2013 literature review.|\n|Etrolizumab|Integrin-targeting agent.|Identified as an investigational agent in a 2013 literature review.|\n|PF-00547659|Investigational monoclonal antibody.|Reported to show high promise in trials with a potentially attractive benefit-risk ratio.|\n|AJM300|Investigational monoclonal antibody.|Reported to show high promise in clinical trials.|\n|rhuMAb β7|Investigational monoclonal antibody.|Reported to show high promise in clinical trials.|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-24", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.7367}, "jev_score": 0.6999, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Gastrointestinal - Drug Hunter", "url": "https://drughunter.com/category/gastrointestinal", "domain": "drughunter.com", "snippet": "Emvistegrast (GS-1427) is an oral α4β7 integrin inhibitor in Ph.\n2 for UC, first disclosed by Gilead at the ACS Fall 2025 meeting.\nIt targets the same clinically validated pathway as vedolizumab (Entyvio®), aiming to deliver gut-selective efficacy in an orally administered drug.\nNotably, this discovery story is a compelling case study in translating an antibody-targeted pathway into a small molecule approach, engineering an exceptional pharmacological profile through atropisomeric control, and optimizing ADME-PK to achieve a selective α4β7 inhibitor suitable for once-daily oral dosing.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-24", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.71}, "jev_score": 0.6674, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "a pipeline of novel drugs for UC management", "url": "https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/efc2/a31ee078832397a8583aedd937aa7a780012.pdf", "domain": "pdfs.semanticscholar.org", "snippet": "a4b7 antagonist\nEmvistegrast (GS-\n1427)\nOral a4b7 integrin inhibitor\nNCT06290934\nPhase 2\nPrimary completion Oct 2025, final completion Feb\n2027\n...\nThe study led to the current Phase 3 trial (NCT05181137)) which began in November 2021 and, based on its estimated completion date, is anticipated to be ongoing; however, no interim results have been publicly reported to date.\n...\n2.2.5 Emvistegrast\nEmvistegrast is an oral a4b7 integrin inhibitor designed to block immune cell migration to the gastrointestinal tract, reducing intestinal inflammation in UC patients.\nA Phase 2 double-blind, placebo-controlled, multicenter RCT evaluates three different doses of GS-1427 against placebo over 76 weeks, with the primary endpoint measuring clinical response at week 12 defined as a decrease in mMS of at least 2 points with 30% reduction from baseline and improved RBS (NCT06290934).\nParticipants must be adults aged 18–75 with moderately to severely active UC confirmed by endoscopy and histology, having at least 15 cm disease extent from anal verge, modified MS of 5–9 points with MES of at least 2, and inadequate response or intolerance to prior treatments including corticosteroids, immunomodulators, or advanced therapies, while excluding those with CD, toxic megacolon, prior vedolizumab exposure, or contraindicated medications, with the study completing primary outcomes in October 2025 and final completion estimated for February 2027.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-21", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.77, "evidence": 0.59}, "jev_score": 0.4543, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "emvistegrast | Ligand page", "url": "https://www.guidetopharmacology.org/GRAC/LigandDisplayForward?tab=clinical&ligandId=14189", "domain": "guidetopharmacology.org", "snippet": "|**Synonyms:** example 356 [WO2020092375] | GS-1427 | GS1427 **Compound class:** Synthetic organic **Comment:** Emvistegrast (GS-1427) is an oral α4/β7 integrin inhibitor.\nIt was designed to reduce α4β7 integrin-mediated recruitment of α4β7-expressing lymphocytes to the gut, as disease-modifying mechanism for inflammatory bowel disease.\nGS-1427 is one of the inhibitors claimed in patent WO2020092375A1 [1].\n...\n|Emvistegrast (GS-1427) is a clinical lead candidate.\nIt is being developed (by Gilead Sciences) for immunomodulatory potential in ulcerative colitis.|\n...\n|NCT06290934|Study of GS-1427 in Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis|Phase 2 Interventional|Gilead Sciences| | |", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-17", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.56}, "jev_score": 0.4536, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "UC Davis Inflammatory Bowel Disease Clinical Trials for 2026", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.ucdavis.edu/inflammatory-bowel-disease", "domain": "clinicaltrials.ucdavis.edu", "snippet": "** Sacramento, California** and other locations\n- ## Duvakitug in Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis\n“Volunteer for research and contribute to discoveries that may improve health care for you, your family, and your community!”\nopen to eligible people ages 16-80\nThis is a multinational, multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, Phase 3 induction study to evaluate the efficacy and safety of duvakitug in participants with moderately to severely active Ulcerative Colitis (UC).\nStudy details include: The study duration may be up to 35 weeks with: - Screening period - 12-week Sub-Study 1 (Single-Arm Open-Label Feeder Induction) or Sub-Study 2 (Pivotal Induction) - 12-week Sub-Study 3 (Extended Induction for non-responders) - 45 days follow-up visit for participants who do not enroll into the maintenance study (EFC18359) The treatment duration will be up to 12 weeks in each sub-study.\n...\n** Sacramento, California** and other locations\n- ## GS-1427 in Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis\n** Sorry, in progress, not accepting new patients\nThe goal of this study is to learn if emvistegrast (formerly GS-1427) is effective in treating participants with moderate to severe ulcerative colitis.\nThe study will compare participants in different treatment groups treated with emvistegrast with participants treated with placebo.\nThe primary objective of this study is to assess the efficacy of emvistegrast, compared with placebo control, in achieving clinical response at Week 12.", "date": "2026-09-23", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.5467}, "jev_score": 0.4428, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "vepdegestrant (ARV-471) - Drug Hunter", "url": "https://drughunter.com/molecule/arvinas-er-chimeric-degrader?hss_channel=tw-1366500304867401729", "domain": "drughunter.com", "snippet": "## emvistegrast (GS-1427)\nEmvistegrast (GS-1427) is an oral α4β7 integrin inhibitor in Ph.\n2 for UC, first disclosed by Gilead at the ACS Fall 2025 meeting.\nIt targets the same clinically validated pathway as vedolizumab (Entyvio®), aiming to deliver gut-selective efficacy in an orally administered drug.\nNotably, this discovery story is a compelling case study in translating an antibody-targeted pathway into a small molecule approach, engineering an exceptional pharmacological profile through atropisomeric control, and optimizing ADME-PK to achieve a selective α4β7 inhibitor suitable for once-daily oral dosing.Read More(", "date": "2025-10-01", "last_updated": "2025-10-06", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.56, "evidence": 0.49}, "jev_score": 0.2744, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 10098.3, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:23+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q025-1", "row_id": "q025", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Ulcerative Colitis competing agents with the same mechanism of action as HEMAY007, targeting TNF-α Tumor Necrosis Factor Alpha", "query": "HEMAY007 ulcerative colitis anti-TNF Phase 2 competitors", "anchors": ["HEMAY007"], "search_latency_ms": 498.2, "target": "drugs competing with HEMAY007: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 418.2, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10627, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000446, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.9183, "results": [{"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Advancing therapeutic frontiers: a pipeline of novel drugs ...", "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/gastroenterology/articles/10.3389/fgstr.2026.1747118/full", "domain": "frontiersin.org", "snippet": "The therapeutic pipeline for moderate to severe ulcerative colitis currently encompasses over 100 investigational agents in Phase II and III clinical development.\n...\nThe introduction of biologic therapies targeting tumor necrosis factor-α (TNF-α) (infliximab, adalimumab, golimumab), integrin α4β7 (vedolizumab), and interleukin (IL)-12/23 pathways (ustekinumab, mirikizumab, guselkumab, risankizumab) has transformed treatment paradigms for moderate to severe UC (11, 13–21).\n...\n|TNF modulator|Hemay007|Small molecule TNF-α regulator|NCT03977480|Phase 2|Terminated early Aug 2022 due to recruitment difficulties|\n|TNF-α/OX40L inhibitor|SAR442970|Bispecific pentavalent Nanobody targeting TNF-α and OX40L|NCT06975722|Phase 2b|Started July 2025; estimated completion Dec 2026|\n|TNFR1 antagonist|Balinatunfib (SAR441566)|Small molecule stabilizing asymmetric soluble TNF|NCT06867094|Phase 2|Recruiting; started March 2025, estimated completion July 2027|\n...\nThree anti-TNF monoclonal antibodies are currently approved for UC: infliximab (chimeric mouse-human IgG1), adalimumab (fully human IgG1), and golimumab (fully human IgG1).\n...\nNext-generation TNF pathway inhibitors employ several innovative strategies to address these limitations: selective TNFR1 antagonists preserving TNFR2 signaling (balinatunfib/SAR441566), bispecific antibodies targeting TNF-α plus additional mediators for synergistic blockade (SAR442970 targeting TNF-α and OX40L\n), small molecule TNF modulators avoiding immunogenicity (hemay007), CD40 antagonists indirectly modulating TNF-related pathways (ravagalimab), enhanced imaging techniques using fluorescently labeled agents to optimize dosing (adalimumab-680LT), and biosimilar formulations providing increased access (CT-P13).\n...\nA Phase II study (NCT03977480) evaluated Hemay007, a small molecule that acts as a TNF-α regulator, using a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled design with four treatment arms comparing different dosing regimens (400 mg BID, 800 mg QD, 600 mg BID, and placebo) over 12 weeks followed by an open-label extension.\nThe primary outcome measured clinical response defined as MS reduction of ≥3 points and ≥30% from baseline with RBS improvement, while inclusion criteria required patients aged 18–70 years with active UC (MS ≥4, MES ≥2) who had treatment failure or intolerance to standard therapies including 5-ASA, corticosteroids, immunomodulators, or anti-TNF agents.\nThe study was terminated early due to recruitment difficulties, completing in August 2022 with only 70 of the planned 288 patients enrolled, and no efficacy or safety results have been posted on ClinicalTrials.gov.\n...\nMufemilast (Hemay005) is a selective phosphodiesterase 4 inhibitor being tested in a multicenter, double-blind, placebo-controlled Phase II RCT (NCT05486104) with three arms comparing 45mg twice daily, 60mg twice daily, and placebo over 12 weeks of treatment followed by 4 weeks of observation.\n...\nTilpisertib (GS-4875) is an oral MAP3K8/TPL2 inhibitor tested in two Phase 2 trials for moderately to severely active UC.", "date": "2026-01-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-29", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.9467}, "jev_score": 0.9183, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Current and Emerging Biologics for Ulcerative Colitis - PMC", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4282853/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "For example, infliximab and adalimumab, which are anti-TNF agents, are being used for treating ulcerative colitis.\nRecently, golimumab, another anti-TNF agent, and vedolizumab, an anti-adhesion therapy, have been approved for ulcerative colitis by the U.S.\nFood and Drug Administration.\n...\nInfliximab, an anti-tumor necrosis factor alpha (TNF-α) monoclonal antibody, is the first biologic to have received the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approval and to be clinically used for ulcerative colitis.\nRecently, the TNF antagonists adalimumab and golimumab have shown significant effectiveness in large scale clinical studies, and have been in use since receiving FDA approval.\n...\n|Golimumab|PURSUIT-Maintenance^29^|N=464 Moderately to severely active UC|100 mg SC every 4 weeks after induction|Clinical response at week 54|49.7% (GLM 100 mg)|\n...\nVedolizumab (MLN-0002) is an α4β7 integrin binding IgG1 humanized monoclonal antibody that suppresses leukocyte adhesion by blocking the interaction between MAdCAM-1 and α4β7 integrin.", "date": "2015-01-15", "last_updated": "2026-09-30", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.8933}, "jev_score": 0.8486, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "TNF-alpha - ACROBiosystems", "url": "https://kr.acrobiosystems.com/category/target-protein/tnf-alpha", "domain": "kr.acrobiosystems.com", "snippet": "|Recombinant anti-TNFα monoclonal antibody (Wuhan Institute of Biological Products)| |Phase 3 Clinical|Wuhan Institute Of Biological Products Co Ltd|Plaque psoriasis|Details|\n...\n|Hemay007|Hemay-007|Phase 2 Clinical|Tianjin Hemay Bio-Tech Co Ltd|Arthritis, Rheumatoid; Colitis, Ulcerative; Inflammatory Bowel Diseases|Details|\n...\n|SOR-101|SOR-101; SOR101|Phase 2 Clinical|Sorriso Pharmaceuticals Inc|Colitis|Details|\n|IMB-101 (IMBiologics)|IMB-101 (IMBiologics); HDM-3019; IMB101 (IMBiologics); HDM3019; NAV-240|Phase 2 Clinical|IMBiologics Corp|Arthritis, Rheumatoid; Hidradenitis Suppurativa|Details|\n...\n|Brivekimig|SAR-442970; SAR442970|Phase 2 Clinical|Sanofi|Colitis, Ulcerative; Crohn Disease; Diabetes Mellitus, Type 1; Glomerulonephritis; Glomerulosclerosis, Focal Segmental; Hidradenitis Suppurativa; Inflammation; Nephrosis|Details|\n|Guselkumab/Golimumab|JNJ-78934804|Phase 2 Clinical|Janssen Research & Development Llc|Colitis, Ulcerative; Crohn Disease|Details|", "date": "2024-09-23", "last_updated": "2026-09-21", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.8733}, "jev_score": 0.8296, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Landscape of new drugs and targets in inflammatory bowel ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9752289/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "f IBD, including anti‐tumour necrosis factor‐α or tumour necrosis factor alpha (TNF‐α) (such as infliximab (IFX), ^1^ , ^2^ adalimumab, ^3^ certolizumab pegol ^4^ and golimumab(GOL) ^5^ ), anti‐integrin *α* ~4~ *β* ~7~ (vedolizumab), ^6^ , ^7^ anti‐interleukin (interleukin)‐12/23 (ustekinumab ,UST), ^8^ Janus kinase (JAK) inhibitors in UC (such as tofacitinib and filgotinib), ^9^ , ^10^ as well as sphingosine‐1 phosphate (S1P) receptor modulator, for the treatment of moderately to severely active UC, which \n...\n^29^ Phase 2 and phase 3 studies are currently underway in UC and CD (including a phase 3 study comparing risankizumab to UST in moderate to severe CD patients, who have failed anti‐TNF).\n...\n^52^ , ^53^ Filgotinib, upadacitinib and ivarmacitinib are three other JAK‐inhibitors that have been developed in IBD.\n...\n^53^ The efficacy of upadacitinib in UC was demonstrated in a phase 2b study and confirmed in three phase 3 studies.\n...\nIvarmacitinib (formely SHR0302) is another novel oral selective JAK1 inhibitor.\nRecruitment for four‐arm (oral SHR0302 4 mg once daily, 8 mg once daily, 4 mg twice daily, and PBO) phase 2 RCT are completed in moderate to severe UC (AMBER2 or NCT03675477) and CD (NCT03677648).\n...\n^151^ , ^152^ , ^153^ , ^154^ Other mechanisms of action include anti‐chemokines (also playing a pivotal role in T cells recruitment in the gut), ^155^ oral anti‐CD3, anti‐CD40 IV/SC, anti‐CD162 IV, inhibitor of phosphodiesterase 4 (apremilast PO), ^156^ oral active TNF‐α inhibitor (hemay007) ^157^ but also anti‐TL1A IV.\n...\n  Phase II study of Hemay007 in patients with active ulcerative colitis ‐ full text view. ClinicalTrials.gov. https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT03977480. Accessed 4 August 2022. [Google Scholar]", "date": "2022-09-16", "last_updated": "2026-05-05", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.93, "evidence": 0.8133}, "jev_score": 0.7564, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Emerging Therapies for Ulcerative Colitis: Updates from Recent ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10441644/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|**Anti-TNF**|CT-P13|TNF|SC|Phase III completed|\n|**Anti-TNF**|OPRX-106|TNF|Oral|Phase II completed|\n...\n|**PDE4 Inhibitors**|Apremilast|PDE4|Oral|Phase II completed|\n...\nMORF-057 is another oral small molecule that inhibits α4ß7 receptors.\nData from the Phase 1 clinical trial were presented as an abstract.40 The medication was well tolerated when it was given to healthy volunteers and had a favorable safety profile.\nA phase IIb study (EMERALD-2) was launched in late 2022.\n...\nCBP-307 is a synthetic, oral S1P receptor modulator with selectivity for S1PR1.103 A phase II randomized controlled trial evaluating the efficacy and safety of 0.2 mg of CBP-307 in moderate-to-severe UC has been completed.", "date": "2023-08-17", "last_updated": "2026-08-12", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.9, "evidence": 0.8067}, "jev_score": 0.726, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Advances in the Treatment of Ulcerative Colitis—From Conventional ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12897911/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Infliximab (IFX) is the most widely and longest-used biologic drug, belonging to the group of tumor necrosis factor alpha (TNF-α) inhibitors [41].\nIt is a chimeric monoclonal antibody containing a murine Fab fragment (25%) and a human Fc fragment (75%).\n...\nMoreover, the phase 3 LUCENT-3 clinical trial is ongoing, with completion date estimated at the end of 2027, which aims to evaluate the long-term efficacy and safety of mirikizumab in participants with moderately to severely active UC.\nThe first reports confirm the effectiveness and safety following 152 weeks of continuous treatment, giving hope for the widespread use of this inhibitor in the near future [75].\n...\n|Ustekinumab|fully human monoclonal antibody of the IgG1қ class|administered intravenously during induction, subcutaneous formulation in maintenance|inhibiting activity of interleukin IL-12 and IL-23 leading to a reduction in inflammation.|[66,67]|\n|Guselkumab|fully human monoclonal antibody of the IgG1λ class|administered intravenously during induction, subcutaneous formulation in maintenance|inhibiting activity of IL-23, a regulatory cytokine that influences the differentiation, expansion, and survival of T lymphocyte subsets|[70,71,72]|\n|Mirikizumab|humanized monoclonal antibody of the IgG4 class|administered intravenously during induction, subcutaneous formulation in maintenance|inhibiting the interaction of human IL-23 cytokine and its receptor.|[72,73]|\n...\nApremilast blocks the synthesis of TNF-α and MMP3 in mucosal cells of patients with IBD.\n...\nAdvances in UC treatment are focusing on targeted therapies, extending beyond traditional steroids to novel biologic drugs, such as anti-TNFs, anti-integrins, anti-IL-12/23 agents, and small molecules, like JAK inhibitors and S1P modulators, which promote improved mucosal healing and reduced systemic side effects.", "date": "2026-02-04", "last_updated": "2026-09-26", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.92, "evidence": 0.7333}, "jev_score": 0.6746, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "This summary aims to give you an overview of the information contained in this", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2025/107914/a127807/sehk25120100830.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Phase II trials have been completed for ankylosing spondylitis (“AS”), with additional trials ongoing or planned for ulcerative colitis (“UC”), atopic dermatitis (“AD”), psoriatic arthritis (“PsA”), Crohn’s disease (“CD”), and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (“COPD”).\n...\nHemay007*(10)(11)\nPDE4B/\nPDE4\nMufemilast**\nTNF-α\nIgE/PDE4\n...\nHemay007, Hemay181 and Hemay808 were conducted as monotherapy therapies.\n...\nFor Hemay007, both Phase II clinical trials were approved based on results derived from the same Phase I clinical trial, Hemay007AU01.\n...\nWe solely conducted research on the development of Hemay007, Hemay808 and Hemay022.\n...\nHemay007\nHemay007 is screened from a compound library directed by multiple pharmacological functional substructures and is a TNF-�small molecule regulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model, Hemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the testing subjects, and pathological examinations of the intestines after treatment revealed that the colon tissue almost returned to a normal state.\nAs of the Latest Practicable Date, we have completed the\nPhase II clinical trial for monotherapy for UC.\nA Phase II clinical trial for rheumatoid arthritis\n(RA) is ongoing.\nFor phase II clinical trial of Hemay007 for UC at week 12, clinical response\nrates, as evaluated by both central laboratory and principal investigator (PI) assessments, there was no statistically significant differences across all groups in both the FAS and PPS populations (P > 0.05 for all comparisons).\nClinical remission rates at Week 12 were also comparable among the treatment and placebo groups, with no statistically significant differences observed.\nFor the development of Hemay007, we will prioritize the clinical trial for\nRA.\nCurrently, we do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps in UC.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-12-04", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.62, "evidence": 0.52}, "jev_score": 0.3224, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Comparative Effectiveness of Biologic or Small-Molecule ...", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK616537/", "domain": "ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "- *Aim 2:* To compare the effectiveness of a second-line biologic agent (vedolizumab) vs small molecule (tofacitinib) among patients with ulcerative colitis (UC) who are anti-TNF primary or secondary nonresponders:\n...\nWhen anti-TNF therapy fails, subsequent treatment options for UC include vedolizumab (an antibody to α4β7 integrin), tofacitinib (Janus kinase inhibitor), ustekinumab (antibody to IL-12/23), upadacitinib (selective Janus kinase 1 inhibitor), and ozanimod (sphingosine-1-phosphate receptor modulator).", "date": "2024-06-07", "last_updated": "2026-09-07", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.34, "evidence": 0.3367}, "jev_score": 0.1145, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Table 1.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12952356/table/T1/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|JAK Inhibitor|Ivarmacitinib (SHR0302)|Selective JAK1 inhibitor blocking JAK-STAT pathway|NCT03675477, NCT05181137|Phase 2, Phase 3|Phase 2 completed Feb 2021; Phase 3 status unknown|\n|JAK Inhibitor|Itacitinib (INCB039110)|JAK1 inhibitor|NCT03627052|Phase 2|Withdrawn Nov 2019 due to lack of recruitment|\n|JAK Inhibitor|Peficitinib (JNJ-54781532)|Oral pan-JAK inhibitor|NCT01959282|Phase 2b|Terminated Aug 2022 due to recruitment difficulties; development discontinued|\n|JAK Inhibitor|Izencitinib (TD-1473)|Gut-selective pan-JAK inhibitor|NCT03758443 (RHEA), NCT03920254|Phase 2b/3|Terminated Oct 2021 based on interim analysis|\n|JAK Inhibitor|Oncostellae (OST-122)|Oral gut-restricted JAK3/TYK2/ARK5 inhibitor|NCT04353791|Phase 1b/2a|Completed Dec 2022; development not pursued further|\n...\n|JAK Inhibitor|Brepocitinib (PF-06700841)|Oral dual TYK2/JAK1 inhibitor|NCT02958865 (VIBRATO)|Phase 2b|Completed May 2021; advanced to alopecia areata trials|\n|TYK2 Inhibitor|Deucravacitinib|Oral selective allosteric TYK2 inhibitor|NCT03934216 (LATTICE-UC), NCT04613518 (IM011-127)|Phase 2|Completed 2021-2023; terminated early for failing primary endpoints|\n|TYK2 Inhibitor|Zasocitinib (TAK-279)|AI-designed highly selective allosteric TYK2 inhibitor|NCT06254950, NCT06764615|Phase 2|Recruiting; estimated completion Aug 2027|\n...\n|α4β7 antagonist|MORF-057|Oral small-molecule inhibitor of α4β7 integrin|NCT05291689 (EMERALD-1), NCT05611671 (EMERALD-2)|Phase 2a, Phase 2b|EMERALD-1 completed Nov 2023; EMERALD-2 primary completion Nov 2024|\n...\n|TNF modulator|Hemay007|Small molecule TNF-α regulator|NCT03977480|Phase 2|Terminated early Aug 2022 due to recruitment difficulties|\n|TNF-α/OX40L inhibitor|SAR442970|Bispecific pentavalent Nanobody targeting TNF-α and OX40L|NCT06975722|Phase 2b|Started July 2025; estimated completion Dec 2026|\n...\n|PDE4 inhibitor|Mufemilast (Hemay005)|Selective phosphodiesterase 4 inhibitor|NCT05486104|Phase 2|Started Nov 2022; estimated completion Dec 2025|\n...\n|Combination|AMT-101 + Adalimumab|IL-10 fusion protein + TNF antagonist|NCT04583358 (LOMBARD), NCT05372939 (MARKET)|Phase 2a|Both completed by July 2022; LOMBARD failed primary endpoint|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-14", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.16, "evidence": 0.1033}, "jev_score": 0.0165, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Market Segmentation", "url": "https://www.coherentmarketinsights.com/industry-reports/ulcerative-colitis-drug-market", "domain": "coherentmarketinsights.com", "snippet": "- In June 2024 EpiEndo Pharmaceuticals, an Iceland-based clinical stage biopharma company, and AlveoliX, a Swiss innovator in organ-on-chip technology, announced progress in their EpicoliX Project with the identification of Enterothelin a Barriolide compound as a promising first-in-class therapy for ulcerative colitis marking an important step toward new treatment options for this chronic inflammatory disease.** **", "date": "2026-03-17", "last_updated": "2026-09-22", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.07, "evidence": 0.15}, "jev_score": 0.0105, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 916.4, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:23+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q025-2", "row_id": "q025", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Ulcerative Colitis competing agents with the same mechanism of action as HEMAY007, targeting TNF-α Tumor Necrosis Factor Alpha", "query": "HEMAY007 ulcerative colitis anti-TNF licensing availability", "anchors": ["HEMAY007"], "search_latency_ms": 1953.9, "target": "drugs competing with HEMAY007: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 397.0, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9184, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000386, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 1, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.574, "results": [{"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "TNF-alpha - ACROBiosystems", "url": "https://kr.acrobiosystems.com/category/target-protein/tnf-alpha", "domain": "kr.acrobiosystems.com", "snippet": "|Hemay007|Hemay-007|Phase 2 Clinical|Tianjin Hemay Bio-Tech Co Ltd|Arthritis, Rheumatoid; Colitis, Ulcerative; Inflammatory Bowel Diseases|Details|\n...\n|Recombinant human anti-TNFα monoclonal antibody (Qilu Pharmaceutical)| |Phase 1 Clinical|Qilu Pharmaceutical Co Ltd|Arthritis, Rheumatoid; Spondylitis, Ankylosing|Details|", "date": "2024-09-23", "last_updated": "2026-09-21", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.84, "evidence": 0.6833}, "jev_score": 0.574, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "This summary aims to give you an overview of the information contained in this", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2025/107914/a127807/sehk25120100830.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Phase II trials have been completed for ankylosing spondylitis (“AS”), with additional trials ongoing or planned for ulcerative colitis (“UC”), atopic dermatitis (“AD”), psoriatic arthritis (“PsA”), Crohn’s disease (“CD”), and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (“COPD”).\n...\nHemay007*(10)(11)\n...\nHemay007\nHemay007 is screened from a compound library directed by multiple pharmacological functional substructures and is a TNF-�small molecule regulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model, Hemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the testing subjects, and pathological examinations of the intestines after treatment revealed that the colon tissue almost returned to a normal state.\nAs of the Latest Practicable Date, we have completed the\nPhase II clinical trial for monotherapy for UC.\nA Phase II clinical trial for rheumatoid arthritis\n(RA) is ongoing.\nFor phase II clinical trial of Hemay007 for UC at week 12, clinical response\nrates, as evaluated by both central laboratory and principal investigator (PI) assessments, there was no statistically significant differences across all groups in both the FAS and PPS populations (P > 0.05 for all comparisons).\nClinical remission rates at Week 12 were also comparable among the treatment and placebo groups, with no statistically significant differences observed.\nFor the development of Hemay007, we will prioritize the clinical trial for\nRA.\nCurrently, we do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps in UC.\n...\nWhile Mufemilast received NDA approval from the NMPA in September 2025, we are in the early stages of commercial launch and do not anticipate recording any product sales in", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-12-04", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.65, "evidence": 0.4933}, "jev_score": 0.3206, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Hemay007(Hemay007) - 药物靶点：TNF-α_在研适应症：类风湿关节炎", "url": "https://synapse.zhihuiya.com/drug/c6cef31360b74c8b9fd3d4c563740a9e", "domain": "synapse.zhihuiya.com", "snippet": "|作用机制 TNF-α抑制剂(肿瘤坏死因子α抑制剂)|\n...\n|非在研适应症 溃疡性结肠炎炎症性肠病|\n...\n|在研机构 峡江和美药业有限公司天津合美医药科技有限公司|\n|非在研机构 Hemay Pharmaceutical Pty Ltd|\n|权益机构-|\n...\n|溃疡性结肠炎|药物发现|中国|天津合美医药科技有限公司|2019-08-13|\n|溃疡性结肠炎|药物发现|中国|峡江和美药业有限公司|2019-08-13|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-13", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.79, "evidence": 0.4033}, "jev_score": 0.3186, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Hemay007 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/c6cef31360b74c8b9fd3d4c563740a9e", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Synonyms\nTarget\nTNF-α\nAction\ninhibitors\nMechanism\nTNF-α inhibitors(Tumor necrosis factor α inhibitors)\n...\nActive Indication\n...\nInactive Indication\nColitis, Ulcerative\nInflammatory Bowel Diseases\nOriginator Organization\nTianjin Hemei Biological Technology Co.,Ltd.\nActive Organization\nXiajiang Hemei Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\nTianjin Hemay Pharmaceutical Technology Co., Ltd.\nInactive Organization\nHemay Pharmaceutical Pty Ltd\nLicense Organization\nDrug Highest Phase\nPhase 2\nFirst Approval Date\nRegulation\nSpecial Review Project (China)\n...\nNCT03977480\nTerminated\nPhase 2\nA Multicenter, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo Parallel Controlled Clinical Study on the Effecacy and Safety of Different Dosing Regimens of Hemay007 in Patients With Active Ulcerative Colitis\nThis study adopts a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, low-medium-high dose group and placebo parallel controlled clinical study design.\n...\nA multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical study on the efficacy and safety of different dosing regimens of Hemay007 in patients with active ulcerative colitis\n...\nChina\nTianjin Hemay Pharmaceutical Technology Co., Ltd.\n13 Aug 2019", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-30", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.72, "evidence": 0.44}, "jev_score": 0.3168, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Table 1.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12952356/table/T1/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|TNF modulator|Hemay007|Small molecule TNF-α regulator|NCT03977480|Phase 2|Terminated early Aug 2022 due to recruitment difficulties|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-14", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.77, "evidence": 0.4067}, "jev_score": 0.3132, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] 概覽", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2026/108622/a133802/sehk26060801682_c.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Hemay007。我們的關鍵產品Hemay007是通過多種藥理功能亞結構組合化\n合物庫篩選而來，是一種TNF-α小分子調節劑。在自發性UC猴模型中，\n...\nHemay007利用多種藥理方法從化合物庫篩選而來，是一種TNF-α小分子調節\n劑。在自發性UC猴模型中，Hemay007減少了患病猴子結腸中的潰瘍數量。給藥後對\n...\n准了補充申請。IND批准適用於在中國\n進行之Hemay007 200毫克片劑的臨床\n試驗的所有階段。(2)\n...\nHemay007：截至最後實際可行日期，針對Hemay007，我們擁有兩項待審的中國\n專利申請、四項已授權的美國專利、一項待審的美國專利申請。已授權的美國專利的\n預期到期時間範圍為2029年10月至2037年11月，包括任何專利期限延長的額外期限。\n我們擬於若干國家根據監管規定尋求上市獨佔期。\n截至最後實際可行日期，十項與Hemay007相關的已授權專利（四項在美國，中", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-04", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.68, "evidence": 0.4467}, "jev_score": 0.3038, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "OVERVIEW", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2025/107914/a127807/sehk25120100842.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Hemay007.\nOur key product, Hemay007 is screened from a compound library directed by multiple pharmacological functional substructures and is a TNF-�small molecule regulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model, Hemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the diseased monkeys, and pathological examinations of the intestines after treatment revealed that the colon tissue almost returned to a normal state.\nAs of the Latest Practicable Date, we had completed the\nPhase II clinical trial for monotherapy for UC and were also conducting a Phase II clinical trial for RA.\nWe plan to prioritize the clinical trial for RA and currently do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps for UC.\n...\nWe discovered and developed Hemay022 and retained global rights for its development and commercialization.\n...\nHemay007 is screened from a compound library using multiple pharmacological approaches and is a TNF-�small molecule modulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model,\nHemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the diseased monkeys.\n...\nFor the development of Hemay007, we will prioritize the clinical trial for RA.\nCurrently, we do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps in UC.\nWe do not currently have plans to initiate any additional clinical trials overseas in respect of Hemay007.\n...\nThe IND approval is\napplicable to all phases\nclinical trials of the use of\nHemay007 in 200mg\ntablets carried out in\nChina.(2)", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-12-04", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.66, "evidence": 0.44}, "jev_score": 0.2904, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Hemay Pharmaceutical Pty Ltd - Drug pipelines, Patents, Clinical trials", "url": "https://synapse-patsnap-com.libproxy1.nus.edu.sg/organization/89e96363c322c7183ab587d4cba40b4c", "domain": "synapse-patsnap-com.libproxy1.nus.edu.sg", "snippet": "Hemay007\nTarget\nTNF-α\nMechanism\nTNF-α inhibitors\nActive Org.\nXiajiang Hemei Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\n[+1]\nOriginator Org.\nTianjin Hemei Biological Technology Co.,Ltd.\nActive Indication\nRheumatoid Arthritis\nInactive Indication\nColitis, Ulcerative\n[+1]\n...\nPhase 2\n...\nPatents (Medical) associated with Hemay Pharmaceutical Pty Ltd\n...\nGlobal Highest Phase\nHemay007\n( TNF-α )\nInflammatory Bowel Diseases", "date": "2025-09-18", "last_updated": "2025-09-18", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.67, "evidence": 0.4067}, "jev_score": 0.2725, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Hemay007: TNF-alpha, Phase 2 in Ulcerative Colitis", "url": "https://assetmemo.bio/drug/hemay007", "domain": "assetmemo.bio", "snippet": "Discontinuedsponsor decision\n...\nDiscontinued, for reasons the sponsor has not stated\nHemay007 is Tianjin Hemay's oral candidate.\nIts only ulcerative colitis study, the Phase 2 NCT03977480, is TERMINATED on ClinicalTrials.gov for failure to recruit.\nScoped to the ulcerative colitis market only: the molecule continued elsewhere, with a Phase 2 rheumatoid arthritis study (NCT05247216) completed and last updated 2024-03, and no Crohn's disease study was ever registered.\n...\nAlso in development:Crohn's Disease · Phase 1\n...\n|Hemay007 — this drug|Phase 2|Small molecule|TNF-alpha| | |", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-21", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.69, "evidence": 0.3833}, "jev_score": 0.2645, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Xiajiang Hemei Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/defdc02b973c4a2db52adc812c16492b", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Hemay007\nTarget\nTNF-α\nMechanism\nTNF-α inhibitors\nActive Org.\nXiajiang Hemei Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\n[+1]\nOriginator Org.\nTianjin Hemei Biological Technology Co.,Ltd.\nActive Indication\nRheumatoid Arthritis\nInactive Indication\nColitis, Ulcerative\n[+1]\nDrug Highest Phase\nPhase 2\nFirst Approval Ctry.\n/ Loc.\nFirst Approval Date\n...\nHemay007\n( TNF-α )\nColitis, Ulcerative\nMore\nDiscontinued", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-30", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.65, "evidence": 0.4067}, "jev_score": 0.2644, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}], "total_ms": 2350.9, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:23+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q025-3", "row_id": "q025", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Ulcerative Colitis competing agents with the same mechanism of action as HEMAY007, targeting TNF-α Tumor Necrosis Factor Alpha", "query": "HEMAY007 TNF-alpha ulcerative colitis clinical development status", "anchors": ["HEMAY007"], "search_latency_ms": 2233.1, "target": "drugs competing with HEMAY007: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 346.9, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10477, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.00044, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 4, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.8011, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Advancing therapeutic frontiers: a pipeline of novel drugs for ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12952356/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|TNF modulator|Hemay007|Small molecule TNF-α regulator|NCT03977480|Phase 2|Terminated early Aug 2022 due to recruitment difficulties|\n|TNF-α/OX40L inhibitor|SAR442970|Bispecific pentavalent Nanobody targeting TNF-α and OX40L|NCT06975722|Phase 2b|Started July 2025; estimated completion Dec 2026|\n...\nThe study led to the current Phase 3 trial (NCT05181137)) which began in November 2021 and, based on its estimated completion date, is anticipated to be ongoing; however, no interim results have been publicly reported to date.\n...\nIt is being tested in a Phase 2, multicenter, placebo-controlled, double-blind RCT for moderately to severely active UC in 207 participants aged 18–75 who have inadequate response to conventional, biologic, or advanced therapies, with the primary outcome measuring clinical remission at week 12 using mMS, currently recruiting with estimated completion in August 2027 (NCT06254950).\n...\nA Phase II study (NCT03977480) evaluated Hemay007, a small molecule that acts as a TNF-α regulator, using a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled design with four treatment arms comparing different dosing regimens (400 mg BID, 800 mg QD, 600 mg BID, and placebo) over 12 weeks followed by an open-label extension.\nThe primary outcome measured clinical response defined as MS reduction of ≥3 points and ≥30% from baseline with RBS improvement, while inclusion criteria required patients aged 18–70 years with active UC (MS ≥4, MES ≥2) who had treatment failure or intolerance to standard therapies including 5-ASA, corticosteroids, immunomodulators, or anti-TNF agents.\nThe study was terminated early due to recruitment difficulties, completing in August 2022 with only 70 of the planned 288 patients enrolled, and no efficacy or safety results have been posted on ClinicalTrials.gov.\n...\nThe study began July 2025 with primary completion estimated December 2026 and study completion October 2029, including 16-week induction, maintenance period, and optional long-term extension up to 104 weeks for eligible participants.", "date": "2026-01-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-25", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.8433}, "jev_score": 0.8011, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Table 1.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12952356/table/T1/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|TNF modulator|Hemay007|Small molecule TNF-α regulator|NCT03977480|Phase 2|Terminated early Aug 2022 due to recruitment difficulties|\n|TNF-α/OX40L inhibitor|SAR442970|Bispecific pentavalent Nanobody targeting TNF-α and OX40L|NCT06975722|Phase 2b|Started July 2025; estimated completion Dec 2026|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-14", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.82}, "jev_score": 0.7708, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "a pipeline of novel drugs for UC management", "url": "https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/efc2/a31ee078832397a8583aedd937aa7a780012.pdf", "domain": "pdfs.semanticscholar.org", "snippet": "The therapeutic pipeline for moderate to severe ulcerative colitis currently encompasses over 100 investigational agents in Phase II and III clinical development.\n...\ninhibitor\nSAR442970\nBispecific pentavalent Nanobody targeting\nTNF-a and OX40L\nNCT06975722\nPhase 2b\nStarted July 2025; estimated completion Dec 2026\n...\nThe following section reviews investigational TNF pathway inhibitors currently in Phase II and III clinical development for moderate to severe UC.\n2.3.1 Hemay007\nA Phase II study (NCT03977480) evaluated Hemay007, a small molecule that acts as a TNF-a regulator, using a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled design with four treatment arms comparing different dosing regimens (400 mg\nBID, 800 mg QD, 600 mg BID, and placebo) over 12 weeks followed by an open-label extension.\nThe primary outcome measured clinical response defined as MS reduction of ≥3 points and ≥30% from baseline with RBS improvement, while inclusion criteria required patients aged 18–70 years with active UC (MS ≥4,\nMES ≥2) who had treatment failure or intolerance to standard therapies including 5-ASA, corticosteroids, immunomodulators, or anti-TNF agents.\nThe study was terminated early due to recruitment difficulties, completing in August 2022 with only 70 of the planned 288 patients enrolled, and no efficacy or safety results have been posted on ClinicalTrials.gov.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-21", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.92, "evidence": 0.72}, "jev_score": 0.6624, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Pipeline Includes Seven Small Molecule Drug Candidates", "url": "https://news.futunn.com/en/post/74292485/ipo-news-he-mei-pharmaceuticals-re-files-application-with-hkex", "domain": "news.futunn.com", "snippet": "The company has completed a Phase II trial for ankylosing spondylitis (AS), and additional trials for ulcerative colitis (UC), atopic dermatitis (AD), psoriatic arthritis (PsA), Crohn’s disease (CD), and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) are either ongoing or planned.\n...\nHemay007\nHemay007 was identified through screening a compound library combining multiple pharmacologically functional substructures and is a small-molecule modulator of TNF-α.\nIn a spontaneous UC monkey model, Hemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colon of subjects; histopathological examination of the gut post-treatment revealed that colonic tissue had nearly returned to a normal state.\nAs of the latest practicable date, the company has completed a Phase II clinical trial of Hemay007 as monotherapy for UC.\nA Phase II clinical trial for rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is currently underway.\nFor the Week 12 primary endpoint of the Phase II trial in UC, neither central laboratory assessment nor principal investigator (PI) evaluation demonstrated statistically significant differences in clinical response rates across all groups in either the full analysis set (FAS) or per-protocol set (PPS) populations (all comparisons: p > 0.05).\nSimilarly, no statistically significant difference was observed in clinical remission rates between the treatment and placebo groups at Week 12.\nCurrently, the company has not established a formal timeline for next steps in UC development.\nGiven limited financial resources, the company intends to prioritize clinical development of Mufemilast.\nConsequently, as of the latest practicable date, the issuance of the Phase II RA clinical trial report will be placed on hold.", "date": "2026-06-09", "last_updated": "2026-07-26", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.72, "evidence": 0.49}, "jev_score": 0.3528, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "This summary aims to give you an overview of the information contained in this", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2025/107914/a127807/sehk25120100830.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Phase II trials have been completed for ankylosing spondylitis (“AS”), with additional trials ongoing or planned for ulcerative colitis (“UC”), atopic dermatitis (“AD”), psoriatic arthritis (“PsA”), Crohn’s disease (“CD”), and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (“COPD”).\n...\nHemay007*(10)(11)\nPDE4B/\nPDE4\nMufemilast**\n...\nIgE/PDE4\n...\nFor Hemay007, both Phase II clinical trials were approved based on results derived from the same Phase I clinical trial, Hemay007AU01.\n...\nHemay007\nHemay007 is screened from a compound library directed by multiple pharmacological functional substructures and is a TNF-�small molecule regulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model, Hemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the testing subjects, and pathological examinations of the intestines after treatment revealed that the colon tissue almost returned to a normal state.\nAs of the Latest Practicable Date, we have completed the\nPhase II clinical trial for monotherapy for UC.\nA Phase II clinical trial for rheumatoid arthritis\n(RA) is ongoing.\nFor phase II clinical trial of Hemay007 for UC at week 12, clinical response\nrates, as evaluated by both central laboratory and principal investigator (PI) assessments, there was no statistically significant differences across all groups in both the FAS and PPS populations (P > 0.05 for all comparisons).\nClinical remission rates at Week 12 were also comparable among the treatment and placebo groups, with no statistically significant differences observed.\nFor the development of Hemay007, we will prioritize the clinical trial for\nRA.\nCurrently, we do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps in UC.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-12-04", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.64, "evidence": 0.5267}, "jev_score": 0.3371, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] 概覽", "url":