{"case_id": "q028-2", "row_id": "q028", "mode": "queries", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression tumour shrinkage in Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma animal models", "query": "HEC234055 PK-59 PDAC monotherapy tumour regression", "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "search_latency_ms": 4214.6, "target": "HEC234055", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 328.3, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7606, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000319, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 1, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.5736, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] E262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4 - HKEXnews", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0423/2026042301899.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Sub-nanomolar cell activity: In a variety of KRAS mutation-driven cancer cell lines, its anti-proliferative activity reaches the sub-nanomolar level, with half- maximal inhibitory concentration (‘‘IC50’’) as low as 0.49 nanomolar (‘‘nM’’), showing potent inhibitory capabilities superior to current benchmark molecules.\n...\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In multiple KRAS-mutated xenograft tumor models\n(including pancreatic, lung and colorectal cancers), oral administration can produce\ndose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induce tumor regression.\n...\nGood pharmacokinetics (PK) and excellent safety profile: Oral bioavailability is good across all preclinical species. The safety evaluation results show that hERG inhibition IC50>10 micromolar (‘‘μM’’), and the safety window in the 28-day GLP toxicology study is over 90 times.\n...\nThe preclinical research data disclosed in this announcement are derived from laboratory and animal model studies, and the relevant drug candidates have not yet undergone clinical trials\nin\nhumans.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-04-23", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.72, "evidence": 0.7967}, "jev_sco