{"case_id": "q031-3", "row_id": "q031", "mode": "queries", "objective": "SPR2015 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) animal models", "query": "SPR2015 PDAC monotherapy xenograft tumour growth inhibition", "anchors": ["SPR2015"], "search_latency_ms": 5321.8, "target": "SPR2015", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 377.8, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9015, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000379, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.9603, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "SPR2015是一种高效且选择性的KRAS G12D（ON）抑制剂，在临床前模型中...", "url": "https://www.posterkeep.com/c/aacr-2026/p/5660", "domain": "posterkeep.com", "snippet": "SPR2015通过增强CypA竞争性结合，实现快速而持续的靶点结合，优于另一种G12D（ON）抑制剂。在小鼠PDAC/NSCLC异种移植模型中，SPR2015在10 mg/kg（口服，q.d.）\n时有效抑制肿瘤生长，并在30 mg/kg（口服，q.d.）时实现肿瘤消退。这些模型中的伴随PK/PD研究建立了肿瘤生长抑制疗效、下游对DUSP6 mRNA的PD抑制，以及血液、肿瘤和其他组织中药物暴露之间的相关性。\n...\nSPR2015在这些体内CRC异种移植模型中显示出显著优越的疗效，作为单药实现了64.7%的客观缓解率（ORR）和94.1%的疾病控制率（DCR）。在安全性方面，SPR2015表现出良好的体外安全性特征，并在28天啮齿动物重复给药毒理学研究中耐受性良好。SPR2015目前正处于IND申报支持阶段，预计将于2026年底推进至人体1期研究。\n...\nIn mouse PDAC/NSCLC xenograft models, SPR2015 effectively inhibited tumor growth at 10 mg/kg (oral, q.d.) and achieved tumor regression at 30 mg/kg (oral, q.d.).", "date": "2026-04-17", "last_updated": "2026-09-28", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.99, "evidence": 0.97}, "jev_score": 0.9603, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS G12D Inhibitor's $2.13B Deal Tests Cross-Border Tech Transfer", "url": "https://www.pharmtech.com/view/kras-g12d-inhibitor-s-2-13b-deal-tests-cross-border-tech-transfer", "domain": "pharmtech.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 functions as an ON-state molecular glue, showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D cell lines with wild-type selectivity and tumor regression in xenograft models.\n...\nSPR2015 is described as a molecular glue inhibitor that engages the ON form of the mutant protein.^1^ It showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity across multiple KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining selectivity over wild-type cells, and it demonstrated monotherapy antitumor efficacy in cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.78}, "jev_score": 0.7566, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Enters into Exclusive Global License Agreement ...", "url": "https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/merck-enters-exclusive-global-license-104500942.html", "domain": "ca.finance.yahoo.com", "snippet": "SPR2015 is a potent and selective novel investigational preclinical molecular glue KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor that has demonstrated nanomolar antiproliferative activities in various KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining good selectivity over KRAS wildtype cells.\n...\nIn addition, SPR2015 has demonstrated compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, as reported in preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7067}, "jev_score": 0.6926, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "MSD takes a $400m bite of SciBrunch's KRAS drug", "url": "https://pharmaphorum.com/news/msd-takes-400m-bite-scibrunchs-kras-drug", "domain": "pharmaphorum.com", "snippet": "The exclusive, global license to SPR2015, which is still in preclinical development, comes with development, commercialisation and other payments – across multiple indications – that could swell the value of the deal to $2.13 million.\n...\nThe company reported studies at this year's American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) congress which showed antitumour efficacy for SPR2015 as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models.\n...\nKRAS G12D mutations are found in 37% of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) cancers, 13% of colorectal cancer cases, and 4% of non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) cases.", "date": "2026-10-02", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7033}, "jev_score": 0.6892, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck licenses SPR2015, an oral KRAS G12D inhibitor, from ...", "url": "https://chemxplore.com/news/merck-scibrunch-spr2015-kras-g12d-license", "domain": "chemxplore.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is a preclinical oral KRAS G12D (ON) molecular‑glue inhibitor showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity and monotherapy efficacy in CDX and PDX models.\n...\nSPR2015 is an investigational preclinical oral KRAS G12D (ON) molecular‑glue inhibitor that has demonstrated nanomolar antiproliferative activity in various KRAS G12D‑mutant cell lines with good selectivity over KRAS wild‑type cells.\nIt has shown antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell‑derived and patient‑derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, with preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7}, "jev_score": 0.686, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Licenses Preclinical KRAS G12D Inhibitor from SciBrunch", "url": "https://www.pharmexec.com/view/merck-licenses-preclinical-kras-g12d-inhibitor-scibrunch", "domain": "pharmexec.com", "snippet": "### Key Takeaways\n...\n- SPR2015 is an oral, potent, selective molecular-glue KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity in multiple G12D-mutant cell lines with sparing of KRAS wildtype.\n- Preclinical monotherapy produced compelling tumor regressions across CDX and PDX models, with AACR 2026 data emphasizing activity in colorectal cancer models where prior G12D agents have struggled.\n...\nSPR2015 is a potent and selective novel investigational molecular glue KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor.^1^ It has demonstrated nanomolar antiproliferative activity in various KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining good selectivity over KRAS wildtype cells.\nKRAS G12D is the most common oncogenic RAS mutation found in human tumors, arising from a substitution of glycine with aspartate at position 12, a change that leaves KRAS active and continuously signaling for cell proliferation and survival.^1^ SPR2015 has also shown compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models, according to preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.^2^\n...\nWhile other KRAS G12D inhibitors in clinical development have reported promising results in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma and non-small cell lung cancer, none had yet demonstrated clinically meaningful monotherapy efficacy in colorectal cancer patients.^2^", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.69}, "jev_score": 0.6762, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Revolution Medicines - MedPath Trial", "url": "https://trial.medpath.com/organization/revolution-medicines", "domain": "trial.medpath.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is a molecular glue inhibitor that showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines with selectivity over KRAS wild-type cells, plus monotherapy antitumor activity in xenograft models.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.68}, "jev_score": 0.6664, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck, SciBrunch Launch Up-to-$2.13B Collaboration ...", "url": "https://www.genengnews.com/topics/cancer/merck-scibrunch-launch-up-to-2-13b-collaboration-to-develop-preclinical-kras-inhibiting-molecular-glue/", "domain": "genengnews.com", "snippet": "SPR2015 is a preclinical molecular glue, more specifically an oral KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor that SciBrunch is developing for forms of cancer that include colorectal cancer (CRC), non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), and pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC)—the most common and aggressive type of pancreatic cancer.\n...\nAccording to SciBrunch, SPR2015 has shown nanomolar antiproliferative activities in various KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining good selectivity over KRAS wildtype cells.\nAt the 2026 American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting, a team of SciBrunch researchers that included founder, chairman, and CEO Tao Hu, PhD, presented preclinical data showing SPR2015 to have demonstrated what it termed compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX and PDX) models.\n“SPR2015 is a highly potent and selective KRAS G12D (on) inhibitor with nanomolar proliferation inhibitory activities in various KRAS G12D cell lines while with good selectivity over KRAS wild type,” Hu and SciBrunch researcher colleagues reported in a poster presentation during AACR 2026.\n...\nIn a head-to-head mouse study comparing a single oral once-daily dose at 100 mg/kg of SPR2015 to another unspecified G12D (ON) inhibitor in over 15 CRC CDX or PDX models, SPR2015 showed significantly superior efficacy in the *in vivo* CRC xenograft models, achieving a 64.7% objective response rate (ORR) and 94.1% disease control rate (DCR) as monotherapy.\n...\nIn June, Verastem reported Phase I/II trial (NCT06162221) data showing 93% (13/14) of heavily pretreated (second- to fourth-line) patients with metastatic PDAC who received 900 mg once-daily monotherapy achieved greater than 50% reduction in the tumor marker CA19-9.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.6733}, "jev_score": 0.6531, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Inks $2.1B Deal With Chinese Biotech to Expand ...", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/merck-inks-2-1b-deal-141200995.html", "domain": "finance.yahoo.com", "snippet": "SPR2015 is an investigational oral molecular glue KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor designed to selectively target the KRAS G12D mutation.\n...\nIn pre-clinical studies, the candidate has shown nanomolar antiproliferative activity in several KRAS G12D-mutant cancer cell lines while maintaining good selectivity over KRAS wild-type cells.\nThe candidate has also demonstrated antitumor activity as a monotherapy in multiple cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.67}, "jev_score": 0.6499, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "SPR2015 / SciBrunch Therapeutics, Merck (MSD)", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=a79f9c66-70d3-404a-a2f7-48a63c49e2fd&Index=0", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "## SPR2015, a highly potent and selective KRAS G12D (on) inhibitor, exhibits favorable pharmacokinetic behavior and significant anti-tumor efficacy against colorectal cancer as monotherapy in preclinical models (AACR 2026) - \"On the safety part, SPR2015 demonstrated favorable in vitro safety profiles and was well-tolerated in a 28-day rodent repeat dosing tox studies. SPR2015 is currently under IND-enabling and is expected to advance to human Phase 1 study by the end of 2026.\"", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10