{"case_id": "q035-3", "row_id": "q035", "mode": "queries", "objective": "BS-HH-002 first regulatory approval or market launch year in acute myeloid leukemia", "query": "BS-HH-002 Bensheng Pharma AML clinical development", "anchors": ["BS-HH-002"], "search_latency_ms": 16051.4, "target": "BS-HH-002", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 426.7, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9918, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000417, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.9572, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Ozmosi | BS HH 002.SA Drug Profile", "url": "https://pryzm.ozmosi.com/product/29037", "domain": "pryzm.ozmosi.com", "snippet": "BS-HH-002 is a newly developed drug with excellent antitumor activity, which resulted from the modification and optimization of the side structure of the homoharringtonine (HHT).\nIt is particularly efficient in treatment for acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes.\n...\nMechanisms of Action: JAK2 Inhibitor\n...\nModality: N/A\nRoute of Administration: Subcutaneous\nFDA Designation: *\nApproval Status: Not Approved\nApproved Countries: None\nApproved Indications: None\n...\nCompany: Shanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical\n...\n###### Active Clinical Trial Count:\n...\n## Highest Development Phases\nPhase 1: Myelodysplastic Syndrome|Acute Myeloid Leukemia|Preleukemia\n|Trial|Phase|Trial Status|Disease|Primary Completion Date|Probability of Success|Latest Trial Update Date|Data Updated|\n|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|\n|BS HH 002.SA|P1|Unknown status|Myelodysplastic Syndrome|Preleukemia|Acute Myeloid Leukemia|2025-02-01|8%|2025-02-04|Primary Endpoints|", "date": "2025-02-04", "last_updated": "2025-07-30", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.9767}, "jev_score": 0.9572, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Therapeutic effects of an innovative BS-HH-002 drug on ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8633684/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "BS-HH-002 improved the characteristics of pharmacodynamic effect, tissue distribution and cardiac safety compared with the precursor compound homoharringtonine.\n...\nBS-HH-002 is a newly developed drug with excellent antitumor activity, which resulted from the modification and optimization of the side structure of the homoharringtonine (HHT).\nIt is particularly efficient in treatment for acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes.\n...\nRecent clinical studies demonstrated its efficacy for remission and post-remission treatments of acute myeloid leukemia (AML), and subsequently, for myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS)-related diseases [42].\n...\nFor this purpose, BS-HH-002 was designed and developed by Shanghai BenSheng Pharmaceutical Corp., Ltd. by modifying the secondary structure of HHT.\n...\nBS-HH-002 has been well validated for treatment of AML and MDS.\nThe drug has been approved by the FDA to enter a phase 1 clinical study in 2018.\nOur study showed that BS-HH-002 was significantly effective for the treatment of both solid tumors and polycythemia vera.", "date": "2021-11-27", "last_updated": "2025-10-21", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.84}, "jev_score": 0.8148, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on BS-HH-002 with Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/e8d3b9c25ec941369c758ac88507fd6c", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Active Indication\nAcute Myeloid Leukemia\n...\nOriginator Organization\nShanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\nActive Organization\nShanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\nInactive Organization\nHangzhou Bensheng Pharmaceutical Co.\nLtd.\n...\nDrug Highest Phase\nPhase 1\n...\nClinical Trials associated with BS-HH-002\nNCT04743115\nUnknown status\nPhase 1\nA Phase I, Open-Label, Dose Escalation and Cohort Expansion Study of BS HH 002.SA in Patients With Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) and Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS)\nIndication:Relapsed or refractory AML in patients for whom no established treatment options are available (this indication will heretofore be referred to as the protocol AML indication), or adult patients with MDS who are classified as high risk or very high risk according to the Revised International Prognosis Scoring System (IPSS-R).\nNumber of Investigators and Study Centers:Up to 5 Investigators in the US.\nObjectives:Dose Escalation Part\nPrimary Objective:\n1. To determine the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) of BS HH 002.SA administered subcutaneously once per day for 12 days of a 28-day cycle.\nSecondary Objectives:\n2. To provide an initial safety profile of single and multiple cycles of BS HH 002.SA.\n3. To assess the pharmacokinetic (PK) profile of BS HH 002.SA.\n4. To explore the anti-tumor activity of BS HH 002.SA in patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS.\n5. To explore cytogenetics of the malignant cells in relation to response to BS HH 002.SA.\nCohort Expansion Part\nPrimary Objectives:\n1. To evaluate safety and tolerability of BS HH 002.SA at MTD and/or lower dose level (DL) in selected cohorts of patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS.\n2. To evaluate preliminary anti-tumor activity of BS HH 002.SA at MTD and/or lower DL in selected cohorts of patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS.\nSecondary Objectives:\n3. To assess the PK profile of BS HH 002.SA.\n4. To explore cytogenetics of the malignant cells in relation to response to BS HH 002.SA.\nStudy Population:Adult patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS.\nStart Date\n01 Feb 2021\nSponsor / Collaborator\nShanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\n...\nAcute Myeloid Leukemia\nPhase 1\nChina\nShanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\n30 Jan 2022\n...\nPhase 1\nShanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.\n01 Feb 2021", "date"