{"case_id": "q023-1", "row_id": "q023", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Inflammatory Bowel Diseases Mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis Ulcerative Colitis competing agents with the same mechanistic class as Gut Microbiome Dysbiosis, including Live Biotherapeutic Product", "query": "VE202 Phase 2 current status licensing", "anchors": ["VE202", "MB310", "SER-287", "EXL01"], "search_latency_ms": 26321.2, "target": "drugs competing with VE202 / MB310 / SER-287 / EXL01: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 363.9, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10436, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000438, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.5307, "results": [{"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "PureTech Founded Entity Vedanta Biosciences Announces Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Ulcerative Colitis Did Not Meet Primary Endpoint", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/puretech-founded-entity-vedanta-biosciences-161600666.html", "domain": "finance.yahoo.com", "snippet": "**Vedanta Biosciences Reports Phase 2 Study of VE202 Did Not Achieve Primary Endpoint**\n**OSTON August , 5** – Pure Health plcNas: P LSE PRTC (\"Pure\") announced today that Vedanta Biosciences (\"Vedanta\"), its Founded Entity specializing in microbiome-based oral therapies for gastrointestinal conditions, revealed that its investigational drug VE202 did not fulfill the primary objective the Phase2 COLiVE trial targeting with mild-moder ulcerativeitis (UC).\nDespite this setback, VE202 was generally well tolerated, with no reports of serious adverse events linked to the treatment.\n...\nVedanta Biosciences has disclosed that Phase  COLLECTVE202's primary endpoint of endoscopic response was not met.\n...\nIn the COLLECTiVE202 study, which was randomized and placebo-controlled, endoscopic and clinical responses were evaluated using standardized measures.\nThe response rates observed in the VE202 group did not differ significantly from those in the placebo cohort.\nOverall, VE202 was found to be safe and well tolerated, with most adverse effects being mild to moderate, and no serious treatment-related adverse events reported.\n...\nThe COLLECTiVE202 study a double, placebo, randomized trial conducted across the United States, Europe, and Australia.", "date": "2025-08-13", "last_updated": "2025-08-13", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.87, "evidence": 0.61}, "jev_score": 0.5307, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Vedanta's Microbiome-Based Candidate Fails to Meet ...", "url": "https://www.appliedclinicaltrialsonline.com/view/vedanta-microbiome-candidate-fails-primary-endpoint-phase-ii-trial-mild-moderate-ulcerative-colitis", "domain": "appliedclinicaltrialsonline.com", "snippet": "**VE202 Phase II Results:**Vedanta Biosciences’ VE202 did not meet the trial’s primary endpoints treating mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (UC), highlighting ongoing challenges for microbiome-based therapies.", "date": "2025-08-14", "last_updated": "2026-02-07", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.86, "evidence": 0.6067}, "jev_score": 0.5218, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "VE-202 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/1fb685bb89f84c16af0a3d32e6f4c385", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|Originator Organization Janssen Research & Development LLC|\n...\n|Active Organization-|\n|Inactive Organization Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.Janssen Research & Development LLC|\n|License Organization Janssen Biotech, Inc.Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.|\n|Drug Highest PhaseDiscontinuedPhase 2|\n...\n|RegulationFast Track (United States)|\n...\nClinical Trials associated with VE-202\nNCT05370885\n/ TerminatedPhase 2\nRandomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Patients With Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis\n...\nPureTech Founded Entity Vedanta Biosciences Announces Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Ulcerative Colitis Did Not Meet Primary Endpoint\n...\n|--|--|--|--|--|\n|Colitis, Ulcerative|Phase 2|United States|Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.|12 May 2022|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-15", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.82, "evidence": 0.6033}, "jev_score": 0.4947, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Vedanta Biosciences Announces Phase 2 Study of VE202 ...", "url": "https://www.vedantabio.com/press-release/vedanta-biosciences-announces-phase-2-study-of-ve202-in-ulcerative-colitis-did-not-meet-primary-endpoint/", "domain": "vedantabio.com", "snippet": "Vedanta Biosciences Announces Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Ulcerative Colitis Did Not Meet Primary Endpoint - Vedanta Biosciences, Inc\n...\n*VE202 was well tolerated, with no reports of treatment-related serious adverse events*\n...\n**CAMBRIDGE, Mass., August 13, 2025** – Vedanta Biosciences, a late clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company developing microbiome-based oral therapies for gastrointestinal diseases, today announced that its candidate VE202 did not meet the primary endpoint of endoscopic response in the Phase 2 COLLECTiVE202 study for the treatment of patients with mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (UC).\n“We are very disappointed that our study did not meet its efficacy endpoints, and our greatest regret is that people living with inflammatory bowel disease will not, for now, have the opportunity to benefit from a new treatment option,” said Bernat Olle, Ph.D., Chief Executive Officer of Vedanta Biosciences.\n...\nIn the randomized, placebo-controlled COLLECTiVE202 study, endoscopic and clinical responses were assessed using standardized criteria, and the observed response rates in the VE202 group were not statistically different from those in the placebo group.\nVE202 was generally safe and well tolerated — most adverse events were mild or moderate in intensity, with no reports of treatment-related serious adverse events.\nAnalyses of bacterial colonization, histological findings, and immune responses are ongoing and will be shared in future scientific forums.\n...\nCOLLECTiVE202 is a double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized clinical trial conducted at sites in the United States, Europe, and Australia.\nThe study enrolled 114 patients, between the ages of 18 and 75 years, with mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis who had not been exposed to any biologic or advanced oral therapies.\n...\nFor more information on COLLECTiVE202 (NCT05370885), visit clinicaltrials.gov.", "date": "2025-08-13", "last_updated": "2026-09-24", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.83, "evidence": 0.58}, "jev_score": 0.4814, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Vedanta's live bacteria cocktail fails phase 2 colitis trial", "url": "https://www.fiercebiotech.com/biotech/vedantas-live-bacteria-cocktail-fails-reduce-ulcerative-colitis-severity-phase-2-trial", "domain": "fiercebiotech.com", "snippet": "Vedanta's live bacteria cocktail fails phase 2 colitis trial\n...\n# Vedanta's live bacteria cocktail fails to reduce ulcerative colitis severity in phase 2 trial\n...\nVedanta Biosciences’ dreams of using live bacteria to treat inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) have been dashed.\nThe Massachusetts-based microbiome outfit’s mixture of 16 bacterial strains failed to reduce disease severity in the colons of patients with ulcerative colitis.\nThe phase 2 Collective202 trial enrolled 114 patients with mild to moderate ulcerative colitis and compared Vedanta’s bacterial cocktail VE202 with placebo.\nWhile VE202 led to no treatment-related adverse events, the company said in an Aug. 13 release, it did not beat placebo at improving disease symptoms, as assessed using an endoscope.\n“We are very disappointed that our study did not meet its efficacy endpoints, and our greatest regret is that people living with inflammatory bowel disease will not, for now, have the opportunity to benefit from a new treatment option,” Vedanta CEO Bernat Olle, Ph.D., said in the release.\n...\nVedanta plans to share further data from the phase 2 trial at upcoming conferences, according to the release.\n...\nWith VE202 on the back burner, VE303 is now Vedanta’s sole clinical focus.", "date": "2025-08-13", "last_updated": "2026-09-23", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.82, "evidence": 0.5833}, "jev_score": 0.4783, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "VE202 ( DrugBank: - )", "url": "https://ddrare.nibn.go.jp/ddrare_Mar2023/cgi-bin/drug_who_e.cgi?query=VE202&disease_id=97", "domain": "ddrare.nibn.go.jp", "snippet": "|1|NCT05370885 (ClinicalTrials.gov)|May 2023|30/3/2022|VE202 in Patients With Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis|Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Patients With Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis|Ulcerative Colitis;Colitis, Ulcerative|Biological: VE202;Drug: Vancomycin Oral Capsule;Other: VE202 Placebo;Other: Vancomycin Placebo|Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.|NULL|Not yet recruiting|18 Years|75 Years|All|100|Phase 2|NULL|\n|2|EUCTR2021-001280-24-LT (EUCTR)|07/12/2021|19/08/2021|Study of VE202 in Patients with Ulcerative Colitis|Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Patients with Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis|Mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (UC) MedDRA version: 20.1;Level: LLT;Classification code 10045365;Term: Ulcerative colitis;System Organ Class: 100000004856;Therapeutic area: Diseases [C] - Digestive System Diseases [C06]|Product Name: VE202 Product Code: VE202 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841829 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841842 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841855 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841894 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841907 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841920 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841933 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-64841946|Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.|NULL|Authorised-recruitment may be ongoing or finished|Female: yes Male: yes|100|Phase 2|Serbia;United States;Czechia;Hungary;Poland;Ukraine;Lithuania;Bulgaria;Netherlands;United Kingdom|\n|3|EUCTR2021-001280-24-HU (EUCTR)|13/10/2021|18/08/2021|Study of VE202 in Patients with Ulcerative Colitis|Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Patients with Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis|Mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (UC) MedDRA version: 20.1;Level: LLT;Classification code 10045365;Term: Ulcerative colitis;System Organ Class: 100000004856;Therapeutic area: Diseases [C] - Digestive System Diseases [C06]|Product Name: VE202 Product Code: VE202 INN or Proposed INN: Not applicable Other descriptive name: JNJ-72537634|Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.|NULL|Authorised-recruitment may be ongoing or finished|Female: yes Male: yes|100|Phase 2|United States;Czechia;Hungary;Poland;Ukraine;Lithuania;Russian Federation;Netherlands|", "date": "2022-03-30", "last_updated": "2025-04-06", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.5567}, "jev_score": 0.4732, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Vedanta Ends UC Program After Phase II Failure, Refocuses Pipeline", "url": "https://igmpi.ac.in/news/clinical-research/vedanta-ends-uc-program-after-phase-ii-failure-refocuses-pipeline", "domain": "igmpi.ac.in", "snippet": "Vedanta Biosciences has announced the discontinuation of its ulcerative colitis (UC) program following the failure of its oral microbiome therapy, VE202, in a Phase II trial.\nThe therapy did not meet its primary endpoint of improving endoscopic response in patients with mild-to-moderate UC, leading the company to also reduce its workforce by 20%.", "date": "2025-08-14", "last_updated": "2025-09-03", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.86, "evidence": 0.5467}, "jev_score": 0.4702, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Vedanta's UC Drug Miss Shifts Focus to Fast-Tracked C. Difficile Treatment in Phase 3", "url": "https://www.stocktitan.net/news/PRTC/pure-tech-founded-entity-vedanta-biosciences-announces-phase-2-study-hgkgis1qkjql.html", "domain": "stocktitan.net", "snippet": "# PureTech Founded Entity Vedanta Biosciences Announces Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Ulcerative Colitis Did Not Meet Primary Endpoint\n...\nBOSTON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- PureTech Health plc (Nasdaq: PRTC, LSE: PRTC) (\"PureTech\"), noted that its Founded Entity, Vedanta Biosciences, (“Vedanta”) a late clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company developing microbiome-based oral therapies for gastrointestinal diseases, today announced that its candidate VE202 did not meet the primary endpoint in the Phase 2 COLLECTiVE202 study for the treatment of patients with mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (UC).\n...\n**CAMBRIDGE, Mass., August 13, 2025** – Vedanta Biosciences, a late clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company developing microbiome-based oral therapies for gastrointestinal diseases, today announced that its candidate VE202 did not meet the primary endpoint of endoscopic response in the Phase 2 COLLECTiVE202 study for the treatment of patients with mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (UC).\n...\nIn the randomized, placebo-controlled COLLECTiVE202 study, endoscopic and clinical responses were assessed using standardized criteria, and the observed response rates in the VE202 group were not statistically different from those in the placebo group.\nVE202 was generally safe and well tolerated — most adverse events were mild or moderate in intensity, with no reports of treatment-related serious adverse events.\nAnalyses of bacterial colonization, histological findings, and immune responses are ongoing and will be shared in future scientific forums.\n...\n** COLLECTiVE202 is a double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized clinical trial conducted at sites in the United States, Europe, and Australia.\nThe study enrolled 114 patients, between the ages of 18 and 75 years, with mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis who had not been exposed to any biologic or advanced oral therapies.\n...\nThe primary endpoints were safety and Week 8 endoscopic response (defined as a reduction of at least 1 point on the Mayo endoscopic subscore).", "date": "2025-08-13", "last_updated": "2026-03-04", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.5567}, "jev_score": 0.4509, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Vedanta Biosciences Cuts 20% of Workforce After ...", "url": "https://trial.medpath.com/news/vedanta-biosciences-cuts-20-of-workforce-after-microbiome-therapy-ve202-fails-phase-2-ulcerative-colitis-trial", "domain": "trial.medpath.com", "snippet": "## Key Insights\n- Vedanta Biosciences (search) will lay off nearly 20% of its staff after experimental microbiome (search) therapy VE202 failed to meet its primary endpoint in a Phase 2 ulcerative colitis (search) study.\n- The VE202 treatment, licensed by Johnson & Johnson in 2015, was not significantly better than placebo at improving disease signs on endoscopic examination after eight weeks of treatment.\n...\nVedanta Biosciences (search), a microbiome (search)-focused biotechnology company backed by PureTech Health, announced Wednesday it will lay off approximately 20% of its workforce following the failure of its experimental therapy VE202 in a Phase 2 ulcerative colitis (search) trial.\n...\nVE202 failed to meet its primary endpoint in the Phase 2 study evaluating patients with mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis (search).\nThe experimental therapy was not significantly better than placebo at improving signs of patients' disease on an endoscopic examination after eight weeks of treatment, according to the company's announcement.\nThe drug, which Johnson & Johnson licensed in 2015, represents one of Vedanta's packaged bacteria strain therapies delivered in pill form.", "date": "2025-08-14", "last_updated": "2026-09-09", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.8, "evidence": 0.5633}, "jev_score": 0.4506, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "controlled, phase 2 study of ve202 in patients", "url": "https://onderzoekmetmensen.nl/en/node/52361/pdf", "domain": "onderzoekmetmensen.nl", "snippet": "RANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, PLACEBO-\nCONTROLLED, PHASE 2 STUDY OF VE202\nIN PATIENTS WITH MILD-TO-MODERATE\nULCERATIVE COLITIS\n...\nThis study has been transitioned to CTIS with ID 2024-512558-40-00 check the CTIS register for the current data.\n...\nEthical review\nApproved WMO\nStatus\nPending\nHealth condition type\n...\nRANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, PLACEBO-CONTROLLED, PHASE 2 STUDY OF VE202 IN\nPATIENTS WITH MILD-TO-MODERATE ULCERATIVE COLITIS\n...\nPrimary\n• Evaluate the efficacy of 8 weeks of treatment with VE202 in terms of\nendoscopic response at Day 56\n• Evaluate the safety of VE202 in Part 1 and Part 2 of the study\n...\nSecondary objective\n1. Evaluate the safety of VE202 in Parts 1, 2, and 3 of the study\n2. Evaluate the efficacy of 2 weeks of treatment with VE202 in terms of\nendoscopic response at Day 56\n3. Evaluate the efficacy of 2- and 8 week courses of VE202 in terms of response\n...\nEligible randomized patients (100 in total) will receive 5 days of pretreatment with oral (po)\nvancomycin at a dose of 125 mg 4 times daily (QID).\nAfter completing vancomycin pretreatment,\npatients in Group A will receive VE202 and patients in Group B will receive\nVE202 placebo at a dose\nof 10 capsules po once daily (QD) for 14 days, followed by 1 capsule po QD from\nDay 15 to 56.\n...\nAt the completion of Part 1, all patients will undergo flexible sigmoidoscopy.\nPart 2: After the flexible sigmoidoscopy at Day 56, patients in Group A will receive vancomycin\nplacebo po QID for 5 days, followed by placebo for VE202 at a dose of 10 capsules po QD for 14 days.\n...\nStudy patients will be randomized in a 1:1 ratio to Group A or Group B after all screening criteria are\n...\nVE202 has been given to 21 healthy volunteers and has not yet been studied in patients with ulcerative colitis.\nThe side effects reported in\n>1 subject who received VE202 were headache, abdominal discomfort, diarrhea,\nweight loss, upper respiratory infection, fatigue, and joint pain.\n...\nDesign\nStudy phase:\n2\nStudy type:\nInterventional\nIntervention model:\nParallel\nAllocation:\nRandomized controlled trial\n...\nControl:\n...\nTreatment\nRecruitment\nNL\nRecruitment status:\nPending\nStart date (anticipated):\n...\nMedical products/devices used\nRegistration:\nNo\nProduct type:\nMedicine\nRegistration:\nYes - NL intended use\nProduct type:\nMedicine", "date": "2024-04-02", "last_updated": "2026-09-19", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.4567}, "jev_score": 0.3699, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}], "total_ms": 26685.1, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:30+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q038-1", "row_id": "q038", "mode": "queries", "objective": "KRAS G12D drugs approved against the target and their regulatory approval status", "query": "ZE980277 KRAS G12D approval status FDA EMA", "anchors": ["ZE980277"], "search_latency_ms": 3583.9, "target": "drugs competing with ZE980277: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 358.0, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8398, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000353, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.837, "results": [{"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "cancer.aestheticsadvisor.com · 2026 · 04KRAS Inhibitors (2026): The Complete Guide to Targeted Therapy...", "url": "https://cancer.aestheticsadvisor.com/2026/04/kras-inhibitors-2026-complete-guide-to.html", "domain": "cancer.aestheticsadvisor.com", "snippet": "Zoldonrasib is a covalent, G12D-selective RAS(ON) inhibitor and holds FDA Breakthrough Therapy Designation for KRAS G12D-mutated disease.\n...\nNo targeted therapy is currently FDA-approved specifically for RAS G12D-mutant cancers; zoldonrasib and related G12D-directed programs (including earlier-stage compounds such as MRTX1133) remain under active clinical investigation.\n...\nNot yet as a G12D-selective agent.\nDaraxonrasib's pancreatic cancer approval covers RAS G12-mutant disease broadly (including G12D and G12V) rather than being G12D-specific.\nZoldonrasib, a G12D-selective RAS(ON) inhibitor, remains investigational, with Phase 3 trials ongoing.\n...\n- No KRAS G12D-selective drug is yet approved anywhere; zoldonrasib is the most clinically advanced candidate, in Phase 3 development.", "date": "2026-09-07", "last_updated": "2026-09-29", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.86, "evidence": 0.9733}, "jev_score": 0.837, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Investigational KRAS G12D Agents Demonstrate Promising ... - ILCN", "url": "https://www.ilcn.org/investigational-kras-g12d-agents-demonstrate-promising-antitumor-activity-in-non-small-cell-lung-cancer/", "domain": "ilcn.org", "snippet": "Early findings from two clinical studies support the continued development of setidegrasib and zoldonrasib to target KRAS G12D mutations.\n...\nKRAS G12D mutations occur in around 5% of patients with NSCLC; however, there are currently no therapies available that specifically target these mutations.\n...\nZoldonrasib was previously granted breakthrough therapy designation by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in January 2026, marking the first time this designation was granted to an investigational drug specifically targeting the RAS G12D mutation.4 The FDA’s recent designation was based on data from the monotherapy cohort of the phase 1 RMC-9805-001 clinical trial, in which zoldonrasib demonstrated encouraging antitumor activity, along with acceptable safety and tolerability.4", "date": "2026-05-26", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.8, "evidence": 0.85}, "jev_score": 0.68, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Therapeutic inhibition of RAS in non-small cell lung cancer - Frontiers", "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/oncology/articles/10.3389/fonc.2026.1817943/full", "domain": "frontiersin.org", "snippet": "As of this writing, both drugs retain their accelerated approvals, but neither have received full or standard FDA approvals based on these results, and neither study has easily interpretable OS results, limited by both sample size and crossover.\n...\n|Glecirasib (JAB-21822)|KRAS G12C|Inhibitor (covalent; GDP/Switch-II pocket)|NCT05009329 NCT05002270|JAB-21822-101 (phase 1) JAB-21822-1001 (phase 1/2)|\n...\n|Zoldonrasib (RMC-9805)|KRAS G12D (ON)|Molecular glue / tri-complex inhibitor (RAS(ON))|NCT06040541|RMC-9805-001 (phase 1/1b)|\n|ASP3082|KRAS G12D|PROTAC / targeted degrader|NCT05382559|ASP3082 first-in-human (phase 1)|", "date": "2026-06-30", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.7833}, "jev_score": 0.6658, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Zoldonrasib in Patients With KRAS G12D–Mutant NSCLC ...", "url": "https://ascopost.com/news/april-2026/zoldonrasib-in-patients-with-kras-g12d-nsclc-previously-treated-with-chemoimmunotherapy/", "domain": "ascopost.com", "snippet": "The investigational KRAS G12D inhibitor zoldonrasib had a favorable safety profile and induced antitumor activity in some patients with *KRAS * G12D–mutated non–small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) who were previously treated with chemotherapy and immunotherapy, according to preliminary findings from an ongoing phase I study presented at the American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting 2026 (Abstract CT021).\n...\nTwo KRAS inhibitors have already been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for the treatment of patients with *KRAS * G12C–mutated NSCLC.\nHowever, there are currently no RAS-targeted therapies available for patients with NSCLC harboring a *KRAS * G12D mutation.\nZoldonrasib is an oral G12D-selective tricomplex RAS(ON) inhibitor that is currently being studied in a phase I clinical trial of patients with solid tumors harboring *KRAS * G12D mutations who have received at least one prior line of therapy.\n...\nPrior results from this study showed encouraging safety and efficacy data in a NSCLC subgroup, which led to the agent receiving an FDA Breakthrough Therapy designation in January 2026.", "date": "2026-04-05", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.76, "evidence": 0.8167}, "jev_score": 0.6207, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS Inhibitor Clinical Trial Landscape, September 2026: 115 ...", "url": "https://datalookout.com/kras-inhibitor-clinical-trials", "domain": "datalookout.com", "snippet": "Revolution Medicines is leading the development of pan-RAS inhibitors that target multiple KRAS mutations simultaneously, including G12D, the dominant mutation in pancreatic cancer:\n...\n- **RMC-9805 (Revolution Medicines)**: KRAS G12D-selective.\nPhase 1 in KRAS G12D-mutant solid tumors, particularly PDAC.", "date": "2026-10-01", "last_updated": "2026-10-01", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.78, "evidence": 0.79}, "jev_score": 0.6162, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Our Pipeline - KRAS G12D inhibitor - Genentech", "url": "https://www.gene.com/medical-professionals/pipeline/kras-g12d-inhibitor", "domain": "gene.com", "snippet": "These compounds and their uses are investigational and have not been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.", "date": "2019-12-19", "last_updated": "2026-09-28", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.57, "evidence": 0.88}, "jev_score": 0.5016, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Search Orphan Drug Designations and Approvals - FDA", "url": "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=1124625", "domain": "accessdata.fda.gov", "snippet": "|Generic Name:|KRAS G12D inhibitor|\n|--|--|\n|Date Designated:|05/01/2026|\n|Orphan Designation:|treatment of pancreatic cancer|\n|Orphan Designation Status:|Designated|\n|FDA Orphan Approval Status:|Not FDA Approved for Orphan Indication|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-11", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.58, "evidence": 0.8133}, "jev_score": 0.4717, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Ongoing | Cancer Accelerated Approvals", "url": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/ongoing-cancer-accelerated-