{"case_id": "q041-2", "row_id": "q041", "mode": "queries", "objective": "competing agents in the same mechanistic class for this indication DB-3Q, Direct Biologics LLC, Medically Refractory Crohn's Disease", "query": "DB-3Q extracellular vesicle Crohn's disease clinical trials", "anchors": ["DB-3Q"], "search_latency_ms": 10433.7, "target": "drugs competing with DB-3Q: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 332.5, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9955, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000418, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 2, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.3328, "results": [{"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "DB-3Q bmMSC-EVs in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing ...", "url": "https://www.allclinicaltrials.com/study/NCT06918808", "domain": "allclinicaltrials.com", "snippet": "DB-3Q bmMSC-EVs in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease\n1. DB-3Q bmMSC-EVs in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease\nRecruiting\nPhase 2\n# DB-3Q DB-3Q bmMSC-EVs in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease\nSponsor:\nDirect Biologics, LLC\nCode:\nNCT06918808\nConditions\nPerianal Fistula Due to Crohn's Disease\n...\nThis is a double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled, sequential cohort, ascending dose clinical trial to evaluate the safety and determine the efficacy of ascending doses of DB-3Q for the treatment of Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease.\n...\nStudy ID\nNCT06918808\nStart date\nMay 19, 2025\nStatus verified date\nFeb, 2026\nCompletion date\nDec 31, 2027\nAnticipated\nPrimary completion date\nJul 30, 2027\nAnticipated\n...\n1. Written informed consent from participant\n2. Men and women 18-75 years of age with a diagnosis of Crohn's Disease for at least six months duration prior to Day 1\n3. One or two perianal fistula(s) with 1 or two external openings, that are actively draining\n4. Failed at least one medical therapy within the last year including, but not limited to, antibiotics, immunomodulators (6-MP, methotrexate, azathioprine), monoclonal antibodies (adalimumab, certolizumab, golimumab, guselkumab, infliximab, risankizumab, ustekinumab, vedolizumab), or small molecule inhibitors (tofacitinib, upadacitinib)\n5. Previous failed surgical intervention, including seton placement at least two weeks prior to screening, or are not candidates for surgical intervention or are not willing to undergo surgical intervention for the management of their fistula\n6. Medical therapy for CD stable for at least 2 months prior to Day 1 (Changes in dosing or dosing intervals related to serum drug levels are not permitted)\n...\nEnrollment\n36 participants\nAnticipated\nAllocation\nRandomized\nIntervention Model\nSequential\n...\nexperimental: Single dose DB-3Q 15 mL direct injection\nplacebo comparator: Single dose Placebo 15 mL direct injection\nexperimental: Single dose DB-3Q 30 mL direct injection\nplacebo comparator: Single dose Placebo 30 mL direct injection\nexperimental: Single dose DB-3Q 15 ml IV and DB-3Q 30 mL direct injection\nplacebo comparator: Single dose Placebo 15 ml IV and Placebo 30 mL direct injection\n...\nDB-3Q (IMP) is the frozen liquid formulation of acellular secretome proteins and extracellular vesicles isolated from human bmMSC and processed under current Good Manufacturing Process standards.\n...\nPrimary outcome measure\n- Combined Remission [ Time Frame: 24 Weeks ]", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-27", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.62, "evidence": 0.5367}, "jev_score": 0.3328, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "DB-3Q bmMSC-EVs in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease", "url": "https://ichgcp.net/clinical-trials-registry/NCT06918808", "domain": "ichgcp.net", "snippet": "# DB-3Q bmMSC-EVs in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease\n...\n## A Phase 2a Study of Allogeneic Bone Marrow Mesenchymal Stem Cell Derived Extracellular Vesicle Isolate Product (DB-3Q) in Patients With Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease\nThis is a double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled, sequential cohort, ascending dose clinical trial to evaluate the safety and determine the efficacy of ascending doses of DB-3Q for the treatment of Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease.\n...\n#### Status\nRecruiting\n...\nInterventional\n#### Enrollment (Estimated)\n36\n#### Phase\n- Phase 2\n...\nNew York\nNew York, New York, United States, 10032\n- Recruiting\n- Columbia University Irving Medical Center/NYPH\nContact:\n- Claudia Musat\n...\nInclusion Criteria:\n- Written informed consent from participant\n- Men and women 18-75 years of age with a diagnosis of Crohn's Disease for at least six months duration prior to Day 1\n- Single and/or multi-tract perianal fistula(s) with 2 or fewer openings, that are actively draining\n- Failed at least one medical therapy within the last year including, but not limited to, antibiotics, immunomodulators (6-MP, methotrexate, azathioprine), monoclonal antibodies (adalimumab, certolizumab, golimumab, guselkumab, infliximab, risankizumab, ustekinumab, vedolizumab), or small molecule inhibitors (tofacitinib, upadacitinib)\n- Previous failed surgical intervention, including seton placement at least two weeks prior to screening, or are not candidates for surgical intervention or are not willing to undergo surgical intervention for the management of their fistula\n- Medical therapy for CD stable for at least 2 months prior to Day 1 (Changes in dosing or dosing intervals related to serum drug levels are not permitted)\n...\n**Primary Purpose**: Treatment **Allocation**: Randomized **Interventional Model**: Sequential Assignment **Masking**: Quadruple\n...\n|Experimental: Single dose DB-3Q 15 mL direct injection|DB-3Q (IMP) is the frozen liquid formulation of acellular secretome proteins and extracellular vesicles isolated from human bmMSC and processed under current Good Manufacturing Process standards.|\n|Placebo Comparator: Single dose Placebo 15 mL direct injection|0.9% NaCl|\n|Experimental: Single dose DB-3Q 30 mL direct injection|DB-3Q (IMP) is the frozen liquid formulation of acellular secretome proteins and extracellular vesicles isolated from human bmMSC and processed under current Good Manufacturing Process standards.|\n|Placebo Comparator: Single dose Placebo 30 mL direct injection|0.9% NaCl|\n|Experimental: Single dose DB-3Q 15 ml IV and DB-3Q 30 mL direct injection|DB-3Q (IMP) is the frozen liquid formulation of acellular secretome proteins and extracellular vesicles isolated from human bmMSC and processed under current Good Manufacturing Process standards.|\n|Placebo Comparator: Single dose Placebo 15 ml IV and Placebo 30 mL direct injection|0.9% NaCl|\n...\n|--|--|--|\n|Combined Remission Time Frame: 24 Weeks|Clinically confirmed 100% closure of all treated external openings, without development of new fistulas or abscesses and drainage > 1 cm by the external openings, occurring spontaneously or after gentle finger compression; and on blinded central review of the MRI results, combined imaging endpoint of >50% reduction in MAGNIFI-CD score and >20% increase in perianal fistula fibrosis-to-fluid ratio.|24 Weeks|\n...\n|Combined Remission Time Frame: 12 Weeks|Clinically confirmed 100% closure of all treated external openings, without development of new fistulas or abscesses and drainage > 1 cm by the external openings, occurring spontaneously or after gentle finger compression; and on blinded central review of the MRI results, combined imaging endpoint of >50% reduction in MAGNIFI-CD score and >20% increase in perianal fistula fibrosis-to-fluid ratio.|12 Weeks|\n...\n#### Study Start (Actual)\nMay 19, 2025\n#### Primary Completion (Estimated)\nApril 30, 2026\n#### Study Completion (Estimated)\nOctober 31, 2026", "date": "2025-06-13", "last_updated": "2025-07-24", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.62, "evidence": 0.5133}, "jev_score": 0.3182, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Claudia Musat, MD - Columbia Surgery", "url": "https://columbiasurgery.org/sites/default/files/2025-03/colorectal-ibd-trials-2025.pdf", "domain": "columbiasurgery.org", "snippet": "DB-3Q: Bone marrow mesenchymal stem cell (bmMSC) derived extracellular \nvesicles product in Patients with Perianal Fistulizing Crohn's Disease (CD) \nPI: Marco Zoccali, MD \nIRB: AAAV6645 \nDisease: Perianal Fistulas due to Crohn's Disease (CD)\nTreatment: DB-3Q (a bone-marrow mesenchymal stem cell product) or Placebo \nThe purpose of this study is to evaluate the efficacy and safety of ascending doses of DB-3Q, a bone-marrow mesenchymal stem cell (bmMSC) derived secretome with extracellular vesicles\n(EVs) isolate product, via direct injection and intravenous (IV) administration, as treatment for \nparticipants with perianal fistulizing Crohn’s disease (PFCD).\nThe investigational product is experimental and has not been approved by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA).\nThe experimental study drug is a biologic product which is purified from the bone marrow of a healthy well-screened individual.\n36 participants with perianal fistulizing Crohn’s disease, randomized 3:1 to IMP or placebo in \nblocks of 4 participants (3 randomized to IMP, and 1 randomized to placebo) such that each cohort will have 12 participants (9 randomized to IMP and 3 randomized to placebo).\nYour participation in this study will be approximately 24 weeks long.\nEligibility: \n1. 18-75 years of age with a diagnosis of Crohn’s Disease for at least six months duration \nprior to Day 1 \n2. Single and/or multi-tract perianal fistula(s) with 2 or fewer openings, that are actively \ndraining \n3. Failed at least one medical therapy within the last year ", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-25", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.73, "evidence": 0.4267}, "jev_score": 0.3115, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "DB-3QDB-3Q for the Treatment of Medically Refractory Crohn's Disease", "url": "https://www.allclinicaltrials.com/study/NCT07625293", "domain": "allclinicaltrials.com", "snippet": "Recruiting\nPhase 2\n# DB-3Q DB-3Q for the Treatment of Medically Refractory Crohn's Disease\nSponsor:\nDirect Biologics, LLC\nCode:\nNCT07625293\nConditions\n...\nEligibility Criteria\nSex: All\nAge: 18 - 70+\nHealthy Volunteers: Not accepted\nInterventions\nDB-3Q\nPlacebo\n...\nThis research study is studying DB-3Q as a possible treatment for medically refractory Crohn's disease.\nThe purpose of this study is to research and evaluate safety and effectiveness of the administration of bone marrow mesenchymal stem cell (bmMSC) derived extracellular vesicles product, DB-3Q, the study drug for Crohn's disease.\n...\nStudy ID\nNCT07625293\nStart date\nJun 1, 2026\nStatus verified date\nAug, 2026\nCompletion date\nDec, 2027\nAnticipated\nPrimary completion date\nJun, 2027\nAnticipated\n...\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. Written informed consent from participant\n2. Males and females 18-75 years of age\n3. Diagnosed with Crohn's disease of at least 6 months duration with medically refractory symptoms that failed to respond or responded but recurred after one advanced immunologic therapy (must have been receiving at least one advanced immunological therapy for 14 weeks duration prior to screening, including, but not limited to, adalimumab, certolizumab, , infliximab, risankizumab, upadacitinib, ustekinumab and vedolizumab), or is intolerant, or has a contraindication to advanced immunological therapy with a next step of subtotal colectomy or escalation in medical management\n4. Active CD as defined by a CDAI score ≥ 220 and/or SES-CD score ≥ 4\n5. Exposure to corticosteroids, 5-aminosalicylic acid (5-ASA) drugs, thiopurines, methotrexate, anti-TNF therapy, anti-integrin and anti-interleukin in the past are permitted but a washout period of 8 weeks for any monoclonal antibody is necessary\n...\nEnrollment\n36 participants\nAnticipated\nAllocation\nRandomized\nIntervention Model\nSequential\nPrimary purpose\nTreatment\n...\nArms\nexperimental: DB-3Q 15 mL IV\nexperimental: DB-3Q 30 mL IV\nexperimental: DB-3Q 45 mL IV\nplacebo comparator: Placebo IV\nInterventions\nDB-3Q\nbmMSC derived, extracellular vesicle enriched secretome product\nPlacebo\n0.9% Saline\nPrimary outcome measure\n- Change from baseline in SES-CD Score [ Time Frame: 12 Weeks ]", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-20", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.6, "evidence": 0.41}, "jev_score": 0.246, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Columbia Enrolls Nation's First Patient in Direct Biologics' Phase 2 ...", "url": "https://columbiasurgery.org/news/columbia-enrolls-nations-first-patient-direct-biologics-phase-2-clinical-trial-fistulizing", "domain": "columbiasurgery.org", "snippet": "Columbia University Irving Medical Center has enrolled the first patient in a multicenter Phase 2 clinical trial investigating the effectiveness of Direct Biologics' proprietary extracellular vesicle technology (DB-3Q, extracellular vesicles (EVs) secreted from bone marrow-derived mesenchymal stem cells) for the treatment of perianal fistulizing Crohn's Disease.\n...\n\"This study aims to determine if this approach is a viable option to treat anal fistula in patients with Crohn's disease specifically.\"\n...\nThis phase 2 multicenter randomized study will have multiple cohorts with three different doses and administration routes.\nThe first uses an initial dose administered in the operating room via direct injection near the fistula.\nThe second phase will double that dose.\nThe third phase will include local injections and add an IV infusion of the medication.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-25", "