in": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "Behind that, and powered by our unique NxWave™ discovery platform, we are advancing an extensive pipeline of over 30 active programs from discovery through to late clinical stage internally and in partnership with leading pharma and biotech companies.\n...\nEP4 ag.\nNXE'744\nInflammatory Bowel Disease\n...\nOur three wholly owned clinical programs are also advancing as planned in Phase 1 development, with several important milestones expected over the next 12-18 months.\nThese programs are: NXE-149, which is targeting unmet needs in schizophrenia and is the subject of an option- to-license agreement with Boehringer Ingelheim; NXE-732, which is being investigated in solid tumors in collaboration with Cancer Research\nUK; and NXE-744, which offers a possible novel mechanism to treat inflammatory bowel diseases.\n...\nThe first subject was dosed in a Phase 1 trial of NXE’744, an oral, gut-restricted EP4 agonist with potential to treat Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD).\nNXE’744 has been designed to bring clinical benefit by accelerating the healing of damaged epithelial mucosa and suppressing exaggerated gut inflammation, with minimal systemic exposure thereby providing significantly enhanced safety and efficacy.\nEP4 agonist\nNXE0033744\n12", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-14", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.56}, "jev_score": 0.4536, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Nxera Pharma Operational Highlights and Consolidated ...", "url": "https://www.biospace.com/press-releases/nxera-pharma-operational-highlights-and-consolidated-results-for-the-fourth-quarter-and-full-year-2024", "domain": "biospace.com", "snippet": "- **First subject dosed in a Phase 1 trial with NXE0033744**, a novel, potent, selective and gut-restricted EP4 receptor agonist in development for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD)", "date": "2025-02-14", "last_updated": "2026-07-23", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.82, "evidence": 0.49}, "jev_score": 0.4018, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "アニュアルレポート", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/jp/common/pdf/20250829_Annual_Report_2024_JP.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "提供する可能性があります。\n...\n消化管で局所作用する炎症性腸疾患（以下「IBD」）の治療薬候補であるEP4受容体作動薬\nNXE0033744のフェーズ1試験で、最初の被験者への投与を実施。NXE0033744は、全身へ\nの影響を最小限に抑えながら、損傷した粘膜上皮の治癒を促進し、腸菅の炎症亢進を抑制\nすることで安全性および有効性を大幅に高め、治療効果を発揮するように設計されている", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-08", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.79, "evidence": 0.5}, "jev_score": 0.395, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Corporate Presentation - October 2025 - Investors", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/common/pdf/Corporate_Presentation_2025Oct_EN_vF2.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "NXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nSME\nInflammatory bowel disease\n...\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nInflammatory bowel diseases\nPh1\nUp to  220\n-\n2023-11-24\n2026-06-30\n2024-05-02\nISRCTN70080074", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-27", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.79, "evidence": 0.5}, "jev_score": 0.395, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Nxera Pharma : Consolidated Financial Results for the FY2024 (IFRS)", "url": "https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/NXERA-PHARMA-CO-LTD-6814799/news/Nxera-Pharma-Consolidated-Financial-Results-for-the-FY2024-IFRS-49058204/", "domain": "marketscreener.com", "snippet": "Within the Group, Nxera Pharma UK Limited (formerly Heptares Therapeutics Ltd), a wholly owned subsidiary based in UK, mainly engages in drug discovery, translational medicine, preclinical and early clinical development; Nxera Pharma Japan Co., Ltd.\n(formerly Idorsia Pharmaceuticals Japan Ltd.; hereinafter referred to as \"NPJ\"), a wholly owned subsidiary based in Japan, and Nxera Pharma Korea Co., Ltd.\n...\nThe approval of QUVIVIQ™, a novel dual orexin receptor antagonist, is based on robust clinical efficacy and safety data including from a dedicated Japanese Phase 3 trial.\n...\nOn December 5, 2024, the Group announced randomization of the first patient in a Phase 3 clinical trial evaluating daridorexant, its novel dual orexin receptor antagonist, for the treatment of adult patients in South Korea with insomnia.\nThe randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled Phase 3 study aims to recruit adult and elderly subjects with insomnia at multiple centers in South Korea.\n...\nOn March 21, 2024, the Group announced it had dosed the first subject in a Phase 1 trial evaluating its novel EP4 receptor agonist, NXE0033744 for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (\"IBD\"), a therapeutic area where there remains significant unmet need for millions of people worldwide.\nNXE0033744 is a potent, selective and gut-restricted prostaglandin EP4 receptor agonist that has been uniquely designed to bring clinical benefit by accelerating the healing of damaged epithelial mucosa and suppressing exaggerated gut inflammation, with minimal systemic exposure to avoid adverse events.\n...\nNXE0033744 aims to address the significant unmet need of people with IBD that do not achieve satisfactory disease control.\n...\nThe Phase 1 trial is a first-in-human randomized, double-blind study to assess the safety, pharmacokinetics and effects on pharmacodynamic biomarkers of single and multiple ascending doses of NXE0033744 in adult healthy volunteers and people with Crohn's disease to generate proof of mechanism.\nThe trial is being conducted in the UK and initial data read-outs are anticipated in 2025.", "date": "2025-02-14", "last_updated": "2025-02-14", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.76, "evidence": 0.4667}, "jev_score": 0.3547, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Nxera Pharma : Consolidated Financial Results for the Nine months Ended September 30, 2024 (IFRS)", "url": "https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/NXERA-PHARMA-CO-LTD-6814799/news/Nxera-Pharma-Consolidated-Financial-Results-for-the-Nine-months-Ended-September-30-2024-IFRS-48229907/", "domain": "marketscreener.com", "snippet": "On March 21, 2024, the Group announced it had dosed the first subject in a Phase 1 trial evaluating its novel EP4 receptor agonist, NXE0033744 for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (\"IBD\"), a therapeutic area where there remains significant unmet need for millions of people worldwide.\nNXE0033744 is a potent, selective and gut-restricted prostaglandin EP4 receptor agonist that has been uniquely designed to bring clinical benefit by accelerating the healing of damaged epithelial mucosa and suppressing exaggerated gut inflammation, with minimal systemic exposure to avoid adverse events.\nThis approach is widely recognized to promote deeper remission and offer better long-term clinical outcomes.\nNXE0033744 aims to address the significant unmet need of people with IBD that do not achieve satisfactory disease control.\n...\nThe Phase 1 trial is a first-in-human randomized, double-blind study to assess the safety, pharmacokinetics and effects on pharmacodynamic biomarkers of single and multiple ascending doses of NXE0033744 in adult healthy volunteers and people with Crohn's disease to generate proof of mechanism.\nThe trial will be conducted in the UK and initial data read-outs are anticipated from 2025.", "date": "2024-11-01", "last_updated": "2024-11-02", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.76, "evidence": 0.43}, "jev_score": 0.3268, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Nxera Pharma Operational Highlights and Consolidated Results for ...", "url": "https://www.samedanltd.com/press-releases/nxera-pharma-operational-highlights-and-consolidated-results-for-the-first-quarter-2024/", "domain": "samedanltd.com", "snippet": "**Progress with in-house programs**\n- First subject dosed in a phase 1 trial with NXE0033744, a novel, potent, selective and gut-restricted EP4 receptor agonist discovered by Nxera in development for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD)", "date": "2024-05-09", "last_updated": "2026-04-06", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.79, "evidence": 0.4133}, "jev_score": 0.3265, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "GSK-4381406(GSK-4381406) - 药物靶点：GPR35_在研适应症 ...", "url": "https://synapse.zhihuiya.com/drug/92c6b248e38c4deb8ac490feb25a8d1b", "domain": "synapse.zhihuiya.com", "snippet": "在研适应症\n炎症性肠病\n非在研适应症\n溃疡性结肠炎\n原研机构\nNxera Pharma Co., Ltd.\n在研机构\nNxera Pharma Co., Ltd.\n非在研机构\nGSK Plc\n权益机构\nGSK Plc\nNxera Pharma Co., Ltd.\n最高研发阶段\n临床前\n首次获批日期\n...\nthe Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare of Japan for the treatment of adult patients with insomnia received in September 2024First subject dosed in a Phase 1 trial with NXE0033744, a novel, potent, selective and gut-restricted EP4 receptor agonist in development for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) Full ownership of NXE0027477 regained from GSK – NXE-477 is a clinic-ready, highly selective, first-in-class, oral GPR35 agonist in development as a potential new treatment for IBD.\n...\nIn addition to several products being commercialized in Japan, we are advancing an extensive pipeline of over 30 active programs from discovery through to late clinical stage internally and in partnership with leading pharma and biotech companies.\n...\nexecutive, is leading the post-acquisition integration of the Nxera Pharma Japan (“NPJ”) and Nxera Pharma Korea (“NPK”) businesses into Nxera and will be responsible for all technical operations Progress with in-house programs First subject dosed in a Phase 1 trial with NXE0033744, a novel\n, potent, selective and gut-restricted EP4 receptor agonist discovered by Nxera in development for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) Regained full ownership from GSK of NXE0027477, a clinic-ready, highly selective, first-in-class, oral GPR35 agonist in\n...\nThis exciting program has already delivered highly promising preclinical data that support its potential as a new therapy for IBD and is poised to enter a Phase 1 clinical trial.\nThis presents a clear opportunity for Sosei Heptares to further advance this program while determining the optimal path forward for further development and commercialization.”\n...\n炎症性肠病\n临床前\n日本\nNxera Pharma Co., Ltd.\n2023-11-24", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-15", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.62, "evidence": 0.4433}, "jev_score": 0.2748, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}], "total_ms": 819.5, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:33+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q042-1", "row_id": "q042", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis, Duration \u00143 Months, Modified Mayo Score 5 to 9, With Inadequate Response, Loss of Response, or Intolerance to Prior Standard-of-Care Medications competing agents in the same mechanistic class as TYK2 Small Molecule", "query": "D-2570 TYK2 ulcerative colitis competitor Phase 2 status", "anchors": ["D-2570"], "search_latency_ms": 6732.2, "target": "drugs competing with D-2570: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 349.2, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9627, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000404, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 4, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.7569, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Emerging Therapies for Ulcerative Colitis: Updates from Recent ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10441644/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "OST-122 is a gut selective oral JAK inhibitor with selectivity for JAK3, TYK2 and AMPK-related protein kinase 5 (ARK5).\nThe phase Ib/IIa trial which enrolled 32 patients with moderate-to-severe UC has been recently completed and results are yet to be published (NCT04353791).84\n...\nDeucravacitinib is an oral TYK2 inhibitor in development for the treatment of moderate-to-severe UC.\nIn a phase II, double-blind trial (LATTICE-UC), 131 patients were randomized to deucravacitinib 6 mg twice daily vs placebo.89 The trial failed to meet its primary endpoint of clinical remission at 12 weeks defined by the modified Mayo score (stool frequency sub-score ≤1 with a decrease from baseline of at least 1 point, a rectal bleeding sub-score of 0, and an endoscopy sub-score of ≤1).", "date": "2023-08-17", "last_updated": "2026-08-12", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.7967}, "jev_score": 0.7569, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Advancing therapeutic frontiers: a pipeline of novel drugs for ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12952356/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|TYK2 Inhibitor|Zasocitinib (TAK-279)|AI-designed highly selective allosteric TYK2 inhibitor|NCT06254950, NCT06764615|Phase 2|Recruiting; estimated completion Aug 2027|\n...\n|TYK2 Inhibitor|D-2570|Novel oral TYK2 inhibitor|NCT07035041|Phase 2|Recruiting; began May 2025, estimated completion Dec 2026|\n...\nIt is being tested in a Phase 2, multicenter, placebo-controlled, double-blind RCT for moderately to severely active UC in 207 participants aged 18–75 who have inadequate response to conventional, biologic, or advanced therapies, with the primary outcome measuring clinical remission at week 12 using mMS, currently recruiting with estimated completion in August 2027 (NCT06254950).\n...\n#### 2.1.9. D-2570\nD-2570 is a novel oral TYK2 inhibitor being developed for autoimmune diseases including psoriasis and UC evaluated in a Phase 2 multicenter double-blind, placebo-controlled RCT (NCT07035041) with 120 participants randomized 1:1:1 to two different D-2570 dosing arms or placebo for 12 weeks.", "date": "2026-01-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-25", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.8}, "jev_score": 0.752, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Interleukin-23p19 Inhibitors in Inflammatory Bowel Disease", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12942054/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "In the ANTHEM-UC trial, a phase 2b study involving 252 adults with moderate-to-severe UC, preliminary results reported dose-dependent improvements in clinical response rates.\n...\nIn addition, small-molecule inhibitors targeting JAK1 and TYK2, which act downstream of the IL-23 receptor, are currently under clinical development.\nDeucr\navacitinib is a selective, allosteric inhibitor of TYK2, an intracellular signaling mediator of IL-23.\nHowever, in three phase 2 clinical trials in patients with moderately to severely active CD and UC (LATTICE-CD, LATTICE-UC, and IM011-127), deucravacitinib demonstrated modest signals of efficacy, but failed to achieve the primary or secondary efficacy endpoints after 12 weeks of treatment across multiple dosing regimens [48].\n...\nOf interest, a next-generation allosteric TYK2 inhibitor, TAK-279 (zasocitinib), is currently in phase 2 evaluation for both UC and CD [51,52].\nTAK-279 is designed for sustained 24 h pathway suppression and these trials will help understand if deeper TYK2 target engagement can translate to mucosal efficacy in IBD.", "date": "2026-02-14", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.92, "evidence": 0.7267}, "jev_score": 0.6686, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Top 7 Leading Drug Candidates in Ulcerative Colitis Treatment", "url": "https://www.delveinsight.com/blog/emerging-drugs-for-ulcerative-colitis-treatment", "domain": "delveinsight.com", "snippet": "**Takeda’s Zasocitinib**\n*Phase II*\n**Zasocitinib (TAK-279)** is an oral, investigational TYK2 inhibitor being studied for moderate-to-severe ulcerative colitis.\nIt is designed to reduce inflammation by targeting the IL-23/TYK2 pathway, and Takeda is evaluating it in phase 2 studies for both ulcerative colitis and Crohn’s disease, including a long-term extension trial for patients who responded in the parent studies.", "date": "2026-06-25", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.91, "evidence": 0.7}, "jev_score": 0.637, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Advancing therapeutic frontiers: a pipeline of novel drugs ...", "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/gastroenterology/articles/10.3389/fgstr.2026.1747118/full", "domain": "frontiersin.org", "snippet": "|TYK2 Inhibitor|D-2570|Novel oral TYK2 inhibitor|NCT07035041|Phase 2|Recruiting; began May 2025, estimated completion Dec 2026|\n...\nIt is being tested in a Phase 2, multicenter, placebo-controlled, double-blind RCT for moderately to severely active UC in 207 participants aged 18–75 who have inadequate response to conventional, biologic, or advanced therapies, with the primary outcome measuring clinical remission at week 12 using mMS, currently recruiting with estimated completion in August 2027 (NCT06254950).\n...\n#### 2.1.9 D-2570\nD-2570 is a novel oral TYK2 inhibitor being developed for autoimmune diseases including psoriasis and UC evaluated in a Phase 2 multicenter double-blind, placebo-controlled RCT (NCT07035041) with 120 participants randomized 1:1:1 to two different D-2570 dosing arms or placebo for 12 weeks.\n...\nThe study began May 2025 with estimated primary completion July 2026 and final completion December 2026, currently in the recruiting Phase with no results yet available as the trial is ongoing.", "date": "2026-01-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-29", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.61, "evidence": 0.4867}, "jev_score": 0.2969, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Yifang Bio-U (688382) 2026 H1 Report Commentary: Multiple Core Pipeline Programs Show Strong Progress; Optimistic About the Realization of Innovation", "url": "https://news.futunn.com/en/post/78219536/yifang-biopharma-u-688382-2026-interim-report-review-core-pipeline", "domain": "news.futunn.com", "snippet": "D-2570 is demonstrating broad therapeutic potential, with the value of its TYK2 inhibitor pipeline continuing to stand out.\nIn the first half of 2026, D-2570 has made significant progress: (1) enrollment and dosing have been initiated for the first patient in a head-to-head Phase III trial in psoriasis; (2) the first patient has been enrolled in a Phase II trial for psoriatic arthritis; (3) the first patient has been enrolled in a Phase II trial for systemic lupus erythematosus;\n(4) all participants have been enrolled in a pivotal Phase III trial for moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis; (5) all participants have been enrolled in a Phase II trial for moderate-to-severe active ulcerative colitis; and (6) the U.S. FDA has formally approved D-2570 for a Phase II monotherapy study in psoriasis.\nIn the Phase II psoriasis trial, D-2570 demonstrated superior efficacy compared to both placebo and currently marketed TYK2 inhibitors, highlighting its \"best-in-class\" potential.\nIts indications are expanding into multiple autoimmune diseases, including psoriatic arthritis, systemic lupus erythematosus, and ulcerative colitis, with substantial market opportunities.", "date": "2026-08-25", "last_updated": "2026-08-26", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.57, "evidence": 0.39}, "jev_score": 0.2223, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study on the Safety of TAK-279 and Whether it Can Reduce Inflammation in the Bowel of Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis", "url": "https://med.agiltrace.com/clinical-trials/NCT06254950", "domain": "med.agiltrace.com", "snippet": "NCT03943446 ·Status: TERMINATED ·Phase: PHASE2\n- A Phase 2 Study of D-2570 in Subjects With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis\nNCT07035041 ·Status: ACTIVE_NOT_RECRUITING ·Phase: PHASE2", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-05", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.59, "evidence": 0.3567}, "jev_score": 0.2105, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "The Efficacy of Hyperbaric Oxygen-assisted Treatment for ASUC and Refractory IBD", "url": "https://med.agiltrace.com/clinical-trials/NCT07257588", "domain": "med.agiltrace.com", "snippet": "- A Phase 2 Study of D-2570 in Subjects With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis\nNCT07035041 ·Status: ACTIVE_NOT_RECRUITING ·Phase: PHASE2\n- A Study to Evaluate IBI112 in the Treatment of Moderate to Severe Active Ulcerative Colitis\n...\n- Clinical Response and Safety Following FMT for UC", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-05", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.57, "evidence": 0.3333}, "jev_score": 0.19, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "SUMMARY", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2026/108029/a128849/sehk26010100538.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Within our clinical-stage pipeline, our Core Products tyrosine kinase 2 (“TYK2”) inhibitor D-2570 and oral estrogen receptor degrader (“SERD”) taragarestrant (D-0502) are both advancing through Phase III registration trials, while our urate transporter 1 (“URAT1”) inhibitor darbinurad (D-0120) has completed a Phase IIb clinical trial.\n...\nD-2570\nTYK2\nAutoimmune \ndiseases\nSubmit NDA in H2 2027\nGlobal\nInitiate Phase III trial in H1 2026\nComplete Phase II trial in H2 2026\nComplete Phase I trial in H1 2026\nInitiate Phase II trial in H1 2026\nInitiate Phase II trial in H1 2026\nSubmit IND in H1 2026\n...\nOur Core Product D-2570 is a self-developed, orally administered, highly selective TYK2 allosteric inhibitor for the treatment of psoriasis and other autoimmune diseases.\nOur Phase II clinical trial in moderate-to-severe psoriasis delivered outstanding results, with efficacy significantly superior to both placebo and approved products of the same class (based on published clinical data), and comparable to that of biologics, while maintaining strong safety and tolerability.\nWe have agreed with the NMPA on the Phase III clinical trial protocol and have initiated the registrational Phase III clinical trial in September 2025.\nIn parallel, we have also commenced a Phase II clinical study for ulcerative colitis (“UC”) in China.\n...\nD-2570 is a TYK2 allosteric inhibitor under development primarily for the treatment of plaque psoriasis and UC.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-06", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.55, "evidence": 0.32}, "jev_score": 0.176, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Study Evaluating ISM5411 Administered Orally to Subjects With Active Ulcerative Colitis (BETHESDA)", "url": "https://med.agiltrace.com/clinical-trials/NCT07265570", "domain": "med.agiltrace.com", "snippet": "NCT02368717 ·Status: COMPLETED ·Phase: PHASE3\n...\n- A Phase 2 Study of D-2570 in Subjects With Moderately to Severely Active Ulcerative Colitis\nNCT07035041 ·Status: ACTIVE_NOT_RECRUITING ·Phase: PHASE2", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-05", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.56, "evidence": 0.2633}, "jev_score": 0.1474, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 7081.4, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:34+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q044-2", "row_id": "q044", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease competing agents in the same mechanistic class as GPR52 Prostaglandin E2 Receptor EP4, including Small Molecule therapies", "query": "NXE0033744 EP4 agonist clinical trial", "anchors": ["NXE0033744", "NXE744"], "search_latency_ms": 5753.3, "target": "drugs competing with NXE0033744 / NXE744: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 330.7, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8673, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000364, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 4, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.4694, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "NXE0033744 / Nxera Pharma - LARVOL DELTA", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=46ed8e5f-d4e9-4c02-93dc-3f749bfc1024", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "/ Nxera Pharma\n...\nMarch 20, 2024\nSosei Heptares Doses First Subject in Phase 1 Trial with HTL0033744, an EP4 Agonist for Inflammatory Bowel Disease\n...\n- \"Sosei Group Corporation...announces it has dosed the first subject in a Phase 1 trial evaluating its novel EP4 receptor agonist, HTL0033744 (HTL’744) for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD)....The trial will be conducted in the UK and initial data read-outs are anticipated from 2025.\"", "date": "2024-03-20", "last_updated": "2025-08-24", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.8, "evidence": 0.5867}, "jev_score": 0.4694, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Presentation title - Nxera Pharma", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/common/pdf/Corporate_Presentation_2025Jan_EN_v2.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "EP4 ag.\nNXE’744\n...\nPhase 2 study start in Schizophrenia\nNXE’744 (EP4 agonist)\n...\nImmuno-oncology\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nSME\nInflammatory bowel disease\n...\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nInflammatory bowel diseases\nPh1", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-10", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.5267}, "jev_score": 0.4477, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Nxera Pharma : Annual Report Year ended 31 December 2024", "url": "https://www.marketscreener.com/news/nxera-pharma-annual-report-year-ended-31-december-2024-ce7c50dcd18dff20", "domain": "marketscreener.com", "snippet": "Behind that, and powered by our unique NxWave™ discovery platform, we are advancing an extensive pipeline of over 30 active programs from discovery through to late clinical stage internally and in partnership with leading pharma and biotech companies.\n...\nEP4 ag.\nNXE'744\nInflammatory Bowel Disease\n...\nOur three wholly owned clinical programs are also advancing as planned in Phase 1 development, with several important milestones expected over the next 12-18 months.\nThese programs are: NXE-149, which is targeting unmet needs in schizophrenia and is the subject of an option-to-license agreement with Boehringer Ingelheim; NXE-732, which is being investigated in solid tumors in collaboration with Cancer Research UK; and NXE-744, which offers a possible novel mechanism to treat inflammatory bowel diseases.\n...\nInternal pipeline progress\nEP4 agonist\nNXE0033744\nThe first subject was dosed in a Phase 1 trial of NXE'744, an oral, gut-restricted EP4 agonist with potential to treat Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD).\nNXE'744 has been designed to bring clinical benefit by accelerating the healing of damaged epithelial mucosa and suppressing exaggerated gut inflammation, with minimal systemic exposure thereby providing significantly enhanced safety and efficacy.", "date": "2025-08-29", "last_updated": "2025-08-29", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.82, "evidence": 0.5233}, "jev_score": 0.4291, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Consolidated Financial Results for the Nine months Ended September 30, 2024", "url": "https://finance.stockweather.co.jp/contents/dispPDF.aspx?disclosure=20241101509584", "domain": "finance.stockweather.co.jp", "snippet": "On March 21, 2024, the Group announced it had dosed the first subject in a Phase 1 trial evaluating its novel EP4 receptor agonist, NXE0033744 for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease\n(“IBD”), a therapeutic area where there remains significant unmet need for millions of people \nworldwide.\nNXE0033744 is a potent, selective and gut-restricted prostaglandin EP4 receptor agonist that has been uniquely designed to bring clinical benefit by accelerating the healing of damaged epithelial mucosa and suppressing exaggerated gut inflammation, with minimal systemic exposure to avoid adverse events.\nThis approach is widely recognized to promote deeper remission and offer better long-term clinical outcomes.\nNXE0033744 aims to address the significant unmet need of people with IBD that do not achieve satisfactory disease control.\n...\nThe Phase 1 trial is a first-in-human randomized, double-blind study to assess the safety, pharmacokinetics and effects on pharmacodynamic biomarkers of single and multiple ascending doses of NXE0033744 in adult healthy volunteers and people with Crohn’s disease to generate proof of mechanism.\nThe trial will be conducted in the UK and initial data read-outs are anticipated from 2025.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-01-07", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.77, "evidence": 0.5033}, "jev_score": 0.3875, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Corporate Presentation - Investors - Nxera Pharma", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/common/pdf/Corporate_Presentation_2025Feb_EN_vF.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "Immuno-oncology\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nSME\nInflammatory bowel disease\n...\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nInflammatory bowel diseases\nPh1\nUp to  220\n-\n2023-11-24\n2026-06-30\n2024-02-15\nISRCTN70080074\n-", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-17", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.8, "evidence": 0.47}, "jev_score": 0.376, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] R&D Day - Investors - Nxera Pharma", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/common/pdf/2025.11.18%20R&D%20Day_vF.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "Phase 2a expansion underway in:\n...\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nSME\nInflammatory bowel disease\n...\nUnder the Clinical Trial and Licence Agreement (CTLA) in 2022, Cancer Research UK sponsors, designs and executes a Phase I/IIa clinical trial of NXE0039732, and Nxera holds a licence to the results generated under the trial to \n...\nFTiH\n...\nNXE-732 is a selective \n...\ncompleted.\n...\nImmuno-oncology\n...\n2023-07-13\n...\nNCT05944237\n-\nNXE0033744\nEP4 agonist\nInflammatory bowel diseases\nPh1\nUp to  220\n-\n2023-11-24\n2026-06-30\n2024-05-02\nISRCTN70080074", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-12", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.78, "evidence": 0.4733}, "jev_score": 0.3692, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Nxera Pharma Operational Highlights and Consolidated Results for ...", "url": "https://www.biospace.com/nxera-pharma-operational-highlights-and-consolidated-results-for-the-first-quarter-2024", "domain": "biospace.com", "snippet": "**Progress with in-house programs**\n- First subject dosed in a Phase 1 trial with NXE0033744, a novel, potent, selective and gut-restricted EP4 receptor agonist discovered by Nxera in development for the treatment of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD)", "date": "2024-05-09", "last_updated": "2026-08-15", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.44}, "jev_score": 0.3564, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank"