{"case_id": "q047-1", "row_id": "q047", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor first regulatory approval or market launch year for acute myeloid leukemia", "query": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML approval launch", "anchors": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor", "CDK12"], "search_latency_ms": 442.3, "target": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor / CDK12", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 362.8, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7590, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000319, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.5945, "results": [{"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "CDK12/13", "url": "https://insilico.com/pipeline_target_cdk12/13", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "CDK12\nCyclin-dependent kinase 12/13 (CDK12/13) Inhibitor:\nTreating Tumors through Induction of BRCAness\n(IND-Enabling)\nAssays Completed\nWholly-owned and Available for Licensing\n- *In vivo* efficacy studies – Combo study with Olaparib and Cisplatin\n- *In vivo* efficacy studies – Single agent\n...\nInhibition or loss of CDK12/CDK13 provokes a ''BRCAness'' phenotype that results in deficiencies in DNA damage repair, promoting synergy with DNA-damaging chemotherapy and PARP inhibitors.\n...\nInsilico Medicine CDK12 Inhibitor Summary – IND-Enabling\n...\nEffective in both mono and combo therapies\n...\n- Potential broader indications such as AML, HCC, SCLC, Colorectal cancer, and Ovarian cancer\nPromising drug-ability as an oral agent\n...\nInsilico Medicine developed an AI-designed covalent inhibitor targeting CDK12.\n*In vivo* efficacy studies in SUM149PT CDX mice models showed strong dose-dependent anti-tumor activity with robust and durable tumor regression.\nThe data also indicated that the inhibitor could induce BRCAness in the tumor cells.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-22", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.91, "evidence": 0.6533}, "jev_score": 0.5945, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "JMC｜With generative AI assistance, Insilico Medicine ...", "url": "https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/1074881", "domain": "eurekalert.org", "snippet": "Insilico Medicine (\"Insilico\"), a clinical stage generative artificial intelligence (AI)-driven biotechnology company, today announced the publication of a novel series of orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitors, as a potential option against refractory and treatment-resistant cancers.\nPublished in the ***Journal of Medicinal Chemistry* ** (IF=7.2), the study showcases the discovery of compound 12b, a potent, selective, and safe therapy targeting CDK12/13, empowered by Insilico’s proprietary generative AI platforms including PandaOmics and Chemistry42.\n...\nDuring the preclinical *in vitro* and *in vivo* testing, compound 12b demonstrated nanomolar potencies across cancer cell lines, desirable ADME properties.\nFurthermore, 12b exhibited significant efficacy in breast cancer and acute myeloid leukemia (AML) models, all without inducing intolerable side effects, paving the way for further therapeutic development.\n...\n\"The research and development process showcases how AI-guided drug design can achieve both precision and safety in cancer therapeutics, and we are striving to advance the compound in this program into clinical trials in the near future.\"", "date": "2025-02-26", "last_updated": "2026-04-21", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.86, "evidence": 0.68}, "jev_score": 0.5848, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Press Releases", "url": "https://insilico.com/news", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "20 October 2023\nInsilico Medicine nominates novel CDK12/13 small molecule inhibitor as preclinical candidate for multiple tumors", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-23", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.86, "evidence": 0.6233}, "jev_score": 0.536, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Insilico Medicine's Post - LinkedIn", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/in-silico-medicine_design-synthesis-and-biological-evaluation-activity-7296190298206973952-MIOC", "domain": "linkedin.com", "snippet": "Here, we report the discovery of compound 12b as a novel, potent, orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitor with a promising safety profile and robust in vivo antitumor properties.", "date": "2025-02-14", "last_updated": "2025-12-05", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.6}, "jev_score": 0.51, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Insilico Medicine", "url": "https://siliconvalleyinvestclub.com/companies/insilico/tear-sheet.pdf", "domain": "siliconvalleyinvestclub.com", "snippet": "Insilico Medicine nominates novel CDK12/13 small molecule inhibitor as preclinical candidate for multiple tumors", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-30", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.82, "evidence": 0.6167}, "jev_score": 0.5057, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Insilico Medicine News", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/company.php?CompanyId=968423&tab=newstrac", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "snippet": "Discovery and evaluation of ISM6466A, a novel covalent CDK12 inhibitor for the treatment of cancer\n...\nResults from a 28-day rat DRF study revealed that the compound did not show evident signs of toxicity at the tested doses, suggesting a reasonable safety window for ISM6466A.In summary, the novel, covalent, small-molecule CDK12 inhibitor, ISM6466A, demonstrated excellent preclinical efficacy along with favorable drug-like properties.\nOur results underscore the therapeutic potential of ISM6466A for the treatment of cancer.", "date": "2025-05-25", "last_updated": "2025-06-03", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.76, "evidence": 0.6067}, "je