but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-12", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.63, "evidence": 0.16}, "jev_score": 0.1008, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "CLINICAL TRIALS", "url": "https://www.amgentrials.com/study/?id=20190172", "domain": "amgentrials.com", "snippet": "AboutScienceProductsResponsibilityStoriesNewsroomPartnersInvestorsCareers\n## CLINICAL TRIALS", "date": "1996-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-03-19", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.28, "evidence": 0.0467}, "jev_score": 0.0131, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "UC hematology experts present research at national conference", "url": "https://www.uc.edu/news/articles/2023/12/uc-hematology-experts-present-research-at-national-conference.html", "domain": "uc.edu", "snippet": "IRAK4 is a protein known to help drive growth of acute myeloid leukemia (AML) cells through overactivation, making it a potential target for new treatments.\n...\nThey found one compound was especially effective at killing AML cells by reducing the levels of a different protein called c-myc that drives cancer growth.\n...\nMany drugs have been developed to target c-myc without much clinical success, so Vick said moving forward the team will test the use of this class of drugs with IRAK4 inhibitors as an alternative approach to target leukemia.\n...\nThe research team tested a new compound in the lab and found it works “very well” against the gatekeeper mutation and shows promise as a treatment that could help lead to long-term survival for patients with AML.\nA Phase 1 clinical trial in healthy volunteers is currently underway to determine the best dose of the treatment in humans, Elgamal said.", "date": "2023-12-08", "last_updated": "2025-10-01", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.04, "evidence": 0.2}, "jev_score": 0.008, "jev_