anged Disease.\nThis phase Ib trial evaluates the safety, side effects, and optimal dosage of SNDX-5613 in combination with standard chemotherapy (daunorubicin and cytarabine) for patients with newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia (AML) harboring NPM1 or MLL/KMT2A gene mutations.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.02, "evidence": 0.03}, "jev_score": 0.0006, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Internal Server Error", "url": "https://cdas.cancer.gov/approved-projects/5003/", "domain": "cdas.cancer.gov", "snippet": "The server encountered an internal error or misconfiguration and was unable to complete your request.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2024-10-20", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.23, "evidence": 0.0}, "jev_score": 0.0, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 3638.2, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:36+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q044-4", "row_id": "q044", "mode": "queries", "objective": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease competing agents in the same mechanistic class as GPR52 Prostaglandin E2 Receptor EP4, including Small Molecule therapies", "query": "NXE744 EP4 agonist competitors IBD", "anchors": ["NXE0033744", "NXE744"], "search_latency_ms": 23475.8, "target": "drugs competing with NXE0033744 / NXE744: other agents in the same mechanistic class or for the same indication, as described in `objective`", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 417.2, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8990, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000378, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.642, "results": [{"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "The update of prostaglandin E2 receptor subtype 4 (EP4) in ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13393408/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "^55^ Various EP4 agonists (such as AGN205203, KAG-308, ONO-4819, ONO-AE1-734, and NXT-10796) have been demonstrated to promote intestinal mucosal repair and to ameliorate the symptoms of IBD and intestinal injury\nby inhibiting intestinal epithelial cell necrosis, decreasing the infiltration of immune cells, and promoting lymphangiogenesis.56, 57, 58, 59, 60 In addition, some comparative studies have found that EP4 agonists are more effective in IBD treatment than the commonly used drugs for IBD, such as aminosalicylates (sulfasalazine, mesalazine, olsalazine), corticosteroids (budesonide), 6-thioguanine, cyclosporine A (CsA), *etc*.\n^61^ Furthermore, a phase II clinical trial has confirmed that the EP4 agonist ONO-4819 is effective in IBD patients resistant to 5-aminosalicylates.^62^ Consistent with the results of the agonists mentioned above, studies using EP4 transgenic animals have also validated the protective role of EP4 in IBD.", "date": "2026-03-27", "last_updated": "2026-09-23", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.9, "evidence": 0.7133}, "jev_score": 0.642, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Earnings call transcript: Nxera Pharma Q4 2025 shows ...", "url": "https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-nxera-pharma-q4-2025-shows-revenue-growth-stock-dips-93CH-4504567", "domain": "investing.com", "snippet": "However, we did successfully begin a new phase II trial with our EP4 antagonist program, and the early clinical data from this program is very encouraging as we aim to fast follow Ono’s product with the same mechanism of action.\n...\nIn our wholly owned in-house portfolio, we have two phase II-ready assets now, NXE149, a GPR52 agonist for schizophrenia, and NXE744, an EP4 agonist for IBD.\nThese are both undergoing competitive licensing processes, and our aim is for both of these programs to be partnered by the end of FY 2026, if not sooner.\n...\nWe have two Phase II-ready assets, NXE149, our first-in-class schizophrenia candidate, and NXE744, our EP4 agonist for IBD.\nBoth of them are undergoing competitive licensing processes, which we announced earlier in the year during J.P.\n...\nNXE744 is a gut-restricted, selective EP4 agonist with dual mode of action.\nIt’s combining an anti-inflammatory activity and is promoting mucosal healing in IBD.\nAll first-in-class study elements have completed dosing in the clinic, and in the SAT and in the MAT studies, there have been no concerning safety signals detected so far.\nImportantly, no systemic exposure, but very high gut tissue levels were observed in healthy volunteers, and we are very pleased that in preliminary analysis, this gut-restrictive profile was also confirmed in a cohort of UC patients.\nIn addition, we are very excited about the interim analysis of our indomethacin study, showing a highly significant reduction of around 50% of indomethacin-induced permeability in our NXE744 treatment group, and thereby confirming target engagement.\nThis asset is now phase II-ready, and we are currently engaging in a competitive licensing process and are in discussions with a number of major pharma companies.\n...\nWhere we see a clear differentiation for EP4 agonist is that we’re having, as you pointed out, a dual mode of action, an anti-inflammatory as well as a barrier repair function.", "date": "2026-02-13", "last_updated": "2026-08-08", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.9, "evidence": 0.6733}, "jev_score": 0.606, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "The prevention of colitis by E Prostanoid receptor 4 agonist through enhancement of epithelium survival and regeneration - PubMed", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17008451/", "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "To investigate this potential application, we have tested another EP4-selective agonist in the DSS-indomethacin mouse colitis model.\n7-[2-(3-Hydroxy-4-phenyl-but-1-enyl)-6-oxo-piperidin-1-yl]-heptanoic acid methyl ester, C23H33NO4 (AGN205203), an analog from the 8-azapiperidinone series of EP4 agonists, is metabolically and chemically more stable than the ONO agonist, because of its lack of oxidizable sulfur atoms in the alpha-chain and of 11-OH group, a potential source of beta-elimination reaction.\nTreatment of mice subcutaneously with AGN205203 at 3 mg/kg/day minimized colitis symptoms, such as weight loss, diarrhea, and colonic bleeding.\n...\nAt cellular level, the drug treatment decreased colon epithelial apoptosis, prevented goblet cell depletion, and promoted epithelial regeneration.\nAGN205203 may be unique among known EP4 agonists for its metabolic and chemical stability, and it is amenable to systemic applications for the prevention and recovery of IBD.", "date": "2007-01-26", "last_updated": "2025-05-26", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.87, "evidence": 0.6633}, "jev_score": 0.5771, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Discovery of NXT-10796, an orally active, intestinally restricted EP4 ...", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37270073/", "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "# Discovery of NXT-10796, an orally active, intestinally restricted EP4 agonist prodrug for the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease\n...\nThe resulting oxalic acid monohydrazide-derived carboxylate isostere demonstrated utility as a class of prodrug showing colon-targeted delivery of parent agonist 2, with minimal exposure observed in the plasma.\nOral administration of NXT-10796 demonstrated tissue specific activation of the EP4 receptor through modulation of immune genes in the colon, without modulation of EP4 driven biomarkers in the plasma compartment.", "date": "2023-07-15", "last_updated": "2025-09-19", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.84, "evidence": 0.6367}, "jev_score": 0.5348, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "EP4 receptor: GPCR with multiple therapeutic Opportunities", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/common/pdf/2022.10.13%20R&D%20Day_vF.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "Ph 2 \nGrapiprant +/- Pembrolizumab (Phase 1 & 1b/2)\nE7046 +/- Pembrolizumab (Phase 1b)\nBMS-986310/ONO-4578 +/- Nivolumab (Phase 1 & 1b/2a)\n...\npredicted oral daily dose\n• EP4 Agonist for GI inflammatory disease (IBD): \n• Successful design of a novel, gut restricted EP4 agonist\n• Opportunity to promote epithelial repair and reduce immune mediated damage in the inflamed gut.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-22", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.65}, "jev_score": 0.5265, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Discovery of Non-prostanoid EP4 Agonists for the ... - PubMed", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41931300/?fc=20240612233255&ff=20260403193118&v=2.19.0.post6+133c1fe", "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "The prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 is linked to intestinal homeostasis, wound repair, and immune cell activation, and EP4 agonists hold promise as a novel treatment for IBD via a tissue repair mechanism.\nA high-throughput screening campaign resulted in the discovery of a non-prostanoid, selective EP4 agonist chemotype, which was optimized through structure-activity relationship (SAR) studies.\nLead compound **11a** was profiled in a mouse pharmacokinetic study and demonstrated efficacy in a mouse model of IBD.\nBlood exposure of **11a** was shown to induce hemodynamic changes in mouse, a known on-target effect of EP4 agonists in systemic circulation.\nHigh-throughput mutagenesis studies and computational modeling indicate that this series of agonists binds orthosterically to the PGE2 site in the EP4 receptor despite structural differentiation from prostanoids.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-04-06", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.81, "evidence": 0.5867}, "jev_score": 0.4752, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease Therapy Area Landscape", "url": "https://mpadvisor.com/tocDocument/MP%20-%20Inflamattory%20Bowel%20Disease%20-%20Therapy%20Area%20Landscape%20-%20October%202024.pdf", "domain": "mpadvisor.com", "snippet": "NXE'744/  Nxera \nPharma / EP4\nSOR-102 / Sorriso \nPharma /  TNF-α & IL-23", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-01-09", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.53}, "jev_score": 0.4505, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Presentation title - Investors - Nxera Pharma", "url": "https://investors.nxera.life/common/pdf/Corporate_Presentation_2025Sep_EN_v1.pdf", "domain": "investors.nxera.life", "snippet": "EP4 ag.\nNXE’744\nIBD\n...\nPhase 2 study start in Schizophrenia\nNXE’744 (EP4 agonist)\nH2 2025\nPhase 2 study start in IBD\n...\nThrough combined anti-inflammatory and barrier repair effects, EP4 agonists are expected to bring benefits in IBD by promoting mucosal healing.\n...\nA first-in-class GI-targeted agent to promote mucosal healing in IBD\n...\nFTIH SAD/MAD studies have completed", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-13", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.8, "evidence": 0.54}, "jev_score": 0.432, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Jefferies Global Healthcare Conference 2026 summary", "url": "https://quartr.com/events/nxera-pharma-co-ltd-4565-jefferies-global-healthcare-conference-2026_F97qKSfr", "domain": "quartr.com", "snippet": "### Out-licensing and clinical asset updates\n- Active discussions underway to out-license phase II-ready EP4 agonist (for IBD) and GPR52 agonist (for schizophrenia), both with completed phase I studies and clean safety profiles.\n- EP4 agonist (NXE'744) confirmed gut-restricted, with target engagement and early UC patient data; GPR52 agonist previously partnered, now returned and phase II-ready.\n- Both assets expected to find new partners in the second half of the year, with potential for monotherapy or combination therapy.", "date": "2026-06-03", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.79, "evidence": 0.5367}, "jev_score": 0.424, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Landscape of new drugs and targets in inflammatory bowel disease", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ueg2.12305", "domain": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com", "snippet": "Etrolizumab (PRO145223) is a humanized monoclonal antibody that selectively binds the *ß* ~7~ subunit of the heterodimeric integrins α~4~β~7~ and α~E~β~7~.", "date": "2022-12-01", "last_updated": "2026-09-28", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.13, "evidence": 0.1733}, "jev_score": 0.0225, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 23893.0, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:36+00:00"}
