{"case_id": "q049-4", "row_id": "q049", "mode": "queries", "objective": "ABSK131 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in MTAP-Deleted KRAS G12D-Mutated Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma animal models", "query": "ABSK131 MTAP-deleted pancreatic xenograft tumour volume", "anchors": ["ABSK131"], "search_latency_ms": 479.1, "target": "ABSK131", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 426.5, "calls": 9, "attempts": 9, "usage": {"input_tokens": 17206, "output_tokens": 324}, "cost_usd": 0.000723, "n_candidates": 9, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.6799, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "ENA-2024-Abstracts.pdf", "url": "https://event.eortc.org/ena2024/wp-content/uploads/sites/33/2024/10/ENA-2024-Abstracts.pdf", "domain": "event.eortc.org", "snippet": "Complete and sustained tumor regressions were observed in 8 xenograft models, including 2 PDX models, spanning KRAS\n...\nhave discovered a potential best-in-class MTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitor\nABSK131 with improved potency, selectivity, and brain-penetrant ability.\n...\nIn vivo efficacy was evaluated in cell line derived xenograft (CDX) mouse models with tumors harboring MTAP gene deletion.\nResults: ABSK131 strongly inhibits proliferation of MTAP-deleted cell lines, with minimal effects on MTAP wild type cell lines in isogenic or cancer cell line panels.\nIt also selectively reduces SDMA in MTAP-deleted but not wild type cancer cell lines.\nOral administration of ABSK131 strongly inhibits tumor growth in MTAP-deleted xenograft tumor models.\nThe improved selectivity of ABSK131 also leads to superior hematological safety profile in animal studies.\nIn addition, ABSK131 significant brain penetration in several animal species.\nConclusion: ABSK131, presented here by Abbisko Therapeutics, is a highly selective MTA-cooperative and brain-penetrant PRMT5 inhibitor.\n...\nIn MTAP deleted xenograft models,\nAZD3470 induced dose dependent tumor growth inhibition with levels of\nSDMA reduction greater than 90%, and with no apparent body weight loss.\n...\nAZD3470\ndemonstrated strong efficacy and induced stasis and regressions in 59% of all models.\nIn addition, AZD3470 induced >80 of SDMA inhibition across the", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-02", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.7233}, "jev_score": 0.6799, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "ABSK131 / Abbisko - LARVOL DELTA", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=77f15c4a-7852-4271-a722-b1143fb00c80", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "(AACR 2026)\n...\n- \"ABSK131 exhibits strong anti-tumor activity in MTAP-deleted lung and pancreatic cancer models and synergizes effectively with multiple therapeutic agents.\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for MTAP-deleted cancers.\"", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-18", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.6933}, "jev_score": 0.6794, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Abbisko Cayman Limited 和譽開曼有限責任公司 - HKEXnews", "url": "https://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2025/0428/2025042800217.pdf", "domain": "hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "ADCs for the treatment of HER2+ cancers with brain metastases.\n...\nTitle 3: The MTA-Cooperative PRMT5 Inhibitor ABSK131 Exhibits Potent Activity and \nBroad Synergistic Potential in MTAP-Deleted Cancer Models\n...\nABSK131 exhibits strong anti-tumor activity in MTAP-deleted lung and pancreatic cancer models and synergizes effectively with multiple therapeutic agents.\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for\nMTAP-deleted cancers.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-08-30", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.6767}, "jev_score": 0.6632, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "EGFR x PRMT5 - Drugs, Indications, Patents - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/target/bcd79dd868b63f4f8d2cf6c5b2425436", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Therapeutics 2 Session Date and Time: April 28, 2025, 2:00 PM - 5:00 PM (CDT) Location: Poster Section 54 Poster Board Number: 14 Poster Number: LB240 Conclusion: Our findings establish ABSK112 as a potent, selective and CNS-penetrant HER2 inhibitor, warranting further clinical evaluation of it as a monotherapy or in combination with HER2-targeted ADCs for the treatment of HER2+ cancers with brain metastases.\n...\nTitle 3: The MTA-Cooperative PRMT5 Inhibitor ABSK131 Exhibits Potent Activity and Broad Synergistic Potential in MTAP-Deleted Cancer Models Session Category: Late-Breaking Research: Experimental and Molecular Therapeutics 4 Session Date and Time: April 30, 2025 9:00 AM - 12:00 PM (CDT) Location: Poster Section 51 Poster Board Number: 9 Poster Number: LB427 Conclusion: ABSK131 exhibits strong anti-tumor activity in MTAP-deleted lung and pancreatic cancer models and synergizes effectively with multiple therapeutic agents.\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for MTAP-deleted cancers.", "date": "2025-10-15", "last_updated": "2025-11-28", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.69}, "jev_score": 0.6624, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on ABSK-131 with Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/b9d0045ee6cb4f9a9de977200d7ee848", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Therapeutics 2 Session Date and Time: April 28, 2025, 2:00 PM - 5:00 PM (CDT) Location: Poster Section 54 Poster Board Number: 14 Poster Number: LB240 Conclusion: Our findings establish ABSK112 as a potent, selective and CNS-penetrant HER2 inhibitor, warranting further clinical evaluation of it as a monotherapy or in combination with HER2-targeted ADCs for the treatment of HER2+ cancers with brain metastases.\n...\nTitle 3: The MTA-Cooperative PRMT5 Inhibitor ABSK131 Exhibits Potent Activity and Broad Synergistic Potential in MTAP-Deleted Cancer Models Session Category: Late-Breaking Research: Experimental and Molecular Therapeutics 4 Session Date and Time: April 30, 2025 9:00 AM - 12:00 PM (CDT) Location: Poster Section 51 Poster Board Number: 9 Poster Number: LB427 Conclusion: ABSK131 exhibits strong anti-tumor activity in MTAP-deleted lung and pancreatic cancer models and synergizes effectively with multiple therapeutic agents.\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for MTAP-deleted cancers.", "date": "2025-05-20", "last_updated": "2025-06-16", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.6833}, "jev_score": 0.656, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026 | Abbisko Therapeutics Showcases Six Research ...", "url": "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/aacr-2026--abbisko-therapeutics-showcases-six-research-advances-highlighting-pan-kras-4th-generation-egfr-and-synthetic-lethality-approaches-302751184.html", "domain": "prnewswire.com", "snippet": "**MTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitor ABSK131**\nABSK131 is a potent and selective small-molecule MTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitor developed by Abbisko Therapeutics, targeting MTAP-deleted tumors, and is currently in clinical development.\n...\nMTAP homozygous deletion occurs in approximately 10–15% of solid tumors and frequently co-exists with oncogenic drivers such as KRAS and EGFR.\nIn addition, MTAP abnormities are associated with poor prognosis following standard-of-care therapies across multiple cancer types.\n...\nPreclinical studies demonstrated that ABSK131 exhibits strong synergistic activity with multiple therapies:\n- **KRAS inhibitors: ** Enhanced tumor growth inhibition in KRAS-mutant, MTAP-deleted models when combined with AMG 510 or ABSK141.\n- **EGFR inhibitors: ** Improved anti-proliferative and in vivo antitumor activity in EGFR-mutant, MTAP-deleted NSCLC models when combined with osimertinib.\n- **MAT2A inhibitors: ** Consistent synergistic effects across multiple tumor models when combined with IDE397.\n- **Chemotherapy: ** Synergistic activity observed both in vitro and in vivo when combined with carboplatin in NSCLC models.\nThese findings support ABSK131 as a potential backbone therapy for combination strategies in MTAP-deleted tumors.", "date": "2026-04-22", "last_updated": "2026-09-30", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.6633}, "jev_score": 0.65, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "和誉医药在第36届EORTC-NCI-AACR大会发布PRMT5*MTA及口服KRASG12D临床前研究成果", "url": "https://www.pharnexcloud.com/zixun/lcyj_26827", "domain": "pharnexcloud.com", "snippet": "PRMT5*MTA inhibition has been shown to be synthetic lethal with MTAP deletion.", "date": "2024-10-24", "last_updated": "2025-06-25", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.64, "evidence": 0.5467}, "jev_score": 0.3499, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "�Z6���K�X}е���{�_O=���\"�f<����]o��:�)[wWAG�0J��^��a��MRF�i�9?`�q��N^�������K���Ȝ�k�1f��''�j�)�cS��{�-�ܜ��ȷ:�� w��U�@Մ�q� z2Ҽ���%�{:��Qc�{'A?k�} *�#c�}.fk�*���)9_��8;8��;�vw��5��jPRJWI�rH� ���`n�_�D�y�ڷ.�5�K�>'J~��w��IǍY��Y����F� ���b���lZ}FY�zp��_8����1���71���c�*m�.UI� 4�j�,�H�# ���w�XXM�L\\�D8��������a̻��j�?�JIxBP8��<�U�j jrE�G/ˬ8Ț��2�C&c�ZwD�ƅ��ך}h��\"��z����?4�m�N:���LNFf��Y�,�~�Y�mK��o�X�O-�Ճ��9��LQt)g댛��W��2�5��(�e�J��52H�4s?NJϥ�y`�g���\\_���2�r5 \\m���l�$rw�1����!�iq�A����v��K�y3N�ߵ�V�S�����L��3 ���ͽ�852���I���`�S�����b��,~����G�����