{"case_id": "q054-1", "row_id": "q054", "mode": "queries", "objective": "DWP216 in vivo animal models and results: cell-line xenograft (CDX), patient-derived xenograft (PDX), syngeneic, orthotopic, or genetically engineered models", "query": "DWP216 HNSCC in vivo xenograft monotherapy", "anchors": ["DWP216"], "search_latency_ms": 1328.4, "target": "DWP216", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 337.8, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7974, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000335, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 3, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.7284, "results": [{"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Development of DWP216, a TEAD1 selective inhibitor for NF2 ...", "url": "https://www.kddf.org/upload/files/1737437863_554b09394faaeee65d0a.pdf", "domain": "kddf.org", "snippet": "TEAD1 selective inhibitors, on the other hand, lack sufficient potency.\n• ‌\u0007In an in vivo mouse model, DWP216 is superior to a TEAD1 selective \ninhibitor, with tumor inhibition equivalent to a pan-TEAD inhibitor.\n• ‌\u0007DWP216 shows a synergistic anti-tumor effect with EGFR inhibitor or KRAS \ninhibitor", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-13", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7433}, "jev_score": 0.7284, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "pan-TEAD inhib News", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/moa.php?MoaId=1032265&tab=newstrac", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "snippet": "DWP216\nDaewoong Pharma\nDWP216, a novel TEAD1 selective inhibitor for NF2 mutant tumors and drug-tolerant persister cells\n(Section 18; Poster Board No: 4) - Mar 25, 2025 - Abstract #AACR2025AACR_6716;\nIn conclusion, DWP216 is a promising TEAD1 selective inhibitor for NF2 mutant tumor and may be a proper option for drug-resistance of targeted therapy.\nDWP216 is preparing toward to IND filing for Phase 1 in 2025.\n...\nBased on the excellent in vitro potency and cross-species PK profile, we advanced 1 into an efficacy study in H226 xenograft mouse model and observed good tolerability and strong in vivo response (i.e., tumor regression).\n...\nWhile treatment of head and neck squamous cell carcinoma FAT1m FaDu and YAP1amp Detroit562 xenografts lead to 58% tumor growth inhibition and 35% tumor regression, respectively.\nThese findings identify AZ4331 as a potent inhibitor of the TEAD transcription factor family and further validate the inhibition of TEAD in Hippo-altered cancers as a potential therapeutic strategy.", "date": "2024-11-14", "last_updated": "2025-06-15", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.84, "evidence": 0.86}, "jev_score": 0.7224, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "[단독] 대웅제약의 '차세대 항암 신약' 비밀병기 3종은? - 헬스케어N", "url": "https://m.healthcaren.com/news/news_article_yong.jsp?mn_idx=550285", "domain": "m.healthcaren.com", "snippet": "[헬스코리아뉴스 / 이충만] 대웅제약의 혁신 신약 후보물질 ‘DWP216’, ‘DWP217’, ‘DWP223’ 3종이 비임상 실험에서 모두 양호한 예비 유효성을 보이면서 항암 치료의 새로운 패러다임을 제시할 것이란 기대를 낳고 있다.\n...\n살아있는 유기체 대상 생체 내(in vivo) 실험에서 ‘DWP216’은 기존에 개발 중인 실험용 TEAD1 억제제 또는 범 TEAD 단백질 억제제보다 뛰어난 종양 억제 효과를 나타냈으며, EGFR 및 KRAS 억제제와 병용했을 때에는 시너지 효과까지 보였다.\n...\n생체 내(in vivo) 실험에서도 유의미한 효능이 확인됐다.\n단독 투여만으로도 30mg/kg 용량에서 종양 억제 효과가 나타났으며, PARP 억제제와 병용 투여 시에는 50% 이상의 종양 위축을 유도하는 시너지 효과가 관찰됐다.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-31", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7}, "jev_score": 0.686, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Preclinical Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9139292/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Upon in vivo xenografting in immunodeficient mice, three cell lines from locally advanced or metastatic HNSCC were established.\nFollowing quality control and basic characterization, drug response was examined after therapy with 5-FU, Cisplatin, and cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors (abemaciclib, THZ1).\n...\nAll cell lines were sensitive to 5-FU, Cisplatin, and THZ1.\n...\nCell-line derived xenografts were generated by injecting 5 × 10^6^ cells of HNSCC16 P1 M1, HNSCC46 P0 M2, and HNSCC48 P0 M2 subcutaneously in the right flank of 6–8 weeks old female NSG mice.\n...\nAn in vivo therapy approach was carried out with HNSCC16 P1 M1.\n...\nIn an in vivo trial, drug response against Cisplatin was examined and HNSCC16 M1 P1 was chosen as experimental model, due to the comparably fast and reliable in vivo growth kinetics (Figure 4B).", "date": "2022-05-18", "last_updated": "2025-10-23", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.09, "evidence": 0.51}, "jev_score": 0.0459, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Download PDF - eScholarship.org", "url": "https://escholarship.org/content/qt146342j0/qt146342j0.pdf", "domain": "escholarship.org", "snippet": "palpable (generally 5–7 d post-inoculation) with low doses of cetuximab (0.4 mg weekly dosed as\n0.2 mg twice per week) with the rationale that \ntreating smaller tumors with lower doses of cetux- imab would facilitate the selection of resistant tumor cells.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-10", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.11, "evidence": 0.3267}, "jev_score": 0.0359, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Targeted therapy for head and neck cancer: signaling pathways and clinical studies", "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41392-022-01297-0", "domain": "nature.com", "snippet": "257 GW2016 is an effective inhibitor of the ErbB-2 and EGFR tyrosine kinase domains that is undergoing development.", "date": "2023-01-16", "last_updated": "2023-01-16", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.07, "evidence": 0.15}, "jev_score": 0.0105, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "titl