{"case_id": "q053-4", "row_id": "q053", "mode": "queries", "objective": "ADT-1004 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma animal models", "query": "ADT-1004 KPC orthotopic tumour volume change day 27", "anchors": ["ADT-1004"], "search_latency_ms": 3950.3, "target": "ADT-1004", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 386.9, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7813, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000328, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 5, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.9504, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "ADT-1004: a first-in-class, oral pan-RAS inhibitor with robust ... - PMC", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11905721/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "To determine the antitumor activity of ADT-1004, luciferase-labeled KPC (KPC-luc) cells with point mutations in KRAS^G12D^ and p53^R172H^ were surgically implanted into the pancreas of C57BL/6J mice.\nMice were imaged one week after implantation (day 0) to randomize mice between the control (vehicle) and ADT-1004 treatment groups.\nTreatment was started on day 0 by once daily oral gavage with either vehicle or ADT-1004 at dosages ranging from 10 to 50 mg/kg (5x/week) (Fig. 1E).\nMice were euthanized on day 27 to determine treatment effects on tumor growth by measuring bioluminescence and tumor weight (Fig.\n1F and G).\nMost mice in the ADT-1004 treatment groups displayed reduced bioluminescence compared with mice treated with vehicle.\nDoses of ADT-1004 from 20 to 50 mg/kg demonstrated comparable statistically significant reductions in tumor weights compared to vehicle-treated mice or mice treated with 10 mg/kg ADT-1004 (Fig. 1G).\nThere were no significant differences in body weight between the ADT-1004 treated and vehicle groups (Fig. 1H).\n...\nIn a side-by-side comparison, oral administration of ADT-1004 led to a dramatic decrease in tumor volume (Fig. 7I) and weight (Fig. 7J and K) compared with vehicle against tumors derived from MIA-AMG-R cells.", "date": "2025-03-13", "last_updated": "2026-02-17", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.99, "evidence": 0.96}, "jev_score": 0.9504, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "ADT-1004: a first-in-class, oral pan-RAS inhibitor with robust antitumor activity in preclinical models of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma - PubMed", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40082968/?fc=20250217093552&ff=20250315023922&v=2.18.0.post9+e462414", "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "ADT-1004 potently blocked tumor growth and RAS activation in mouse PDAC models without discernable toxicity with target engagement and reduced activated RAS and ERK phosphorylation.", "date": "2025-03-13", "last_updated": "2026-01-18", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.99, "evidence": 0.84}, "jev_score": 0.8316, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Abstract LB322: Antitumor activity of 1st-in-class pan-RAS inhibitor ADT-1004 in mouse models of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma", "url": "https://aacrjournals.org/cancerres/article/83/8_Supplement/LB322/725683/Abstract-LB322-Antitumor-activity-of-1st-in-class", "domain": "aacrjournals.org", "snippet": "Once daily oral administration of ADT-1004 significantly inhibited the growth of orthotopically implanted PDA tumors with a corresponding reduction in RAS/MAPK signaling.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-11-04", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.99, "evidence": 0.83}, "jev_score": 0.8217, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "ADT-1004 / Auburn University, ADT Pharma - LARVOL DELTA", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=6ff25253-89b9-4c9d-9da5-c4334486e2e5", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "Daily oral administration of ADT-1004 significantly inhibited RAS signaling and tumor growth in orthotopic and PDX mouse models of pancreatic cancer.\"", "date": "2025-12-31", "last_updated": "2026-02-17", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.8167}, "jev_score": 0.8004, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "ADT-007 / ADT Pharma, ChemomAb", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=6ac1f0ab-2853-4944-b164-e472fe11819b", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "Daily oral administration of ADT-1004 significantly inhibited RAS signaling and tumor growth in orthotopic and PDX mouse models of pancreatic cancer.\"", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-18", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.7833}, "jev_score": 0.7363, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "A potent and selective pan-RAS inhibitor, ADT-1004, targeting complex KRAS mutations for pancreatic cancer.", "url": "https://ascopubs.org/doi/10.1200/JCO.2024.42.16_suppl.e15085", "domain": "ascopubs.org", "snippet": "Tumor burden was assessed weekly by monitoring bioluminescence signals using the IVIS Xenogen imaging system.\n...\n**Conclusions:**ADT-1004 inhibited tumor growth of KRAS mutant PDA tumors by targeting activated RAS to disrupt downstream MAPK/AKT signaling.", "date": "2024-06-01", "last_updated": "2025-02-23", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.73}, "jev_score": 0.7154, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Table 1.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12730280/table/biomedicines-13-03013-t001/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|ADT-1004|Pan-RAS (G12D/G12V/G12C)|Ras pathway;KRAS/ERK pathway|Inhibit pancreatic cancer growth|PDX|[33]|", "date": "2025-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-12-27", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.69}, "jev_score": 0.6762, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Assessing the effects of androgen-deprivation therapy ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4530043/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Prostate volume also decreased significantly by 33% (9–58%) from a median of 57 ml to a median of 39 ml (p<0.001), with the peripheral zone in particular demonstrating a larger decrease of 44% compared with a 29% decrease in transition zone volume.", "date": "2015-03-29", "last_updated": "2025-09-12", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.11, "evidence": 0.1333}, "jev_score": 0.0147, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Proprietary Information of MD Anderson", "url": "https://cdn.clinicaltrials.gov/large-docs/27/NCT02684227/Prot_SAP_000.pdf", "domain": "cdn.clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "Proprietary Information of MD Anderson\n...\nProprietary Information of MD Anderson", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-13", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.28, "evidence": 0.0233}, "jev_score": 0.0065, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Physics and Imaging in Radiation Oncology - DiVA portal", "url": "https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1534228/FULLTEXT01.pdf", "domain": "diva-portal.org", "snippet": "For 44 patients, the relative tumour volume was reduced, and 43 patients had reduced reference volume, see\nTable 1. \n...\nTumour \nvolume \n(cm3) \n−24% ± 16% \n92%  \n5.8  \n4.3 ", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-27", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.03, "evidence": 0.08}, "jev_score": 0.0024, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 4337.2, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:40+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q054-2", "row_id": "q054", "mode": "queries", "objective": "DWP216 in vivo animal models and results: cell-line xenograft (CDX), patient-derived xenograft (PDX), syngeneic, orthotopic, or genetically engineered models", "query": "DWP216 NCI-H1373 monotherapy tumour volume", "anchors": ["DWP216"], "search_latency_ms": 4105.1, "target": "DWP216", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 518.8, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 25290, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.001062, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 1, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.6855, "results": [{"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "[단독] 대웅제약의 '차세대 항암 신약' 비밀병기 3종은? - 헬스케어N", "url": "https://m.healthcaren.com/news/news_article_yong.jsp?mn_idx=550285", "domain": "m.healthcaren.com", "snippet": "살아있는 유기체 대상 생체 내(in vivo) 실험에서 ‘DWP216’은 기존에 개발 중인 실험용 TEAD1 억제제 또는 범 TEAD 단백질 억제제보다 뛰어난 종양 억제 효과를 나타냈으며, EGFR 및 KRAS 억제제와 병용했을 때에는 시너지 효과까지 보였다.\n...\n생체 내(in vivo) 실험에서도 유의미한 효능이 확인됐다.\n단독 투여만으로도 30mg/kg 용량에서 종양 억제 효과가 나타났으며, PARP 억제제와 병용 투여 시에는 50% 이상의 종양 위축을 유도하는 시너지 효과가 관찰됐다.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-31", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7067}, "jev_score": 0.6855, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "NCI-H1373 AdagR", "url": "https://ribometrix.com/app/uploads/2024/09/ESMO2024Poster_Final.pdf", "domain": "ribometrix.com", "snippet": "Importantly, RBX-6610 monotherapy in vivo causes significant tumor growth inhibition, and the combination therapy with sotorasib results in significant tumor regression in a naïve NSCLC xenograft model.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-05-30", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.16, "evidence": 0.5133}, "jev_score": 0.0821, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "\"� �����/f�˪���~��EwI��LIq7����5�����]�dO`��㪗F�to��^(@����H<��v{�ZF�m� `G�:I_0w�������~8 ���ԛ������R6�Lx��a