{"case_id": "q058-2", "row_id": "q058", "mode": "queries", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo efficacy in combination with another agent in Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma, including the combination partner", "query": "HEC234055 combination partner PDAC xenograft", "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "search_latency_ms": 2975.7, "target": "HEC234055", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 349.0, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8475, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000356, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 2, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.759, "results": [{"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Three innovative drugs showcased at the 2026 AACR Annual ...", "url": "https://www.moomoo.com/news/post/68755735/dongyang-sunshine-pharmaceutical-06887-three-innovative-drugs-showcased-at-the", "domain": "moomoo.com", "snippet": "Synergistic enhancement in combination therapy: Co-administration with PD-1 antibodies further significantly enhanced anti-tumor efficacy, showing broad prospects for combination therapy.\n...\nHEC234055 - An oral high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor targeting undruggable targets.\n...\nThe investigational product HEC234055 is an orally administered, high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor independently developed by the group, designed for broad-spectrum coverage of various KRAS mutations and wild-type amplifications.\n...\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In various xenograft tumor models with KRAS mutations (covering pancreatic cancer, lung cancer, and colorectal cancer), oral administration produced dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induced tumor regression.\n...\nBroad combination therapy potential: Co-administration with chemotherapy drugs (5-FU), anti-VEGF antibodies, VEGFR inhibitors, and KRAS G12C inhibitors all exhibited significant synergistic effects.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-04-24", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.99, "evidence": 0.7667}, "jev_score": 0.759, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "C262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4", "url": "https://www.hecpharm.com/uploads/20260424/09387cfb2e90905d791878048b2ac9fa.pdf", "domain": "hecpharm.com", "snippet": "聯合治療協同增效：與PD -1 抗體聯合給藥可進一步顯著增強抗腫瘤療\n效，展現出廣闊的聯合用藥前景。\n...\n二、HEC234055 — 攻克「不可成藥」靶點的口服高活性Pan-RAS分子膠抑制劑（摘\n...\n亞型仍存在巨大未滿足的臨床需求。在研產品HEC234055 為本集團自主研發\n的口服高活性Pan-RAS 分子膠抑制劑，旨在廣譜覆蓋KRAS 多種突變及野生型\n...\n廣譜覆蓋與高活性：可同時作用於KRAS 的活性（三磷酸鳥苷（「GTP 」）結\n合）與非活性（GDP 結合）狀態，並覆蓋G12D 、G12C 、G12V 、G13D 、\n...\n顯著的體內療效：在多種KRAS 突變的異種移植瘤模型中（涵蓋胰腺癌、\n肺癌及結直腸癌），口服給藥可產生劑量依賴性的腫瘤生長抑制乃至誘導\n腫瘤消退。\n...\n廣泛的聯合用藥潛力：與化療藥物(5 -FU) 、抗VEGF 抗體、VEGFR 抑制劑\n及KRAS G12C抑制劑聯合給藥，均表現出顯著的協同增效作用。", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-13", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7333}, "jev_score": 0.7186, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Molecular alterations and targeted therapy in pancreatic ...", "url": "https://d-nb.info/122186016X/34", "domain": "d-nb.info", "snippet": "When applied together with AZD6244, BKM120, a PI3K inhibitor, leads to robust apoptosis in PDAC-derived organotypic models or murine models, resulting in a longer median survival (131.5 vs 71 days) [59] and indi- cating that the combined inhibition of MEK and PI3K may have clinical value.\n...\nUlixertinib, an ERK inhibitor, exerts an inhibitory\neffect on solid tumour xenograft models [60] and ap- pears to prevent tumour growth to a greater extent when combined with MEK inhibitors [61].\n...\nThe application of abemaciclib and YAP1 or HuR inhibitors also exerts a synergistic inhibitory effect on PDAC cell lines [114].", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-02-21", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.21, "evidence": 0.4}, "jev_score": 0.084, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Combinatorial Screening of Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma Reveals Sensitivity to Drug Combinations Including Bromodomain Inhibitor plus Neddylation Inhibitor", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5457712/", "domain": "ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Combination of the bromodomain inhibitor JQ1 and the neddylation inhibitor MLN4294 altered production of reactive oxygen species in PDAC cells, ultimately leading to defects in the DNA damage response.\nDual bromodomain/neddylation blockade inhibited *in vivo* growth of PDAC cell line xenografts.\nOverall, this work revealed novel combinatorial regimens, including JQ1 plus MLN4294, which show promise for the treatment of *RAS*-driven PDAC.\n...\nAgents that contribute most often to effective combinations include SN-38, the active metabolite of irinotecan (topoisomerase I inhibitor), PF-431396 (FAK, PYK2 inhibitor), MLN4924 (neddylation activating enzyme inhibitor), JQ1 (BET family inhibitor), Foretinib (MET, VEGFR2 inhibitor), and GSK1120212 (MEK inhibitor).\nOf note, the bromodomain inhibitor JQ1 and neddylation inhibitor MLN4924 combine superadditively to halt growth and inhibit viability and colony formation in a broad range of PDAC cell lines, and control human PDAC grown as mouse xenografts.\nEffectiveness of this combination occurs in part through the induction of reactive oxygen species (ROS) that promote increased DNA damage, leading to apoptosis.\n...\nWhen the size of the xenograft (n = 3-5 per group) reached approximately 80-120 mm\n3, the mice were randomized and intraperitoneally treated with JQ1 (50 mg/kg, daily) and/or MLN4924 (25 mg/kg, every other day) for 14 days and showed significant synergistic effect.\n...\nImportantly, combination of JQ1 and MLN4924 suppressed growth of MiaPaCa-2 mouse xenografts under conditions where the single agents were ineffectual (Fig. 6F, left).\nThis reinforces the potential for substantial improvement over single-agent responses with this combination regimen.\n...\nPairwise combination of these seven agents reduced clonogenic colony formation and were often super-additive.", "date": "2017-06-11", "last_updated": "2024-10-11", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.18, "evidence": 0.31}, "jev_score": 0.0558, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Treatment of pancreatic cancer with a combination ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0923753419478381", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-19", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.28, "evidence": 0.0567}, "jev_score": 0.0159, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Combinatorial screening of pancreatic adenocarcinoma reveals ...", "url": "https://scispace.com/pdf/combinatorial-screening-of-pancreatic-adenocarcinoma-reveals-4agzt1hdnh.pdf", "domain": "scispace.com", "snippet": "Dual bromodomain/neddylation blockade inhibited in vivo growth of PDAC cell line xenografts.\n...\nOf note, the bro- modomain inhibitor JQ1 and neddylation inhibitor MLN4924 combine superadditively to halt growth and inhibit viability and colony formation in a broad range of PDAC cell lines, and control human PDAC grown as mouse xenografts.\n...\nImportantly, combination of JQ1 and MLN4924 suppressed growth of Mia-\n...\nWe show for the first time that the combination of the JQ1 bromodomain inhibitor and MLN4924 neddylation inhibitor is highly effective for PDAC in both in vitro and in vivo studies.\n...\nHence, it is noteworthy that we identified a series of effective combination partners both for JQ1 and for MLN4924.\nJQ1 combined well with gemcitabine, BI-2536, MLN-8237, peme- trexed, and PF-431396.\nMLN4924 combination partners includ- ed PF-431396, SN-38, MLN-8237, oligomycin, and pemetrexed.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-11", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.06, "evidence": 0.1633}, "jev_score": 0.0098, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Patient-Derived Xenograft Models of Pancreatic Cancer - PMC", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7281668/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "The data showed that gemcitabine or AZD7762 alone or in combination suppressed tumor growth in two subcutaneous pancreatic PDX models.", "date": "2020-05-22", "last_updated": "2026-08-27", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.05, "evidence": 0.17}, "jev_score": 0.0085, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "A potential therapeutic target for pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022356525397867", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-03", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.19, "evidence": 0.0333}, "jev_score": 0.0063, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Experimental drugs and drug combinations in pancreatic cancer", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0923753420311522", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-09", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.13, "evidence": 0.03}, "jev_score": 0.0039, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Table 2.", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8000738/table/jcm-10-01151-t002/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Bioconjugation strategy has been categorized into three methods: lysine-based random, site-specific via sortase-mediated reaction, and direct iodination.", "date": "2021-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-10-29", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.04, "evidence": 0.02}, "jev_score": 0.0008, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 3324.7, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:43+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q059-2", "row_id": "q059", "mode": "queries", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo animal models and results: cell-line xenograft (CDX), patient-derived xenograft (PDX), syngeneic, orthotopic, genetically engineered models", "query": "HEC234055 PDX model", "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "search_latency_ms": 1230.2, "target": "HEC234055", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 377.9, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7835, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000329, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 2, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.7469, "results": [{"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] C262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4", "url": "https://stockn.xueqiu.com/06887/20260423391014.pdf", "domain": "stockn.xueqiu.com", "snippet": "二、HEC234055 — 攻克「不可成藥」靶點的口服高活性Pan-RAS分子膠抑制劑（摘\n要號#2634）\nRAS基因突變驅動約四分一的人類癌症，其中KRAS G12D、G12V等常見突變\n亞型仍存在巨大未滿足的臨床需求。在研產品HEC234055 為本集團自主研發\n的口服高活性Pan-RAS 分子膠抑制劑，旨在廣譜覆蓋KRAS 多種突變及野生型\n擴增。此次公佈的臨床前數據亮點如下：\n...\n廣譜覆蓋與高活性：可同時作用於KRAS 的活性（三磷酸鳥苷（「GTP 」）結\n合）與非活性（GDP 結合）狀態，並覆蓋G12D 、G12C 、G12V 、G13D 、\nQ61H等多種突變類型及野生型擴增。\n...\n亞納摩爾級細胞活性：在多種KRAS 突變驅動的癌細胞系中，其抗增殖活\n性達到亞納摩爾級別，半抑制濃度（「IC50」）低至0.49 納摩爾（「n M」），顯\n示出優於當前對標分子的強效抑制能力。\n...\n顯著的體內療效：在多種KRAS 突變的異種移植瘤模型中（涵蓋胰腺癌、\n肺癌及結直腸癌），口服給藥可產生劑量依賴性的腫瘤生長抑制乃至誘導\n腫瘤消退。", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-12", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.77}, "jev_score": 0.7469, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Sunshine Lake Pharma Co., Ltd. Showcases Three Innovative ...", "url": "https://www.marketscreener.com/news/sunshine-lake-pharma-co-ltd-showcases-three-innovative-oncology-drug-candidates-at-2026-aacr-annu-ce7f58d8dd8ffe27", "domain": "marketscreener.com", "snippet": "HEC234055 is an orally available high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor independently developed by the Group, designed to target a broad spectrum of multiple KRAS mutations as well as wild-type amplifications.\nThe preclinical data highlights announced this time are as follows: Broad-spectrum coverage and high activity: It can act on both active (guanosine triphosphate (GTP)-bound) and inactive (GDP-bound) states of KRAS, and covers various mutation types such as G12D, G12C, G12V, G13D, Q61H, and wild-type amplification.\n...\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In multiple KRAS-mutated xenograft tumor models (including pancreatic, lung and colorectal cancers), oral administration can produce dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induce tumor regression.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-05-14", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.72}, "jev_score": 0.7056, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Establishment of Patient-derived Xenografts (PDX) Models ...", "url": "https://www.mdanderson.org/patients-family/diagnosis-treatment/clinical-trials/clinical-trials-index/clinical-trials-detail.IDPA13-0592.html", "domain": "mdanderson.org", "snippet": "Help us celebrate and fuel the groundbreaking innovations and transformative advancements that define MD Anderson.", "date": "2015-11-24", "last_updated": "2026-01-24", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.13, "evidence": 0.11}, "jev_score": 0.0143, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "PDX models | CancerTools.org", "url": "https://cancertools.org/tools-category/pdx-models/", "domain": "cancertools.org", "snippet": "CancerTools provides large, diverse collections of Patient–Derived Xenograft (PDX) models for breast cancer and lung cancer that are:\n- Highly valuable in recapitulating patient tumour characteristics, including intratumour heterogeneity, genomic features, metastatic patterns, and drug responses\n- Highly translatable preclinical models that can be used to more accurately test therapy efficacy and predict patient drug responses than traditional models", "date": "2024-11-15", "las