{"case_id": "q058-3", "row_id": "q058", "mode": "queries", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo efficacy in combination with another agent in Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma, including the combination partner", "query": "HEC234055 AACR 2026 combination efficacy", "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "search_latency_ms": 2140.3, "target": "HEC234055", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 439.1, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8872, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000373, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 3, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.7774, "results": [{"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Three innovative drugs showcased at the 2026 AACR Annual ...", "url": "https://www.moomoo.com/news/post/68755735/dongyang-sunshine-pharmaceutical-06887-three-innovative-drugs-showcased-at-the", "domain": "moomoo.com", "snippet": "Dongyangguang Pharmaceutical (06887) announced that at the 2026 Annual Meeting of the American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) held in San Diego, California, USA, from April 17 to 22, 2026, the group presented the latest preclinical research findings on three pipeline candidates in the field of oncology treatment through three poster presentations.\n...\nHEC234055 - An oral high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor targeting undruggable targets.\n...\nThe investigational product HEC234055 is an orally administered, high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor independently developed by the group, designed for broad-spectrum coverage of various KRAS mutations and wild-type amplifications.\n...\nSub-nanomolar cellular activity: In various cancer cell lines driven by KRAS mutations, its anti-proliferative activity reaches sub-nanomolar levels, with a half-maximal inhibitory concentration (IC50) as low as 0.49 nanomoles (nM), demonstrating stronger inhibitory capabilities than current benchmark molecules.\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In various xenograft tumor models with KRAS mutations (covering pancreatic cancer, lung cancer, and colorectal cancer), oral administration produced dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induced tumor regression.\n...\nBroad combination therapy potential: Co-administration with chemotherapy drugs (5-FU), anti-VEGF antibodies, VEGFR inhibitors, and KRAS G12C inhibitors all exhibited significant synergistic effects.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-04-24", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7933}, "jev_score": 0.7774, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "C262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4", "url": "https://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0423/2026042301900_c.pdf", "domain": "hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "本集團欣然宣佈，於2026 年4 月17 日至22 日在美國加利福尼亞州聖地亞哥舉行的\n2026年美國癌症研究協會(AACR)年會上，本集團以三份壁報形式集中展示了腫瘤\n...\n二、HEC234055 — 攻克「不可成藥」靶點的口服高活性Pan-RAS分子膠抑制劑（摘\n要號#2634）\n...\n亞型仍存在巨大未滿足的臨床需求。在研產品HEC234055 為本集團自主研發\n的口服高活性Pan-RAS 分子膠抑制劑，旨在廣譜覆蓋KRAS 多種突變及野生型\n...\n廣譜覆蓋與高活性：可同時作用於KRAS 的活性（三磷酸鳥苷（「GTP 」）結\n合）與非活性（GDP 結合）狀態，並覆蓋G12D 、G12C 、G12V 、G13D 、\n...\n亞納摩爾級細胞活性：在多種KRAS 突變驅動的癌細胞系中，其抗增殖活\n性達到亞納摩爾級別，半抑制濃度（「IC50」）低至0.49 納摩爾（「n M」），顯\n示出優於當前對標分子的強效抑制能力。\n...\n顯著的體內療效：在多種KRAS 突變的異種移植瘤模型中（涵蓋胰腺癌、\n肺癌及結直腸癌），口服給藥可產生劑量依賴性的腫瘤生長抑制乃至誘導\n腫瘤消退。\n...\n廣泛的聯合用藥潛力：與化療藥物(5 -FU) 、抗VEGF 抗體、VEGFR 抑制劑\n及KRAS G12C抑制劑聯合給藥，均表現出顯著的協同增效作用。", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-01", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.78}, "jev_score": 0.7644, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Sunshine Lake Pharma Co., Ltd. Showcases Three Innovative ...", "url": "https://www.marketscreener.com/news/sunshine-lake-pharma-co-ltd-showcases-three-innovative-oncology-drug-candidates-at-2026-aacr-annu-ce7f58d8dd8ffe27", "domain": "marketscreener.com", "snippet": "At the 2026 Annual Meeting of the American Association for Cancer Research (AACR), held from 17 to 22 April 2026 in San Diego, California, USA, the Group presented the latest preclinical research results of three oncology pipeline candidates through three poster presentations.\n...\nHEC234055 is an orally available high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor independently developed by the Group, designed to target a broad spectrum of multiple KRAS mutations as well as wild-type amplifications.\nThe preclinical data highlights announced this time are as follows: Broad-spectrum coverage and high activity: It can act on both active (guanosine triphosphate (GTP)-bound) and inactive (GDP-bound) states of KRAS, and covers various mutation types such as G12D, G12C, G12V, G13D, Q61H, and wild-type amplification.\nSub-nanomolar cell activity: In a variety of KRAS mutation-driven cancer cell lines, its anti-proliferative activity reaches the sub-nanomolar level, with half-maximal inhibitory concentration (IC50) as low as 0.49 nanomolar (nM), showing potent inhibitory capabilities superior to current benchmark molecules.\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In multiple KRAS-mutated xenograft tumor models (including pancreatic, lung and colorectal cancers), oral administration can produce dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induce tumor regression.\n...\nBroad potential for combination therapy: Co-administration with chemotherapy drugs (5-FU), anti-VEGF antibodies, VEGFR inhibitors, and KRASG12C inhibitors all exhibit significant synergistic effects.\n...\nThe preclinical research data disclosed in this announcement are derived from laboratory and animal model studies, and the relevant drug candidates have not yet undergone clinical trials in humans.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-05-14", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7133}, "jev_score": 0.699, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "東陽光薬（06887.HK）の3種類の創薬が2026年AACR年次総会で発表", "url": "https://www.moomoo.com/ja/news/post/68755580", "domain": "moomoo.com", "snippet": "グローベンター（格隆汇）4月23日付｜東陽光薬（06887.\nHK）は、2026年4月17日から22日まで米国カリフォルニア州サンディエゴで開催された2026年米国癌学会（AACR）年会上において、グループが3つのポスター発表形式で腫瘍\n治療領域における3つの研究開発パイプライン（CDH17/4-1BB二重特異性抗体「HEC-922」、経口高活性Pan-RAS分子グリュー阻害剤「HEC234055」、経口低分子PD-L1阻害剤「HEC201625」）の最新前臨床研究成果を集中的に発表したことを発表しました。", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-04-24", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.91, "evidence": 0.4667}, "jev_score": 0.4247, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR Annual Meeting 2026 – Post-event summary", "url": "https://www.insights.bio/bioinsights/journal/article/3821/aacr-annual-meeting-2026-postevent-summary-clinical-data-readouts-and-emerging-themes", "domain": "insights.bio", "snippet": "Within the ovarian cancer subgroup, 80% of patients demonstrated tumor shrinkage, with an ORR of 37.5% overall, increasing to 60% in the CCNE1-amplified subgroup.\n...\nAfter a median follow-up of 11.7 months, the confirmed ORR was 47.1%, DCR was 94.1%, and mPFS reached 14 months, representing a clinically meaningful outcome in a population for whom no targeted therapeutic options currently exist.", "date": "2026-05-14", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.17, "evidence": 0.33}, "jev_score": 0.0561, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR DRUG DISCOVERY AND DEVELOPMENT ( ...", "url": "https://www.aacr.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/D32026_AbstractTitlesOnly.pdf", "domain": "aacr.org", "snippet": "B068 A sphingolipid-derived paclitaxel nanovesicle enhances efficacy of combination therapies in triple-negative breast cancer and pancreatic cancer.", "date": "2026-06-22", "last_updated": "2026-07-13", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.13, "evidence": 0.2367}, "jev_score": 0.0308, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Advances in antibody-drug conjugates in cancer - PMC - NIH", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13332605/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Trispecific constructs targeting PD-L1, B7-H3, and VEGF were designed to simultaneously deliver cytotoxic payloads while blocking immune checkpoints and inhibiting angiogenesis [3].\nThese agents demonstrated enhanced tumor binding, improved internalization, and superior antitumor efficacy compared to monospecific counterparts, while maintaining a favorable safety profile by sparing non-target immune cells.\nSuch designs effectively embed combination therapy within a single molecular entity, maximizing therapeutic synergy.", "date": "2026-07-04", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.05, "evidence": 0.2733}, "jev_score": 0.0137, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026: Emerging Antibody-Drug Conjugates for the ...", "url": "https://www.adcreview.com/conference-coverage/aacr/aacr-2026-emerging-antibody-drug-conjugates-for-the-treatment-of-solid-tumors-part-1/", "domain": "adcreview.com", "snippet": "An active phase 1/2 clinical trial (NCT07354711 and CTR20254555) is underway to evaluate the safety, efficacy, and pharmacokinetics of 3H-10000 in patients with unresectable or metastatic advanced solid tumors.[24]", "date": "2026-05-05", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.04, "evidence": 0.06}, "jev_score": 0.0024, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026", "url": "https://medical.emdserono.com/en_US/medinfo/therapeutic-areas/oncology/congress-presentations/aacr-2026.html", "domain": "medical.emdserono.com", "snippet": "2026 American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting – April 17-22, 2026 / San Diego, CA", "date": "2026-05-11", "last_updated": "2026-09-21", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.16, "evidence": 0.01}, "jev_score": 0.0016, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Annual Meeting 2026 Session Recaps Archives", "url": "https://www.aacrmeetingnews.org/category/2026/recap-2026/", "domain": "aacrmeetingnews.org", "snippet": "Alberto Giovanni Leone, MD, shared results from cohort two of the single-arm, nonrandomized phase II INFINITY clinical trial assessing a combination treatment of two immune checkpoint inhibitors, tremelimumab and durvalumab.", "date": "2026-05-07", "last_updated": "2026-09-23", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.03, "evidence": 0.0167}, "jev_score": 0.0005, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 2579.4, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:43+00:00"}
