effects on serum cytokines, when EOM613 was added to the standard-of-care therapy.\n...\n|AVR-118|Crohn Disease More|Preclinical|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-30", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.8467}, "jev_score": 0.8128, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "FDA Clears IND for EOM613 Trial in Cancer Cachexia Patients", "url": "https://www.clinicaltrialvanguard.com/news/fda-clears-ind-for-eom613-trial-in-cancer-cachexia-patients/", "domain": "clinicaltrialvanguard.com", "snippet": "Cancer cachexia has killed patients before their underlying malignancy could, yet across decades of failed trials no drug has earned FDA approval for the condition — and EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings is now cleared to run only a 20-patient open-label Phase 2a study to test whether that changes.\n...\nThe company’s simultaneous planning for a Crohn’s diseaseCrohn’s disease trial in Q4 2026 signals an intent to validate EOM613’s cytokine-modulation mechanism across indications rather than commit resources to a single confirmatory cachexia program.", "date": "2026-05-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-24", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.8267}, "jev_score": 0.7854, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "reticulose (EOM613) / EOM Pharma", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=8bd00719-c964-4a7b-85e5-3bcf4092483b", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "/ EOM Pharma\n...\n- \"EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings, Inc...provides an update on its clinical program for its lead drug candidate EOM613....This clinical finding is of particular interest since the pathophysiology of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) is known to be largely driven by the release of inflammatory cytokines in the gastrointestinal tract, in particular TNF-alpha, interleukin 12 (IL-12), interleukin-23 (IL-23) and sIL-2R.\nIn light of these clinical trial results, the company is currently preparing to initiate an EOM613 clinical program in Crohn's disease.\"", "date": "2023-11-07", "last_updated": "2025-10-28", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7967}, "jev_score": 0.7728, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Methods of treating inflammatory bowel diseases", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/WO2025049974A1/en", "domain": "patents.google.com", "snippet": "- EOM613 was not previously investigated for use in treating IBD, such as Crohn’s disease or ulcerative colitis.\n...\nDisclosed herein are methods of treating inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) in a subject, including administering a therapeutically effective amount of EOM613 to the subject.\nIn some aspects, the IBD is Crohn’s disease.\nIn some aspects, treatment with EOM613 reduces one or more symptoms of IBD, such as rectal bleeding, abdominal bloating, diarrhea, multiple daily bowel movements, fatigue, weight loss, and abdominal pain or cramps.\n...\nAn appropriate dose can be determined, for example, in clinical trials.", "date": "2024-08-30", "last_updated": "2025-07-20", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.63}, "jev_score": 0.6111, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "max_keep"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Clinical Trials in the European Union - EMA", "url": "https://euclinicaltrials.eu/", "domain": "euclinicaltrials.eu", "snippet": "This website provides information on individual clinical trials in the European Union and European Economic Area since its launch on 31 January 2022.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-10", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.07, "evidence": 0.01}, "jev_score": 0.0007, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Find Studies | ClinicalTrials.gov", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/find-studies", "domain": "clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "A patient registry is a type of observational study.\n**Note:** The ClinicalTrials.gov results database became available in September 2008.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-18", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.04, "evidence": 0.0067}, "jev_score": 0.0003, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "ICTRP Search Portal - World Health Organization (WHO)", "url": "https://www.who.int/tools/clinical-trials-registry-platform/the-ictrp-search-portal", "domain": "who.int", "snippet": "The ICTRP Search Portal aims to provide a single point of access to information about ongoing and completed clinical trials.\nIt provides a searchable database containing the trial registration data sets made available by data providers around the world meeting criteria for content and quality control.\nTrial registration data sets are available on the ICTRP Search Portal in English only.\n...\nIf available, these may be searched by going directly to the web sites\nof the individual registries.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.04, "evidence": 0.0033}, "jev_score": 0.0001, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}], "total_ms": 4438.5, "ts": "2026-10-04T12:16:44+00:00"}
